  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Triffid">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonSapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Triffid</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sociocultural Characteristics Human experimentation (theorised) Physical Characteristics Average height 7-10 feet Venomous stinger Real World Information First appearance The Day of the Triffids Created by John Wyndham The Triffids are bio-engineered organisms created by John Wyndham for his 1951 novel The Day of the Triffids and later expanded into the Cthulhu Mythos by Chaosium for the Call of Cthulhu role-playing game. Description The Triffids are hostile plants with a straight stem from which its mouth appears and four stick-like protrusions which they use as legs. The Triffids were theorised to have been the result of a scientific program - possibly Soviet - but their seeds have spread throughout the world. They can grow in any environment, but take four to five years to mature.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>Venomous stinger</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Day of the Triffids</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>John Wyndham</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Storm_Cellar">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Storm Cellar</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Short story they thrive in darkness: mythos and madness was published in 2018 . It tells the tale of a tornado that forced a family into a storm cellar . They were attacked by a ghoul and managed to escape with their lives .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Madness</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>They Thrive in Darkness: Mythos</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tony_Morgan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tony Morgan</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Bounty Hunter</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The bounty hunter is a fictional character created by fantasy flight games . Originally created as an investigator for their second edition release of arkham horror . Has since made appearances in several of their other games including eldritch horror and arkham horror: the card game .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Kingsport Horror Deluxe Expansion</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Black_Wings">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Black Wings</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>S. T. Joshi English PS Publishing is a series of six anthologies of original H. P. Lovecraft -influenced fiction, edited by Lovecraft scholar S. T. Joshi and published by PS Publishing from 2010 to 2017. They were reprinted (using the alternate titles of Cthulhu 1-6) by Titan Books. Best of : Tales of Lovecraftian Horror , was published by Drugstore Indian Press in 2019. Series : New Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (PS Publishing, 2010) II: New Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (PS Publishing, 2012) III: New Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (PS Publishing, 2014) IV: Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (PS Publishing, 2015) V: New Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (PS Publishing, 2016) VI: New Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (PS Publishing, 2017) Best of : Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (Drugstore Indian Press, 2019) Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shuggon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shuggon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Altuan"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Altuas"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Earth Also known as Altuan (unconfirmed) Altuas (unconfirmed) Continent Created by Lin Carter is an ancient continent created by the late American author Lin Carter for his Cthulhu Mythos works. Overview In the Cthulhu Mythos works of Lin Carter related to Hyperborea , is the ancient continent of the Mesozoic serpent people destroyed in a cataclysm c.65 million B.C.E. which caused the surviving serpent people to migrate to Elder Valusia and aided in the extinction of the dinosaurs. is named in the Necronomicon but goes unnamed in most other texts. It may also be the same as Altuas or Altuan .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Continent</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Earth"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Wendigo_%28story%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Wendigo (story)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the wendigo" is a novella by algernon blackwood . It was first published in the lost valley and other stories in 1910 . The story is set in the wilderness of western ontario, north of the real-life town of rat portage .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Algernon_Blackwood"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Stories</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The Lost Valley</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1910</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gretchens_Wood:_and_Other_Lovecraftian_Tales_of_Terror_in_Columbiana_County,_Ohio">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gretchen's Wood: and Other Lovecraftian Tales of Terror in Columbiana County, Ohio</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ran Cartwright United States English Genre(s) Horror PublishAmerica Release Date June 2005 198 is a collection of short stories by American Ran Cartwright . Overview Collecting eleven stories with a Lovecraftian theme, the stories contained within Gretchen's Wood are all set in the real-world county of Columbiana, Ohio. It was first published in June 2005 by PublishAmerica, and runs to a total of 198 . Contents Acknowledgments Foreword: Something in the Dark " The Black Horror of Dungannon " " Tommy's Goat " " The Horror of Organ Grinder Road " " The House in the Woods " " The Horror from the Sky " " Dreaming in Darkness " " The Calling of the Hounds " " Summoning Tsathoggua " " Gretchen's Wood " " The Highlandtown Lake Horror " " Alder's Rest " Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ran_Cartwright"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>198</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2005</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hyperion_Hotel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hyperion Hotel</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAccessibilityL>Road</ex:hasAccessibilityL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The hyperion is a "shabby old residence hotel" located in san francisco's mission district . Along with short-term room rentals, the hyperion also plays home to several long-term residents . Those who frequent its ageing corridors are mostly people considered by the bulk of society as the outcasts and down-and-outs . Residents chester chase , a 75-year-old man who has decided to oppose the forces of the cthulhu my</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Hotel</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>See text</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#California"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#San_Francisco"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>USA</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Pool"/>
  </rdf:Description>
