    <rdfs:label>Mythos Collector Summer 2002</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Robert H. Knox English Mythos Collector Dark Tree Press Release Date June 2002 56 Preceded by Winter 2002 Followed by Fall 2002 was the third edition of the sporadically-released fanzine Mythos Collector . Edited by Brian Lingard, it featured cover art by Robert H. Knox, and was published by Dark Tree Press in June 2002 . Contents Editorial: First Words by Brian Lingard Interview with W. Paul Ganley by Brian Lingard "Madness" by J. R. Cain "Dreaming R'lyeh Posse" by Lee Clark Zumpe "The Gemstone from Out of Space" by P. J. Roberts Interview with S. T. Joshi by Christopher O'Brien Auction Watch Reviews by Brian Lingard Mythos Gallery (artwork by Robert H. Knox) Contributor Bios References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>56</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mythos_Collector"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2002</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Alfred_Jermyn">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Alfred Jermyn</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sir alfed was the son of nevil jermyn and the father of arthur jermyn . He became a baronet before his fourth birthday, but his tastes never matched his title . At the age of twenty he joined a band of music hall performers . At thirty-six he deserted his wife and son to travel with an american circus .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Facts Concerning the Late Arthur Jermyn</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>His Family</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Armandra">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Armandra</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Created by Brian Lumley is the daughter of the Great Old One Ithaqua and a powerful sorceress and priestess who wages war against her parent in the Titus Crow book series by Brian Lumley .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Marit_Lage">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Marit Lage</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a god from the fictional universe of the magic: the gathering collectible card game . It has been associated with black mana and said to have been both a mage and a sorceress . Not much is known about the entity, including its origins or history, what it is, and its current status .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shang">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shang</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ulthar Blacksmith Human First appearance HPL : " The Cats of Ulthar " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a resident of the town of Ulthar where he works as a blacksmith. He was one of the town burgesses who helped pass the law that made it illegal to kill cats . ( HPL : " The Cats of Ulthar ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Cats_of_Ulthar"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Little_Glass_Bottle">
