  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Within_Stranger_Aeons">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Within Stranger Aeons</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lovecraft's Mythos in the 21st Century Various English J. Ellington Ashton Press Release Date 21 May 2016 228 : Lovecraft's Mythos in the 21st Century is anthology of Lovecraftian fiction and poetry published by J. Ellington Ashton Press in May 2016. edited by Michael Fisher , both paperback and digital versions were released. Overview Contents Foreword by Michael Fisher " Nyarlathotep " by H. P. Lovecraft "New Year's Day" by Andrew Bell "That Thing About Feinberg" by Mord McGhee "Gänna" by Juan J. Gutiérrez "Oldbook" by Glynn Owen Barrass "From the Murky Depths" by Michael Fisher "Gorloth: Live and on Fire!" by Kevin Candela "The Thing in the Tub" by Roy C. Booth and William Henry Tucker "Vexteria" by Ashley Dioses "Nameless One" by Andrew J. Lucas "Truth Behind the Lies" by Essel Pratt "The Potholes Horror" by G. Zimmerman " A Visage of Great Truths " by Brian Barr "Always Read the Small Print" by Mark Woods "Algol" by Juan J. Gutiérrez "They Have Always Been Here" by Justin Hunter "A Natural Mother" by Amanda M. Lyons "Fair Warning" by Dona Fox "Adjudication" by Charie D. La Marr</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>228</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>21 May 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chorazin_%28location%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Chorazin (location)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Chorazin was a community in biblical palestine, located in what is now modern israel . It appears in the new testament, was associated in tradition with the antichrist . It was mentioned in the horror fiction of m. r. james .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Diary_of_Alonzo_Typer"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Settlement</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Modern-day Israel</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Count_Magnus"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#More_Annotated_Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>More Annotated Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>United States English Genre(s) Non-Fiction Dell Release Date August 1999 312 is a non-fiction book by Howard Phillips Lovecraft scholars S. T. Joshi and Peter Cannon . Overview The volume contains several stories along with notes by Joshi and Cannon offering insights into Lovecraft's writings. It runs to a total of 312 . Contents Introduction, by Peter Cannon " The Picture in the House " " Herbert West—Reanimator " " The Hound " " The Shunned House " " The Horror at Red Hook " " Cool Air " " The Call of Cthulhu " " Pickman’s Model " " The Thing on the Doorstep " " The Haunter of the Dark " Publication History was first published in August 1999 by Dell.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Non-Fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>312</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 1999</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecraftian_Limerick">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lovecraftian Limerick</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Andrew J. Wilson English Genre(s) Humour Wildside Press Weirdbook Annual 2 date February 2019 " " is, as it’s name implies, a short poem by Scottish Andrew J. Wilson . Overview The poem namechecks a number of Lovecraftian staples, including Shoggoths , Yog-Sothoth and the Great Race of Yith . History "" was published in the anthology Weirdbook Annual 2 by Wildside Press in 2019.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Andrew_J._Wilson"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Humour</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Weirdbook Annual 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nezaral">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nezaral</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chthon"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Lord Nezaral</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as Lord Chthon First appearance Blade: The Vampire-Hunter Vol 1 #8 Created by Ian Edginton is a fictional character from Marvel Comics created in 1995 by Ian Edginton. It first appeared in issue #8 of the 1st volume of Blade: The Vampire-Hunter comic book series. Background is a demon who is an agent of the Elder God Chthon . It is a giant demon able to swallow a human whole. The demon is immortal, possesses an endless hunger for souls, has superhuman strength, and is able to empower others with demonic abilities.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Blade: The Vampire-Hunter Vol 1 #8</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Ian Edginton</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lord_of_the_Deep">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lord of the Deep</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a malevolent lovecraftian -like entity in the fictional universe of the rifts pencil-and-paper roleplaying game by palladium . It is somewhat similar in function to cthulhu and has some mythos overtones in its description . Some believe that is the originator of the kraken myth of pre-cataclysmic earth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Rifts"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Palladium Games</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Innsmouth_Covenant">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Innsmouth Covenant</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the diary of hannah greeley" is a short story by american jennifer m. oaks . It was self-published in the chapbook collection the brides of innsmouth (year unknown) it was reused as a plot device for oaks's companion piece, "the diary of hannah greeley"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jennifer_M._Oaks"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Brides_of_Innsmouth"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sonia_H._Greene">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftsCoAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonFictionAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sonia H. Greene</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1972 December 26</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sonia haft greene was a one-time pulp fiction writer and amateur publisher, a single mother, business woman and successful milliner . She is best known for her two-year marriage to american weird fiction writer h. p. lovecraft . Greene was a president of the united amateur press association .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>Ichnia Ukraine</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasChildrenR>infant boy (name unknown) Florence Carol Greene (Carol Weld)</ex:hasChildrenR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1883 March 16</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Asenath">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Asenath</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ashley Dioses United States English Genre(s) Horror Wildside Press Weirdbook Annual 2 date February 2019 " " is a poem by American Ashley Dioses , written on the Cthulhu Mythos established over many decades by many authors. Synopsis The four verses are, in essence, a pared-down retelling of " The Thing on the Doorstep " by Howard Phillips Lovecraft . History "" was published in the Wildside Press anthology Weirdbook Annual 2 in February 2019.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ashley_Dioses"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Weirdbook Annual 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brotherhood_of_the_Yellow_Sign">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cults"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Brotherhood of the Yellow Sign</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationO rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hastur"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesO>Brothers of the Yellow Sign</ex:hasAlternativeNamesO>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesO>Cult of the Yellow Sign</ex:hasAlternativeNamesO>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The , also known as the brothers of the yellow sign and the cult of the yellow sign, is an evil fanatic cult of hastur in its king in yellow form . Occasionally they gather to destroy mi-go outposts and to worship hastur and shub-niggurath .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Chemb</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Claret</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Colia Thalna</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Druf</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Dulius Decula</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Garniss</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Giussppe Colombo</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Harcourt</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Khorbon</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Livius Carbo</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Lucius</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Malcolm Quarrie</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Milos</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Milton Drac</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Octavius</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>People of Ssanu</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>People of Valusia</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Resseka</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Roberto Anzalone</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Thomas Villiers</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasPurposeO>Assist Hastur to become Earth's living god</ex:hasPurposeO>
    <ex:hasPurposeO>Open a portal of Far Realm from Carcosa to Arcanis</ex:hasPurposeO>
    <ex:hasPurposeO>Reach</ex:hasPurposeO>
    <ex:hasPurposeO>bring Hastur to Earth .</ex:hasPurposeO>
    <ex:hasPurposeO>enter Carcosa.</ex:hasPurposeO>
    <ex:hasPurposeO>spread maddening influence of Hastur upon humanity.</ex:hasPurposeO>
    <ex:hasTypeO>Cult</ex:hasTypeO>
    <ex:isLocatedAtO>Coryon</ex:isLocatedAtO>
    <ex:isLocatedAtO>Freeport</ex:isLocatedAtO>
    <ex:isLocatedAtO>Liberportus</ex:isLocatedAtO>
    <ex:isLocatedAtO>Vastalanium</ex:isLocatedAtO>
    <ex:wasCreatedBynO rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Futurama_Comics">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Futurama Comics</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>is the name of the main series of , which includes all Futurama comic issues excluding four crossovers and two special issues, with another special issue simply being a variant cover for "Monkey Sea, Monkey Doom!". In February 2017, it was announced that no further issues of would be published in print and all future issues from issue 82 onward would only be released in the Futuramaland app. In the prologue to #49 , Turanga Leela has just come back from a bad date with Cthulhu , one of a series of references to and namechecks of the Mythos in the Futurama series.</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humankind_in_the_Cthulhu_Mythos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Humankind in the Cthulhu Mythos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Products of elder thing technology differs from its real-world counterpart in a number of ways . Its ability to interbreed with vastly different beings (usually referred to as "miscegenation" in lovecraft's writings) and its origins . Some believe that the ancestors of modern humans might have originated from the original fifth planet of the solar system .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stuart_Hartwell">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Stuart Hartwell</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_University"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Hartwell is a fictional character created by american author peter rawlik for his cthulhu mythos stories . He made his debut in the episodic novel reanimators . He was a student and protégé of celebrated miskatonic university physician dr. allan halsey .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Weird_Company"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Reanimators"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Peter_Rawlik"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Last_Night_on_Earth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Last Night on Earth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Edward Morris United States English Genre(s) Horror Dark Regions Press Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror date 2017 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by American Edward Morris . Synopsis In this very short tale, a child writes down the horrors he witnesses during the Mi-Go occupation of Earth , amongst them the death of his parents, aliens wearing wax masks to appear human, and the Akeley family patiently waiting their arrival. Characters The Unnamed Narrator , a child living in an apparently remote mountainside area. History "" was published in the Dark Regions Press anthology Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror in 2017.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Edward_Morris"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stephen_Strange">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Stephen Strange</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Doctor strange is a superhero in the fictional marvel universe . Created in 1963, he has been one of its main superheroes, a b-list hero with several of his own comic book series . He has clashed with more old ones than any other of earth's heroes .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Final_Defense"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Marvel_Premiere_%28Doctor_Strange%29"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Midnight_Massacre"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Montesi_Formula"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Ascent into Hell . Vampiric Verses</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Born Again</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Strange Tales Vol 1 10</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Stan Lee</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Steve Ditko</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Wentworth_Akeley">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Henry Wentworth Akeley</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A farmer residing at the akeley farm on black mountain, . Vermont, he is a correspondent of professor . Albert wilmarth . He is beset by several home invasions and killed by these outer beings from . Yoggoth . He has one documented relative, his son, who lives in . San diego .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Documents_in_the_Case_of_Elizabeth_Akeley"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtC>Brain in a Mi-Go brain cylinder en route to Yuggoth</ex:isLocatedAtC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Whisperer_in_Darkness"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#E-poh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>E-poh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Lloigor</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Zhar</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Plateau of Sung Powers and Abilities Sorcery Leader of the Tcho-Tcho people Zhar and Lloigor Tcho-Tcho First appearance AWD : " The Lair of the Star-Spawn " EXP : " The Descent into the Abyss " Created by August Derleth and Mark Schorer is a character created by August Derleth and Mark Schorer for their short story " The Lair of the Star-Spawn ". Biography is a Tcho-Tcho sorcerer from the fabled city of Alaozar in the Plateau of Sung , Burma, and leads his people in worship of Zhar and Lloigor . He is "slightly taller" than the typical four-foot-tall Tcho-Tcho, and "disfigured by a hump on his back". He is said to be over 7,000 years old ( AWD : " The Lair of the Star-Spawn "). According to Lin Carter 's " The Descent into the Abyss ", he is the prototype of the Tcho-Tcho people, the first member of his to be created.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Descent_into_the_Abyss"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lair_of_the_Star-Spawn"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#August_Derleth"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_Schorer"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Big_Nasty">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Big Nasty</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A small team of researchers from miskatonic university uncover a frozen chthonian at the old starkweather-moore antarctic expedition site . When the worm defrosts, they face a frantic battle for survival .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Josh_Reynolds"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2003</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lair_of_the_Dreamer:_A_Cthulhu_Mythos_Omnibus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lair of the Dreamer: A Cthulhu Mythos Omnibus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Franklyn Searight United States English Hippocampus Press Release Date July 2007 308 is a collection of short stories by American Franklyn Searight . Overview First published by Hippocampus Press in July 2007, Lair of the Dreamer contains a total of ten Mythos stories and an introduction by Robert M. Price . It runs to 308 , and has not been reissued. Contents "Tainted Lineage" introduction by Robert M. Price "There Is a Pond" "The Sorcerer's Pipe" "The Innsmouth Head" "Armillaria" "The Guardian of the Pit" "The Closing of the Gate" "Mists of Death" ( with Richard F. Searight ) "Stomach Pains" "Lair of the Dreamer" Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Franklyn_Searight"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>308</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>July 2007</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Old_One_%28Buffy%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Old One (Buffy)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The old ones were pure-breed demons that ruled earth prior to man . They bred with or infected the mortal animals of earth, creating 100s of demon species . 1000s of the old ones were buried in the "deeper well", whose corpses or essences were contained within sarcophagi to prevent their resurrection .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Blue_Canoe">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Blue Canoe</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A letter from a dead man describes the day, many years ago, when his life was changed by a chance encounter with an alien entity . The stranger caused a wave of madness to sweep through the patrons before burning the building to the ground .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Ben Scotti</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 1</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Thing_on_the_Doorstep_%28DART_production%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleAudioAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Thing on the Doorstep (DART production)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The thing on the doorstep is a dark adventures radio theatre production by the h. p. lovecraft historical society . Based on the short story of the same name . Features a set of period-authentic props to enhance the immersive experience .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Thing_on_the_Doorstep"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sarnath">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sarnath</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Sarnath the Magnificent ( The Doom That Came to Sarnath ) Sarnath the Doomed ( The Nameless City )</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Created by howard phillips lovecraft was a vast, majestic and powerful city in mnar , an extremely remote land on earth . Its dwellers were human empire builders of immense wealth; but their mighty city was built on blood . Not long after they laid its foundations, the people of had the ancient city of ib , where dwelled the thuum'ha .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Nameless City The Quest of Iranon</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Humans</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>The land of Mnar</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>likely on Earth</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Doom_That_Came_to_Sarnath"/>
    <ex:wasDestroyedOnL>000 B.C.E. circa 8</ex:wasDestroyedOnL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Willis_Conover">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftsCorrespondents"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Willis Conover</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1996 17 May 1996</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Willis conover, jr. (18 december 1920 - 17 may 1996) was an american broadcaster and music producer . He corresponded with horror author howard phillips lovecraft at the age of fifteen . Their correspondence has been collected in the volume lovecraft at last .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Young weird fiction fan who edited the Science-Fantasy Correspondent (1936–1937) and was a late correspondent of Lovecraft. He fashioned his brief correspondence with Lovecraft into a splendid book, Lovecraft at Last (1975).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>New York USA Buffalo</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Willis Clark Conover. Jr.</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Lovecraft's correspondent</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1920 18 December 1920</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_Warner">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>David Warner</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>24 July 2022</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>David hattersley warner was an english actor who had multiple roles in the cthulhu mythos . He played amos hackshaw in cast a deadly spell and chancellor thayer of miskatonic university in the unnamable ii: the statement of randolph carter . He also performed a great number of characters in the doctor who franchise, both in television and audio plays .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#England Manchester</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>David Hattersley Warner</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Actor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>29 July 1941</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
