  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Forte">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Frank Forte</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author Filmmaker United States https://frankforte.com/  is an American artist, author, filmmaker and comic book creator who has written numerous Lovecraftian and Cthulhu Mythos stories, and also worked as a storyboard artist for the HBO television series Lovecraft Country , itself based on the novel of the same name by Matt Ruff . In addition, he is the founder of indy publishing outfit Asylum Press, through which many of his works have been released. Selected Works Collections Beyond Lovecraft (2020) Short Stories " Asphinxiation " (2020) " The House at the End of the Street " (2020) " The Connection " (2020) " The Sleeping One " (2020) " Shocking Terrors #13 " (2020) " Dead Thing " (2020) " Incident at the Hanford Inn " (2020) " The Insidious Doom " (2020) " The Strange Terror From Beyond " (2020) " The Cursed Appeal of Knowledge " (2020) " An Account of Ozgamuun " (2020) " That Which Lurks " (2020) " The Experiment " (2020) Film &amp; Television Lovecraft Country (2020, storyboard artist) See Also Images by External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://frankforte.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Filmmaker</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Witch_Hunt_%281994_film%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Witch Hunt (1994 film)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Witch hunt is a 1994 sequel to cast a deadly spell . Film takes place in a fictional los angeles where magic is real . Lovecraft is hired by film star to dig up dirt on her husband .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Joseph Dougherty</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Crime</ex:hasGenreW>
