    <rdfs:label>Providence, Rhode Island</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Providence Rhode Island, USA City Founded in 1636 Notable Features Brown University Swan Point Cemetery Humans First appearance HPL : " The Call of Cthulhu " HPL : " From Beyond " CIRCLE : " The Shambler from the Stars " HPL : " The Haunter of the Dark " CIRCLE : " The Shadow from the Steeple " HPL : " The Shunned House " HPL : " Ibid " HPL : The Case of Charles Dexter Ward AWD : " Providence: Two Gentlemen Meet at Midnight " Providence is H. P. Lovecraft 's home town and is the capital and the most populous city of the U.S. state of Rhode Island , and one of the first cities established in the United States. Located in Providence County, it is the estimated third-largest city in the New England region. The area which is now Providence was first settled in June 1636 by Roger Williams, and was one of the original Thirteen Colonies of the United States. External links at Wikipedia</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#From_Beyond"/>
