  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dunwich_Horror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dunwich Horror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>It is considered one of the core stories of the cthulhu mythos . Dunwich is "a vague echo of the decadent massachusetts countryside around springfield" the name "dunwich" may have been inspired by the town of greenwich .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Journey_Into_Mystery_Vol_2_4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleComicBookAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Journey Into Mystery Vol 2 4</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Journey Into Mystery Vol 2 #4 H. P. Lovecraft (original story) Ron Goulart (adaptation) United States English Marvel Comics Publication date January 23, 1973 Journey Into Mystery Vol 2 #4 is an issue of Marvel Comics ' long-running horror anthology series. It features an adaptation of H. P. Lovecraft 's short story " The Haunter of the Dark ", written by Ron Goulart and illustrated by Gene Colan. The following issue featured an adaptation of Robert Bloch 's continuation " The Shadow from the Steeple ". External Links at the Marvel Database wiki</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Ron Goulart</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1973 January 23</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Twas_the_Night_Before_Madness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>'Twas the Night Before Madness</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Twas the Night Before Madness S. Alessandro Martinez English Cthulhu Christmas Special and Other Lovecraftian Yuletide Tales date November 2017 "' ‘Twas the Night Before Madness " is a festive Cthulhu Mythos poem by S. Alessandro Martinez. It was published in the Jesse Dedman / William C. Marchese -edited anthology Cthulhu Christmas Special and Other Lovecraftian Yuletide Tales in November 2017. Synopsis The twelve four-line verses describe how, at Christmas time, a cultist conducts a murderous ritual to summon the Old Ones to our plane of existence. As they return to the material realm, they grant him incredible knowledge, but shatter his sanity in the process. Trivia The entities summoned by the cultist include Yog-Sothoth , Dagon , Hastur , Yig , Gla'aki , Cthulhu , Ithaqua , Nyarlathotep , and Cthylla .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>S. Alessandro Martinez</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Cthulhu Christmas Special</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Lovecraftian Yuletide Tales</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Adrian_Cole">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Adrian Cole</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Adrian Christopher Synnot Cole Pseudonym(s) Norma N. Johns Connection to the Mythos Author Editor Birth Date 22 July 1949 Plymouth, England, UK United Kingdom Adrian Christopher Synnot Cole is a British author and editor, many of whose works have a distinctly Lovecraftian flavour. In particular, his Nick Nightmare series is a hybrid of hardboiled detective stories and the dark horror and fantasy of the Cthulhu Mythos . Cole's Mythos works have been published in anthologies such as The Cthulhu Mythos Megapack and Cthulhu: Weirdbook Annual 2 . Selected Bibliography Short Fiction " The Crossing " (1994) " Dark Destroyer " (2000) " The War Among the Gods " (2008) " Enter the Cobweb Queen " (2019) External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#England UK Plymouth</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Adrian Christopher Synnot Cole</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Norma N. Johns</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Editor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>22 July 1949</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
