    <rdfs:label>Geschichten aus dem Cthulhu-Mythos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jeffrey Thomas Cover Artist Babbarammdass Germany German H. P. Lovecrafts Bibliothek des Schreckens Festa Release Date August 2012 333 is a selection of German- translations of the works of American Jeffrey Thomas . It was published by Festa in August 2012 as part of thei r H. P. Lovecrafts Bibliothek des Schreckens . Contents "Meine Frau, der Shoggoth" (" I Married a Shoggoth ") "Die Gebeine der Großen Alten" (" The Bones of the Old Ones ") "Die Avatare der Großen Alten" (" The Avatars of the Old Ones ") "Die Abkömmlinge der Großen Alten" (" The Young of the Old Ones ") "Zu Diensten" (" Servile ") "Konglomerat" (" Conglomerate ") "Hinter undurchsichtigem Glas" (" Through Obscure Glass ") "Aus dem Bauch der Hölle" (" Out of the Belly of Sheol ") "Die Fratze Baphomets" (" The Face of Baphomet ") "Leichenkerzen" (" Corpse Candles ") "Pazuzus Kinder" (" Pazuzu's Children ") "Der Tanz der Ugghiutu" ("The Dance of Ugghiutu") "Die Kinder des Drachen" ("Children of the Dragon") "Zwischen Providence und Punktown" interview with Jeffrey Thomas by Christian Endres</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>Germany</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>333</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>German</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecrafts_Bibliothek_des_Schreckens"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 2012</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#An_Account_of_Ozgamuun">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>An Account of Ozgamuun</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Frank Forte English Asylum Press Beyond Lovecraft date September 2020  " " is a Lovecraftian short story by American Frank Forte . It was published in the collection Beyond Lovecraft by Asylum Press in September 2020. Synopsis When his uncle dies, a man comes into possession of the old man's journal. Within it he finds an account of how Laurens can Ginneken, the uncle, crossed paths with an ancient evil in the fjords of Sweden, and how this encounter wrought a horrendous change on his mind and body. The journal further tells of how this evil was later washed into the ocean by Swedish authorities and causes the man to wonder just what repercussions this may have for the human race in the future…</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Forte"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beyond_Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>September 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
