  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tiania">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dreamers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tiania</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Elder Gods</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Titus crow is a character created by brian lumley as part of his titus crow series of cthulhu mythos novels . She resides in a floating palace in the other-dimensional realm of elysia and is the ward of the elder god known as kthanid .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Clock_of_Dreams"/>
    <ex:hasCharacterMateC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Transition_of_Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Great_Stone_Face">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Great Stone Face</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nathaniel Hawthorne United States English The Snow-Image, and Other Tales date 1850 " " is a novelette by the late American Nathaniel Hawthorne , first published in The Snow-Image, and Other Tales in 1850. It has been cited by leading scholars S. T. Joshi and David E. Schultz as one of the influences behind H. P. Lovecraft 's The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath . Synopsis The story concerns a New England prophecy which tells that a native-born man will one day look upon a local geographical feature and be recognised as "the greatest and noblest personage of his time". The story then goes on to recite the procession of men who attempt to fulfil the prophecy. External Links " " at Wikipedia References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nathaniel_Hawthorne"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Tales</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The Snow-Image</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1850</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ward_Phillips">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dreamers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ward Phillips</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The name of several characters in the cthulhu mythos is derived from the name of lovecraft . The name of the reverend in august derleth's " the lamp of alhazred" is the closest of all to lovecraft . Lovecraft died at the same age he was when he died .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lamp_of_Alhazred"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Complete Dreamlands</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Through_the_Gates_of_the_Silver_Key"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#San_Francisco">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>San Francisco</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The city is the setting for a number of cthulhu mythos stories by other writers . It was founded as a spanish mission in 1776 and claimed by the united states in 1846 . Its population was 506,676 in 1920, rising to 873,965 by 2020 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>Dagon The Call of Cthulhu The Last Test The Electric Executioner</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>City</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#California"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>USA</ex:isLocatedAtL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Scions_of_Forever">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Scions of Forever</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional organization in the cthulhutech pencil-and-paper roleplaying game by wildfire llc . It's rumored that it's members can manipulate time and many of them are virtually immortal . They revere yog-sothoth and are the world's most private and quiet citizens .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Klenze">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Klenze</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>1917 August 12th</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Imperial German Navy</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>August 12th, 1917 Germany Navy Lieutenant (Submariner) Imperial German Navy Human First appearance HPL : " The Temple " Created by H. P. Lovecraft Lieutenant is a fictional character in the story " The Temple " by H. P. Lovecraft . He was a lieutenant and second-in-command serving aboard the German submarine U-29 under Lieutenant-Commander Karl Heinrich during the First World War. At the culmination of the supernatural events experienced by the crew of the submarine, and Heinrich were the only men aboard left alive by the time the disabled U-29 came to rest among the underwater ruins of an Atlantean city. eventually went mad and took his own life by exiting the submarine.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Temple"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ashley_K._Williams">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ashley K. Williams</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Chosen One</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Lady Ash</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>She-Ash</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lady ash is a hero in the fictional army of darkness universe who was created in 2012 by marat mychaels, elliott r. serrano . She first appeared in issue #1 of the 3rd volume of army of darkness by dynamite entertainment . Like ash worked at s-mart and ended up fighting the forces of the necronomicon ex mortis .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Army of Darkness Vol 3 1</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Elliott R. Serrano</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Marat Mychaels</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Schneider">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Schneider</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>1917 June 28th</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Imperial German Navy</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>June 28th, 1917 Germany Navy Engineer (Submariner) Imperial German Navy Human First appearance HPL : " The Temple " Created by H. P. Lovecraft Engineer is a fictional character in the story " The Temple " by H. P. Lovecraft . He served as an engineer aboard the German submarine U-29 under Lieutenant-Commander Karl Heinrich during the First World War. During the supernatural events experienced by the crew, and fellow engineer Raabe were both killed by an explosion in the engine room.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Temple"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars_of_the_Old_Ones">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Avatars of the Old Ones</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jeffrey Thomas Todd H. C. Fischer English Imelod Publications Release Date 1999 Preceded by The Bones of the Old Ones and Other Lovecraftian Tales is a chapbook collection of Cthulhu Mythos fiction by American Jeffrey Thomas . It was published by Imelod Publications in 1999 and features illustrations by Todd H. C. Fischer . also includes an introduction by the late American W. H. Pugmire . The two would later go on to collaborate on the Enoch Coffin series of stories published in 2013, and one of Thomas's stories in this volume - " Through Obscure Glass " - takes place in Pugmire's fictional Sesqua Valley setting. Contents " Through Obscure Glass " " Corpse Candles " " The "</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1999</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Castle_Freak_%282020_film%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleFilmAndTelevisionAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Castle Freak (2020 film)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Castle freak is a 2020 remake of the 1995 film of the same name . It was directed by tate steinsiek from a script by kathy charles, based on h. p. lovecraft's short story " the outsider ". (" the dunwich horror " is also a major inspiration.)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWriterW>Kathy Charles</ex:hasWriterW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dunwich_Horror"/>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Outsider"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2020 December 4</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
