  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#In_Memory_of_Day_%28Call_of_Cthulhu_LCG%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>In Memory of Day (Call of Cthulhu LCG)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>In Memory of Day Fantasy Flight Games Publication Date 2008 Living Card Game Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game In Memory of Day is an expansion pack for Fantasy Flight Games ' Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game . Overview The second Asylum Pack in the Dreamlands Cycle series of expansions, In Memory of Day contains 60 cards in the standard format of three sets of 20 unique cards. First released in 2008, it was later reissued through Fantasy Flights' in-house print-on-demand service, but was discontinued in 2015 with the demise of Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game . Contents The Captain, Dreamlands Navigator (Character; The Agency) Prize Pistol (Support; Neutral) Daybreak! (Event; Neutral) Obsessive Insomniac (Character; Miskatonic University ) Dreamlore Documents (Support; Miskatonic University) Clover Club Regular (Character; Syndicate) Forcibly Removed (Event; Syndicate) Day of the Deep Ones (Event; Cthulhu ) Curse of Darkness (Event; Cthulhu) The Seventy Steps, Of Light Slumber (Support; Hastur ) The Seven Hundred Steps, Of Deeper Slumber (Support; Hastur) Enraged Gug (Character; Yog-Sothoth ) City of Gugs, Beneath the Earth (Support; Yog-Sothoth) Ghoul Spawn (Character; Shub-Niggurath ) Back From the Dead (Event; Shub-Niggurath) Secretive Zoog (Character; Neutral) The Enchanted Wood (Support; Neutral) Kaman-Thah, Priest of the Dreamlands (Character; Neutral) Nasht, Priest of the Dreamlands (Character; Neutral) Slime Mold (Character; Neutral) Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2008</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Barrens">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Barrens</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story's narrator is the proprietor of a small accounting firm in new jersey . She is contacted by an ex-lover from college, jonathan creighton . He seeks her help investigating the folklore of jersey's pine barrens . As she takes him deeper into ' mysteries, her sanity and reality itself are at risk .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#F._Paul_Wilson"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecrafts_Legacy"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 1990</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Rise_of_Yog-Sothoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Rise of Yog-Sothoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ash Cheshire English Fate of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Evil Hat Productions Release Date 2021 23 is a timeline supplement for the Fate of Cthulhu horror roleplaying game. Written by Ash Cheshire, it was published by Evil Hat Productions in a solely digital format in 2021 . Overview References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Ash Cheshire</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>23</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fate_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2021</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Murder_at_the_Motel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Murder at the Motel</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The dark rites of cthulhu is a short story by american writer brian m. sammons . The sorcerer grigory is dragged off by creatures who wish to restore the balance of life . The story was published in the collection the dark rites of cthulhu .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_M._Sammons"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dark_Rites_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror-Horn">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Horror-Horn</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story focuses on a man who vacations in the swiss alps, around the ungehoerhorn mountains . Days later, the man wanders in the forest and meets one of these people, an old hag of a woman . He manages to escape it, but is horrified beyond wits .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#E._F._Benson"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Huchinson's Magazine</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1922 September</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beneath_the_Pimple">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Beneath the Pimple</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Bryn fortey's short story was first published in 2021 issue of lovecraftiana zine . It tells the tale of how a centuries long plan was orchestrated to trick the duplicitous outer god olkoth . The phantom dog is gelert, the faithful hound of a well-known and tragic welsh legend .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Bryn Fortey</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 4</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2021</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Resurrected_III:_Out_of_the_Vault">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Resurrected III: Out of the Vault</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Heather Hudson English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Pagan Publishing Release Date 2002 164 is a scenario supplement for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu horror roleplaying game. Written by an ensemble lineup of games designers, it was published by third-party content provider Pagan Publishing in 2002 . Overview Contents "Within You Without You" by John Tynes , illustrated by Blair Reynolds "The Travesty" by Chris Klepac , illustrated by Toren Atkinson "The House on Stratford Lane" by John H. Crowe, III , illustrated by Heather Hudson "The Beast in the Abbey" by Kevin A. Ross , illustrated by Heather Hudson "The Lambton Worm" by Steve Hatherly, illustrated by Heather Hudson "Blood on the Tracks" by J. Todd Kingrea , illustrated by Toren Atkinson "Dark Harvest" by Kevin A. Ross, illustrated by Heather Hudson "What Goes Around Comes Around" by Jeff Moeller , illustrated by Toren Atkinson "All Good Children" by Chris Klepac, illustrated by Heather Hudson "In Media Res" by John Tynes, illustrated by Toren Atkinson Design Team Written by: John Crowe , Steve Hatherley, J. Todd Kingrea , Chris Klepac , Jeff Moeller , Kevin Ross , and John Scott Tynes Artwork by: Toren Atkinson, Jane Brooks, Heather Hudson, and Blair Reynolds Production staff: Brian Appleton Gallery References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>164</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2002</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Mark_of_Cthulhu:_An_Escape_Room_Adventure_Book">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Mark of Cthulhu: An Escape Room Adventure Book</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Gauthier Wendling David Chapoulet English Genre(s) Gamebook Skyhorse Publishing Release Date May 2, 2023 288 is a Cthulhu Mythos gamebook written by Gauthier Wendling and published by Skyhorse Publishing in 2023, featuring illustrations by David Chapoulet. It is inspired by the multipath adventure genre that was popularized by the Fighting Fantasy and Choose Your Own Adventure gamebooks, as well as real-life escape room challenges. Overview</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Gauthier Wendling</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Gamebook</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>288</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2023 May 2</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
