  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tuscan_Rituals">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosBooksFictional"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tuscan Rituals</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a book which contains rituals to the god Summanus . It originated in Tuscany. A copy is held by the British Museum. Created by Brian Lumley in his short story " What Dark God? " from the Arkham House anthology Nameless Places , later reprinted in his vampire tales anthology A Coven of Vampires .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cold_One">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ServitorRaces"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cold One</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Aphoom-Zhah"/>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Rlim_Shaikorth"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Ghosts</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Hands of the White Worm</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Servants of the Cold Flame</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Snow Demons</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Ylidheem</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cold ones are a fictional race expanded on by chaosium in 1994 for the call of cthulhu role playing game . They appear as wailing humanoid spectres of swirling snow and vapor, appearing and disappearing into snowy skies . Whether they are a distinct species or the tortured souls of once-human worshippers of the great old ones is disputed .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>Ghost-like beings</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>appearing as human-shaped swirling snow</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>vapor</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Light from the Pole</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Clark_Ashton_Smith"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Hounds_of_the_Dawn">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Hounds of the Dawn</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the hounds of dawn" is a lovecraftian short story by british-born william meikle . It was self-published in the chapbook collection up from the deep in may 2023 . The story is told in the form of an account written by a roman slave .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Lovecraftian horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shadows_of_an_Inner_Darkness"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dreams_of_a_Diseased_Mind_%28collection%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dreams of a Diseased Mind (collection)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dreams of a Diseased Mind Steve Lines Steve Lines Cover Artist Steve Lines English B. J. M. Press Release Date 2000 63 Dreams of a Diseased Mind is a collection of poetry by the late , artist and editor Steve Lines , who also provided the cover art and an illustration for each poem. Running to a total of 63 , it was published by B. J. M. Press in 2000. Contents "Down to a Sunless Sea" "The Comptonbury Horror" "The Feaster in the Tomb" "The Ghoul" "The Black Pharaoh" "Pickman's Painting" "Dreamhound" "Black Flame" "R'lyeh Rising" "The Gathering" "Monolith" "The Severnford Seals" "The Mad Poet" "Beyond" "Strange Aeons" "The Tind'losi Hounds" "Nctosa and Nctolhu" "The Black Stone" "Innsmouth Jewellery" "The Delirium of Nish" "Flower Woman" .The Nightmares of Nebb" "Shul'nar Thak" "The Silent Sea" "When They Return"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Steve_Lines"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>63</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2000</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ashes">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ashes</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Horror short story by american authors h. p. lovecraft and c.m. Eddy, jr. it first appeared in the march 1924 issue of weird tales . The narrator, identified only as " prague ", is paid a visit by his dear friend malcolm bruce . It is one of the few short stories by lovecraft that has a happy ending .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Howard_Phillips_Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>C. M. Eddy. Jr.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Army_of_Darkness_Vs._Hack_/_Slash">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Army of Darkness Vs. Hack / Slash</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Tim Seeley Daniel Lester English Dynamite Entertainment Release Date July 2013 - Feb 2014 Media Type Comic book Army of Darkness Vs. Hack/Slash is a 6-issue crossover mini-series written by Tim Seeley. Synopsis Cassandra Hack and Ash Williams join forces against the Army of Darkness.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Tim Seeley</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>July 2013 - Feb 2014</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyaghoggua_%28short_poem%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nyaghoggua (short poem)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nyaghoggua Full story online here Robert A. W. Lowndes United States English Famous Fantastic Mysteries date April 1941 Nyaghoggua is a Cthulhu Mythos poem by Robert A. W. Lowndes , a correspondent of Lovecraft . It was published in Famous Fantastic Mysteries in April 1941. Contents</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_A._W._Lowndes"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
