  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Call_of_Cthulhu:_Dark_Corners_of_the_Earth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Call of Cthulhu: Dark Corners of the Earth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Survival horror is a video game released in 2005 for the xbox and 2006 for pc platforms, developed by headfirst productions and published by bethesda softworks . The game is based on the call of cthulhu role-playing game by chaosium and loosely follows the plot of h.p. Lovecraft's novella the shadow over innsmouth . The main character is a private investigator suffering from amnesia following a mysterious case in 1915</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2005 (Xbox) 2006 (PC)</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Mark_of_Madness_%28Call_of_Cthulhu_LCG%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Mark of Madness (Call of Cthulhu LCG)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Mark of Madness Fantasy Flight Games Publication Date 2015 Living Card Game Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game The Mark of Madness is an expansion pack for Fantasy Flight Games ' Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game . Overview The tenth and final of the deluxe expansion sets, The Mark of Madness contains the standard set of 165 cards divided into three sets of 55 unique cards. As is also standard, the focus is on one particular faction (in the case the Hastur faction), although there are also a handful of cards for each of the other factions along with some general-purpose ones. First released in 2015, it was discontinued later the same year with the demise of Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game , likely due to licensing considerations. Contents Starving Artist (Character; Hastur) Moon Worshiper (Character; Hastur) Quixotic Poet (Character; Hastur) Brother of the Black Lotus (Character; Hastur) Starry-Eyed Adherent (Character; Hastur) Surrealist (Character; Hastur) Swift Byakhee (Character; Hastur) Unhinged Laborer (Character; Hastur) Demented Composer (Character; Hastur) Patron of the Arts (Character; Hastur) Mad Maudlin, Touched (Character; Hastur) Tom O'Bedlam, Well-Adjusted Sociopath (Character; Hastur) Erich Zann , Bringer of Music (Character; Hastur) Benjamin Herriot, A Unique Perspective (Character; Hastur) Daughter of Atlach-Nacha (Character; Hastur) A Scheme of Byakhees (Character; Hastur) Alila, Queen of Perdition (Character; Hastur) Tru'nembra , The Angel of Music (Character; Hastur) Hastur, He Who Is Not To Be Named (Character; Hastur) Straightjacket (Support; Hastur) Catacombs de Paris, Illuminated Labyrinth (Support; Hastur) Fregoli Delusion (Support; Hastur) The Dikes of Ys, Holding Back the Tides (Support; Hastur) Unspeakable Promise (Support; Hastur) Drawing the Sign , Mark of Madness (Support; Hastur) Forbidden Sutra, Tainted and Twisted (Support; Hastur) Corruption of Enlightenment (Event; Hastur) The Dance of the Yellow King (Event; Hastur) Acute Melancholia (Event; Hastur) Lure of the Moon (Event; Hastur) Cassilda's Song (Event; Hastur) Induce Terror (Event; Hastur) The Door that will not Close (Conspiracy; Hastur) Whispers of Aoide (Conspiracy; Hastur) Opening Night (Conspiracy; Hastur) The Supplicant, True Believer (Character; Neutral) The Archmage, Arcanis, Master of the Arcane Arts (Character; Neutral) Thaumaturgical Insight (Event; Neutral) Jean-Jacques Minot, Obsessive Tactician (Character; The Agency) Ward of Protection (Support; The Agency) Mandy Aurel, An Old Soul (Character; Cthulhu ) Striking Tentacle (Event; Cthulhu) Walter Gilman , Resister of Temptation (Character; Miskatonic University ) Black Book of Azathoth , Truth...at a Cost (Support; Miskatonic University) Maria Suleman, Mother of Many (Character; Shub-Niggurath ) The Thousand (Character; Shub-Niggurath) Argent Adept (Character; Silver Twilight ) Monsieur Lamar, Often Lucid (Character; Silver Twilight) Dmitri Konstantinov, Taking the Long View (Character; Silver Twilight) Enchanted Gargoyle (Support; Silver Twilight) Invocation of the Abyss (Event; Silver Twilight) Parrain François, Paranoid and Violent (Character; Syndicate) Milieu Enforcement (Support; Syndicate) La Comtesse, Subverter of Plans (Character; Yog-Sothoth ) Seer of the Gate (Character; Yog-Sothoth) Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2015</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
