  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Elizabeth_Bear">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Elizabeth Bear</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sarah bear is a science fiction writer who publishes under the name . She has repeatedly written stories connected to the cthulhu mythos . Her boojumverse stories combine the cthulhu mythos with the lewis carroll bestiary .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Connecticut Hartford</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Sarah Bear Elizabeth Wishnevsky</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.elizabethbear.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>22 September 1971</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Golden_Goblin_Press">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SmallPress"/>
    <rdfs:label>Golden Goblin Press</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Current Status Active Key People Oscar Rios (president) Lisa Padol (staff editor) Horror Roleplay gaming https://www.goldengoblinpress.com/ is an indie publishing house and third-party gaming content provider founded by prolific games designer Oscar Rios . Overview Taking their name from a fictional company which appears in Robert E. Howard 's short story " The Black Stone ", is a small publisher which focuses primarily on providing licensed third-party gaming content for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game, particularly the Cthulhu Invictus time period. They also publish a certain amount of fiction, again largely tied to Call of Cthulhu , along with some merchandising. Selected Publications Fiction Tales of Cthulhu Invictus (2015) Heroes of Red Hook (2016) Further Tales of Cthulhu Invictus (2017) Tails of Terror (2018) Shadows of an Inner Darkness (2019) Tales of Cthulhu Invictus: Britannia (2021) Children of Lovecraft Country (2020) An Eldritch Legacy (2020) Gaming Supplements The Legacy of Arrius Lurco (2011) Island of Ignorance: The Third Cthulhu Companion (2013) De Horrore Cosmico (2015) Tales of the Caribbean (2016) Cold Warning (2017) Fronti Nulla Fides (2019) An Inner Darkness (2020) The Eldritch New England Holiday Collection (2021) The Mystery of April Snow Tales of Valor Heroes and Heroines of Britannia Heroes and Heroines of the Shadow War 7th Edition Cthulhu Invictus Screen Terror of Octobernomicon Britannia &amp; Beyond (2023) References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.goldengoblinpress.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#C_M_Eddy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>C M Eddy</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1967</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Pulp fiction writer for whom Lovecraft revised several stories in 1923–1924 and who also worked with Lovecraft on ghostwriting work for Harry Houdini in 1926.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1896</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Disinterment_of_Venus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#AveroigneCycle"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ClarkAshtonSmithWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Disinterment of Venus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the disinternment of venus" is a short story by british author, set in french province of averoigne . Story relates the unearthing of a pagan statue of venus at the abbey of périgon . Eight monks are driven by lust to temporarily leave the abbey . Brother louis is crushed to death beneath the toppled sculpture's embrace .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Clark_Ashton_Smith"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Averoigne"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 1994</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Cthulhu_and_Other_Weird_Stories">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Call of Cthulhu and Other Weird Stories</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft English Genre(s) Horror Penguin Classics Release Date 1 October 1999 Media Type Print Followed by The Thing on the Doorstep and Other Weird Stories is an anthology of works by American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Publication History Published by Penguin Classics in 1999, was edited by S. T. Joshi , and contains an introduction and story notes of his. The stories contained within are the corrected versions previously published by Arkham House , which were also edited by Joshi. Contents " Dagon " " The Statement of Randolph Carter " " Facts Concerning the Late Arthur Jermyn and His Family " " Celephaïs " " Nyarlathotep " " The Picture in the House " " The Outsider " " Herbert West -- Reanimator " " The Hound " " The Rats in the Walls " " The Festival " " He " " Cool Air " " The Call of Cthulhu " " The Colour Out of Space " " The Whisperer in Darkness " " The Shadow Over Innsmouth " " The Haunter of the Dark " Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1 October 1999</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#John_Bell">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>John Bell</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Colonial Security</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Paxton Police Department</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>John "johnny" bell is a character created by american author jeffrey thomas . Made his first appearance in the 1995 short story " the bones of the old ones " bell is a recurrent protagonist in his punktown series of dystopian science fiction stories .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Avatars_of_the_Old_Ones"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Young_of_the_Old_Ones"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Bones_of_the_Old_Ones"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Eric_Stokes_Brooks">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Eric Stokes Brooks</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Blade is a human/vampire hybrid who was born to a woman bitten and killed by a vampire . Grew up into a vampire hunter, dedicating himself to hunting down and exterminating all vampires . Has clashed with their allies, the cult of the darkhold and once came under the influence of the elder god chthon .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Midnight_Massacre"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Montesi_Formula"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Curse of the Mutants</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>War of the Vampires</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Tomb of Dracula Vol 1 10</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Marv Wolfman</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Return_of_the_Lloigor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Return of the Lloigor</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Colin wilson's tale of the lloigor first appeared in tales of the cthulhu mythos in 1969 . The lloigor are alien entities that "existed as 'vortices' of power in their natural state" they enslaved humanity on mu before becoming weakened and retreating . They are responsible for the destruction of not only mu but atlantis and other lost cities .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Colin_Wilson"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tales_of_the_Cthulhu_Mythos"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1969</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Horror_on_the_Orient_Express">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Horror on the Orient Express</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Call of cthulhu is a horror roleplaying game developed by chaosium . Two editions were issued, a boxed set in 1991, and a revised hardcover release in 2013 . A board game spin-off of the game is planned to launch in 2024 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lynn_Willis"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_Morrison"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Penelope_Love"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_Watts"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Thomas_Ligotti"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Bernard Caleo</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Christian Lehmann</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Geoff Gillan</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Marion Anderson</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Nick Hagger</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Peter F. Jeffery</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Phil Anderson</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Russell Waters</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
