  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Unnamable_%28short_story%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Unnamable (short story)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the unnamable" is a short story by science fiction and horror writer h. p. lovecraft . It was written in 1923 and was first published in the july 1925 issue of weird tales . In the story, a mysterious entity attacks the two men, leaving them with various lacerations, including scarring from a horn-shaped object .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Keeper_of_the_Cage">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Keeper of the Cage</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The keeper was an enormous once-human monstrosity who dwelt deep within the dreamlands in the h.p. Lovecraft -inspired cthulhu mythos . As his name might suggest, he was the guardian of an enormous cage filled with beings who were to be sacrificed to the great old ones . Previously a mortal man who had been remade by the great old ones after they caught him trying to use their own power against them .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Clock of Dreams ( EXP )</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Challenge_from_Below">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#StoryCycles"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Challenge from Below</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Lore date December 1995-September 1996 is a story arc comprising four short works by different authors. Stories Part 1: " Under the Mound " ( Robert M. Price , 1995) Part 2: " The Trial " ( Peter Cannon , 1996) Part 3: " The Horror at the Lake " (Donald R. Burleson, 1996) Part 4: " Beyond the Wall of Time " ( Brian McNaughton , 1996)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lore</ex:isPublishedAsW>
