    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Haunted Clubhouse</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Leigh Carr Enmanuel Martinez Cover Artist Enmanuel Martinez English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Trepan Interactive Release Date 2017 21 : The Little Play House of Horrors is a scenario supplement for the Call of Cthulhu horror roleplaying game. Written by Leigh Carr and featuring artwork by Enmanuel Martinez , it was published by third-party content provider Trepan Interactive in 2017 ; both digital and print-on-demand editions were made available. Overview The storyline involves a young boy who has been sucked into another reality by an Interdimensional entity. The boy is now trying to find his way back, using his newfound psychic powers to acquire body matter, and stop anyone who tries to get in his way. Gallery References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Leigh_Carr"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>21</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Lonely_and_Curious_Country">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Lonely and Curious Country</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Matthew Carpenter , editor English Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos Ulthar Press Release Date August 4, 2015 236 : Tales from the Lands of Lovecraft is an anthology of Cthulhu Mythos fiction edited by Matthew Carpenter , and published in 2015 by Ulthar Press with a digital release landing the following year. The title of the anthology comes from the beginning of H. P. Lovecraft 's " The Dunwich Horror ": “When a traveller in north central Massachusetts takes the wrong fork at the junction of Aylesbury pike just beyond Dean's Corners he comes upon ...." In his introduction, editor Matthew Carpenter notes an explosion in the Mythos genre: "Over the last five years more than 50 Cthulhu Mythos story anthologies have been published," he maintains; "this does not include such genres as comic books, novels or children’s books." He adds: Contents Introduction by Matthew Carpenter "The Dreamer of Nothingness" by Steven Prizeman "Paudie O'Brien and the Bogman" by Seán Farrell "Turn on, Tune in, Infiltrate, Disrupt" by K H Vaughn "Down Through Black Abysses" by Pete Rawlik "Project Handbasket" by Rebecca Allred "Incense and Insensibilty" by Christine Morgan "Salt Water Bodies" by Susan Hicks Wong "Interrogation" by Damir Salkovic "Radical Division" by Jonathan Titchenal "Igawesdi" by Cliff Biggers "After Birth" by Brian M. Sammons &amp; Jamie D. Jenkins "Rehab" by Kevin Wetmore "Unsung Heroes" by Don Webb "The Litany of Yith" by Brett Davidson "The Third Oath of Dagon" by Robert M. Price "Down By the Highway Side" by Paul R. McNamee "In the Forest, with the Night" by Aaron J. French</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Matthew_Carpenter"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>editor</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>236</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2015 August 4</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Further_Tales_of_Cthulhu_Invictus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Further Tales of Cthulhu Invictus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Golden Goblin Press Release Date 2017 is an anthology of historical Cthulhu Mythos stories published by Golden Goblin Press in 2017 as a companion work to their Cthulhu Invictus line of Call of Cthulhu supplements. Edited by Brian M. Sammons and Oscar Rios , it has only been issued in digital formats. Overview Contents " What the Moonlight Brought " by Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. " The Eye of Cybele " by Peter Rawlik " Turning the Tide " by Tom Lynch " The Sybil at Cumae " by Penelope Love " Poisoned Gifts " by Konstantine Paradias " Outposts " by William Meikle " A Special Day " by Oscar Rios " The Apotheosis of Osirantinous " by Edward M. Erdelac " The Eighth Hill " by Christine Morgan " The Doom that came to Suetonius Colonia " by Lee Clark Zumpe Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
