  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#John_C._Adams">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonFictionAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>John C. Adams</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author https://www.johncadamsreviews.com/ is an author who has written a handful of works around the expanded Cthulhu Mythos begun with the works of H. P. Lovecraft . These have been published in anthologies such as Swords Against Cthulhu II: Hyperborean Nights (2017, Rogue Planet Press ) and zines including Lovecraftiana . Selected Works Short Fiction " Annals of the South Part Two " (2017) Non-Fiction "Review: The Children of Gla'aki" (2020) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.johncadamsreviews.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Zealia_Brown">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Zealia Brown</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1968</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lovecraft’s revision client. Lovecraft ghostwrote “The Curse of Yig” (1928), “The Mound” (1929–1930), and “Medusa’s Coil” (1930) for her based on her slim plot synopses.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1897</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cat">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonSapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cat</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cats are often featured in the cthulhu mythos and play a prominent role in the writings of h. p. lovecraft . The cats of the dreamlands are a noble race, friendly towards humans, and inimical towards the zoogs and the alien cats from saturn . Lovecraft also wrote poems to cats, including one to his friend and correspondent frank belknap long .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Repairer of Reputations A Shop in Go-by Street The Cats of Ulthar The Rats in the Walls The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath The Case of Charles Dexter Ward Cassius Demons of Cthulhu Passing of a Dreamer The Horror on the Beach The Thing from the Blasted Heath Dylath-Leen</ex:hasAppearanceC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Salem_Horror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Salem Horror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The spirit of dark priestess abigail prinn, executed during the salem witch trials, is awakened when a man moves into her old home . Abigail attempts to summon forth a dark evil using the witch room, but is ultimately thwarted by occultist michael leigh . Historywas first published in the may 1937 edition of pulp horror magazine weird tales .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Kuttner"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 1937</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_S._Pointer">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>David S. Pointer</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Poet United States United States  is an American author and poet who has written a handful of pieces inspired by the works of Howard Phillips Lovecraft and the Cthulhu Mythos . These have appeared in anthologies such as Swords Against Cthulhu (2015, Rogue Planet Press ) and Lovecraft after Dark (2015, James Ward Kirk Publishing). Selected Works Poetry " Edler's Erotic Corps " (2015) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>United States</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Poet</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Black_Rite_of_Yaddith">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Black Rite of Yaddith</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. English Genre(s) Fantasy Nightscapes date April 1998 " " is a short poem by American-born Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. Synopsis The poem is presented as an account by the sorcerer Eibon of the creatures of Yaddith 's supplication to dark gods during the dying days of their civilisation. History "" was first published in Nightscapes in April 1998, and was later included in the Robert M. Price -edited anthology The Book of Eibon in 2002. Trivia Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. dedicated "" to Lin Carter .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Joseph S. Pulver. Sr.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nightscapes"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>April 1998</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sex_and_the_Cthulhu_Mythos_%28book%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sex and the Cthulhu Mythos (book)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sex and the cthulhu mythos is a non-fiction book by bobby derie . It looks at the role of sexuality and gender in the life and work of h.p. Lovecraft, and in the cthulhu mythos that he inspired . Derie discusses a number of writers in the mythos tradition whose work has dealt with sexual themes to a greater or lesser extent .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Bobby_Derie"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Literary Criticism</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>314</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2014</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
