  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Bone%E2%80%99s_Prayer">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CaitlinRKiernanWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Bone’s Prayer</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the bone's prayer" is a short story by caitlin r. kiernan . It first appeared in the february 2009 issue of kiernan's ezine sirenia digest . The story is about a writer whose life is upended by the discovery of a small carved stone .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caitlin_R._Kiernan"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sirenia_Digest"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2009</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#White_Rabbit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>White Rabbit</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Powers and Abilities Telepathy Camouflage (normal rabbit) Ageless (Wonderland) Regeneration (Wonderland) Servant of the Jabberwocky Rabbit First appearance Alice's Adventures in Wonderland 1st ( ADJ ): Grimm Fairy Tales: Return to Wonderland Vol 1 0 Created by Lewis Carroll The was created by Lewis Carroll in 1865, first appearing in Alice's Adventures in Wonderland . In 2008, it first appeared in Zenescope Entertainment's Grimm Fairy Tales fictional universe, in the issue #0 of the 1st volume of Grimm Fairy Tales: Return to Wonderland . Background The is a rabbit that was purchased by the scientist Henry Allen in 1860, the first test subject he used in his experiments with the portal to Wonderland . Forced through the portal, it ended up in Wonderland where it was transformed by the Jabberwocky into a creature of madness and corruption. Which lured Calie Liddle into Wonderland, after which the rabbit returned to Alice Liddle whom he slowly drove insane, ending in her suicide.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>1st ( ADJ ): Grimm Fairy Tales: Return to Wonderland Vol 1 0</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Alice's Adventures in Wonderland</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Lewis Carroll</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Black_Ships_Seen_South_of_Heaven">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CaitlinRKiernanWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Black Ships Seen South of Heaven</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story is set in chicago after a lovecraftian apocalypse . Main character, susannah, is an officer in the paramilitary guard, but is secretly an agent of the black pharaoh .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caitlin_R._Kiernan"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Black_Wings_IV"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2015 February 1</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Freddy_vs._Jason_vs._Ash:_The_Nightmare_Warriors">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Freddy vs. Jason vs. Ash: The Nightmare Warriors</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jeff Katz, James Kuhoric Jason Craig English Dynamite Entertainment, Wildstorm Productions Release Date Aug 2009 - Dec 2009 Media Type Comic book is a 6-issue mini-series published by Dynamite Entertainment and written by Jeff Katz and James Kuhoric. It was published between August and December 2009. Synopsis The United States government resurrects Freddy Krueger and Jason Voorhees in an attempt to use their supernatural powers and are unable to control them. Freddy and Jason attempt to take over the world via the Necronomicon Ex-Mortis , resulting in a showdown between the three in Washington DC.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>James Kuhoric</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Jeff Katz</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>Aug 2009 - Dec 2009</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Encyclopedia_Cthulhiana/Contents_T-Z">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
