    <rdfs:label>The Encyclopedia Cthulhiana/Contents T-Z</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>This page lists the contents from a-g of the chaosium reference book the encyclopedia cthulhiana by daniel harms . It contains the text from the book the encyclopedia cthulhiana by daniel harms .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Curse_of_Nineveh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Curse of Nineveh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Call of Cthulhu (Role-Playing Game) ( Cthulhu Britannica ) Genre(s) Roleplaying game Cubicle 7 Entertainment Release Date May 2015 224 is a scenario sourcebook released by Cubicle 7 Entertainment as part of their Cthulhu Britannica line of supplements for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Running to a total of 224 in a hardcover format, it was published in May 2015; it is currently out of print. Overview External Links at RPGGeek at RPG.net Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
