  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sergio_Palumbo">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sergio Palumbo</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Italian is an italian author who has written a number of lovecraftian stories . Is the co-editor (with michele dutcher) of steampunk anthology steam-powered dream engines (2018) and the science fiction collection xenobiology: stranger creatures (2020) he also designs and builds sci-fi dioramas . Credits horror writers stephen king and and edgar allan poe as inspirations .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>Italian</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft._Pantheon_and_Bestiary">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>H. P. Lovecraft. Pantheon and Bestiary</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a Russian illustrated encyclopedic bestiary released in 2019. Description from the official site This is the first attempt of Russian-speaking researchers to generalize and present to the readers' judgment information about deities, races and creatures, born of the prolific fantasy of Howard Phillips Lovecraft and his investigators such as Brian Lumley , Robert E. Howard , August Derleth , and other writers, editors, artists and Lovecraft specialists took part in the work on the book, which made it possible to make this work is as accurate, accurate and close as the letter and spirit literary primary sources. The edition is a richly illustrated guide to Lovecraft's pantheon and bestiary, indicating we have titles, names, works and authors, and it will be interesting and useful for everyone who is seriously interested in the life of Cthulhu and dares to dive into the depths of cosmic horror deeper than ever before. Content Old Ones Abhoth Azathoth Bokrug Bugg-Shash Byatis Ghatanothoa Gla'aki Dagon Daoloth Ithaqua Yig Yog-Sothoth Cthugha Cthulhu Nodens Nyarlathotep Rhan-Tegoth Tsathoggua Ubbo-Sathla Umr at-Tawil Hastur Chaugnar Faugn Shub-Niggurath Shudde M'ell Star Races Great Race of Yith Deep One Flying Polyp Man of Leng Mi-Go People of K’n-yan Denizen of Yaddith Elder Thing Being from Yekub Creatures Bhole Byakhee Ghast Hound of Tindalos Gug Ghoul Zoog Moon-beast Night-gaunt Shantak Shoggoth</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Army_of_Darkness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosAdjacentFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Army of Darkness</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sam Raimi Sam Raimi Ivan Raimi Bruce Campbell Embeth Davitz Release date 9 October 1992 Running time 81-88 minutes, depending on cut United States English $11 million Box office $21.5 million is a 1992 comedy horror film from Sam Raimi . It is the final instalment in his original Evil Dead series, with a semi-sequel/reboot taking 21 years to make its appearance. Synopsis Department store clerk Ash Williams once again faces off against the demon contained in the Necronomicon Ex-Mortis , which casts him back in time. In medieval England , he must battle an evil version of himself at the head of the titular army of undead , and keep the Necronomicon from destroying the world. Trivia Although features the Necronomicon Ex-Mortis as a central plot device, it is important to note that this is not intended to be the same book as Lovecraft 's Necronomicon , and is in fact a tome possessed by a malevolent spirit, written in ancient Sumerian, and bound in human skin.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasWriterW>http://example.org/lovecraft#Sam_Raimi Ivan Raimi</ex:hasWriterW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>9 October 1992</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
