  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Josh_Maybrook">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Josh Maybrook</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author New Jersey , USA Lovecraftian  is an American-born poet and occasional author currently living near Edinburgh, Scotland, who has written a handful of Lovecraftian and Cthulhu Mythos works. These have appeared in zines such as Gavin Chappell 's Lovecraftiana and S. T. Joshi 's Spectral Realms ; in 2023, his poem " Summoning the Outer Gods " was nominated by the fanbase to be included in the anthology The Best of Lovecraftiana . Selected Bibliography Poetry " Memory " (2020) "Necronomicon" (2020) " Summoning the Outer Gods " (2023) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA http://example.org/lovecraft#New_Jersey</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#End_Time">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>End Time</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Call of Cthulhu Roleplaying At The World's End Dr. Michael C. LaBossiere United States English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Chaosium Release Date 2003 96 : Call of Cthulhu Roleplaying At The World's End is a supplementary sourcebook for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Overview contains information on the future of mankind, one in which a limited colonisation of the solar system has been undertaken. Included are a potted future history of the human race, descriptions of the new settlements, new skills and occupations, creatures, equipment, and vehicles. Behind the Mythos Running to a total of 96 , was written by Dr. Michael C. LaBossiere . It was published by Chaosium as part of their Monograph range of Call of Cthulhu supplements in 2003, both in softcover and digital download formats.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Dr. Michael C. LaBossiere</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>96</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2003</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Masks_of_Nyarlathotep_Companion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Masks of Nyarlathotep Companion</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various, see list Various, see list English Genre(s) Roleplaying game Chaosium Sixtystone press Yog-Sothoth.com Release Date 2013 is a gaming supplement designed for use with the Call of Cthulhu campaign Masks of Nyarlathotep . Created by the fan community on Yog-Sothoth.com, it nevertheless contains contributions from designers such as Bret Kramer , Chad Bowser , and David Conyers . It was published by Chaosium in conjunction with Sixtystone Press and Yog-Sothoth.com in 2013 . Interestingly, this companion work is in fact longer than the original supplement. Overview Designers Bret Kramer Matthew Pook Dave Sokolowski Anthony Warren Sam Zeitlin Chad Bowser Jean-Philipe Chapleau Don Coatar David Conyers Mike Czaplinski Z. N. Dillon Hal Eccles Sam Friedman Mathew Gregory James Haughton Pete Mackenzie Paul Maclean James Morton Neil Shaw Scott Slemmons Hans-Christian Vortisch Artists Gennifer Bone David Conyers Adam Crossingham Dennis Detwiller Mathew Gregory David Lee Ingersoll Stephanie McAlea Jon Potter Francisco Javier Rubio Jani Savolainen Eric M. Smith Chris Spatola Gallery References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>see list</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2013</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#High_Priest_Not_to_Be_Described">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>High Priest Not to Be Described</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Elder Hierophant</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Tcho-Tcho Lama of Leng</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The , also known as the tcho-tcho lama of leng, is a minor character in the dream-quest of unknown kadath by h.p. Lovecraft . Little is known about the priest as it is encountered only once in the story .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Celephaïs Fungi from Yuggoth</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Hecate's Fountain</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dream-Quest_of_Unknown_Kadath"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sea-Green_Gown_With_Gold_Buttons">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sea-Green Gown With Gold Buttons</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Short story was published in the collection horrors &amp; abominations: 24 tales of the cthulhu mythos in december 2018 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_McLaughlin"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Michael Sheehan. Jr.</ex:hasAuthorW>
