  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tsathoggua_%28Michael_Shea%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tsathoggua (Michael Shea)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"tsathoggua " is a short story by the late american michael shea . It consists of two storylines whose characters intersect at the beginning and end . The first involves an old woman named maxie trying to eke out an existence . She stumbles across a strange ooze which appears to be contaminating the locals . In the second, another elderly woman is infected by the creatures spawned from the ooze, turning them into one herself .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Shea"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Tales</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The Autopsy</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2008</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Iao_Thamungazoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Iao Thamungazoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>First appearance EXP : The Wizard of Lemuria Created by Lin Carter Iaon-Thamungazoth, Lord of Chaos is a Great Old One worshiped in ancient Lemuria , one of the three primal lords of Lemuria and an aspect of the Triple God of Chaos . References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Wizard_of_Lemuria"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecrafts_Necronomicon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>H. P. Lovecrafts Necronomicon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Bob Eggleton Germany German Festa Release Date April 2018 393 is a German- anthology of Lovecraftian fiction. Running to a total of 393 , it was edited by Frank Festa , features cover art by Bob Eggleton, and was published by Festa in April 2018. In addition to the reprinted fiction, the book also contains four short texts purporting to be from the German translations of the the Necronomicon and the Necronomicon Spellbook . These are credited to Simon, and so are presumably intended to be from the Simon translation. These texts are: "Die Beschwörung des Wächters" ("The Summoning of the Guardian") "Der dritte Name ist MARUTUKKU" ("The third name is MARUTUKKU") "Der vierte Name ist BARASHAKUSHU" ("The fourth name is BARASHAKUSHU") "Die Gräuel" ("The Abominations") Contents Das Necronomicon: Tatsachen über eine Erfindung, introduction by Frank Festa "Der Hund" by H. P. Lovecraft (" The Hound ") "Die Weltraumfresser" by Frank Belknap Long (" The Space-Eaters ") "Meine Frau, der Shoggoth" by Jeffrey Thomas (" I Married a Shoggoth ") "Die Rückkehr des Hexers" by C. A. Smith (" The Return of the Sorcerer ") "Mortellis Bajazzo" by Frank Festa "Stadt ohne Namen" by H. P. Lovecraft (" The Nameless City ") "Der Schrecken von Salem" by Henry Kuttner (" The Salem Horror ") "Der Gott ohne Gesicht" by Robert Bloch (" The Faceless God ") "Der Hüter des Buches" by Henry Hasse (" The Guardian of the Book ") "Das Grauen von der Brücke" by Ramsey Campbell (" The Horror from the Bridge ") "Das Pergament des Entsetzens" by Manly Wade Wellman ("The Terrible Parchment") "Settlers Mauer" by Robert A. W. Lowndes ("Settler's Wall") "Das Fest" by H. P. Lovecraft (" The Festival ") "Die verteufelte Valenz der Elementarteilchen" by Edward Lee ("The Deviltry of Elemental Valence") "Geschichte des Necronomicon" by H. P. Lovecraft (" History of the Necronomicon ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>Germany</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>393</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>German</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>April 2018</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#In_the_Mind_of_H._P._Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>In the Mind of H. P. Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft English Genre(s) Non-fiction Read &amp; Co. Release Date June 2020 156 : A Collection of Essays is a collection of non-fiction works by the late American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Running to a total of 156 , it was published by Read &amp; Co. in June 2020; both paperback and digital editions were released . Overview Contents H. P. Lovecraft (introduction) Supernatural Horror in Literature "Introduction" "The Dawn of the Horror-Tale" "The Early Gothic Novel" "The Apex of Gothic Romance" "The Aftermath of Gothic Fiction" "Spectral Literature on the Continent" "Edgar Allan Poe" "The Weird Tradition in America" "The Weird Tradition in the British Isles" "The Modern Masters" " The Allowable Rhyme " " Metrical Regularity " " The Despised Pastoral " " Notes on Writing Weird Fiction " "I" "II" "III" " Literary Composition " " Cats and Dogs " " At the Root " " The Crime of the Century " Gallery References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Non-fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>156</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2020</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Innsmouth_Escape">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Innsmouth Escape</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Board game is based on h.p. Lovecraft's classic novella the shadow over innsmouth . Designed by darrell hardy, it was published by twilight creations, in 2008 . Game is designed for between two and five players ages 12 and over .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2008</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Alfredo:_A_Tragedy">
