  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ghoth_the_Burrower">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ghoth the Burrower</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Relatives K'baa the Serpent (parent) Little People First appearance HPL : Selected Letters of H. P. Lovecraft 4.617 Created by H. P. Lovecraft is an entity in the Cthulhu Mythos created by the late American author H. P. Lovecraft . Overview According to a fictional family tree provided by Lovecraft, Ghoth is a descendant of Cthulhu and an ancestor of Lovecraft himself. It is referred to as "one of the Little People". It mated with Viburnia , something which Lovecraft described as "a hellish and nameless tragedy". See Also Lovecraft's Family Tree of Azathoth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Selected Letters of H. P. Lovecraft 4.617</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Book_of_Yng">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosBooksFictional"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Book of Yng</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Unknown Arabic English (modern translation) Real World Information Created by Fred C. Adams The is an occult text created by and editor Fred C. Adams for his Translations from the series. Overview The exact origin of the is unknown, but it can be deduced to predate the time of Classical Greece by some margin. The text is stated to have been translated by Fred C. Adams himself whose copy was written in Arabic, although it is unclear if this was an original version or was itself translated from some earlier tongue. The book contains some of the stories which inspired the mythology of Ancient Greece. It must be noted that when translating the text Adams had to employ a degree of guesswork, as acknowledged in the following note: Thus, some of the meaning of the contents may have been either lost or unknowingly twisted to fit a more modern worldview.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasCreatedByA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fred_C._Adams"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stephen_Somers">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Stephen Somers</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Artist Birth Date 1972 Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA United States Horror https://www.artstation.com/stephen_somers (born 1972) is an American freelance digital artist from Milwaukee, USA , who has created several images for Fantasy Flight Games ' Arkham Horror Files line of Mythos -related content. He is currently the Art Director at Fantasy Flight Games . Somers' non-Mythos output includes spin-off media work for properties including Star Wars and Twilight Imperium . See Also Images by External Links at ArtStation at DeviantArt at BoardGameGeek References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Wisconsin Milwaukee</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.artstation.com/stephen_somers</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1972</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
