  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_House_of_the_Temple">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#BrianLumleyWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The House of the Temple</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A man inherits his late uncle's scottish estate, under the condition that he destroy it . He sent the manuscript simultaneously to the english- italian magazine kadath . Both outlets accepted it, and it was later reprinted in his collections .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kadath"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 1980</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>1980</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Court_of_Azathoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dimensions"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Locations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Court of Azathoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a place mentioned in the cthulhu mythos . Sometimes it is called "the final void" the name of the final boss of kirby star allies is translated into spanish as "final void"</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Last_to_Die">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Last to Die</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jason Scott Aiken English Rogue Planet Press Swords Against Cthulhu II: Hyperborean Nights date January 2017 " " is a very short Cthulhu Mythos story by American Jason Scott Aiken . It was published in the Rogue Planet Press anthology Swords Against Cthulhu II: Hyperborean Nights in January 2017. Synopsis A warrior tells the story of how he and his band of raiders mounted an attack on a village in the land of Lomar . They are repulsed by a mysterious and beautiful warrior woman named Nuja who kills them to man. The story inexplicably ends with the man stating that after his death " he next thing I knew, I was sitting here raising a horn of mead and staring at your ugly mugs. "</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jason_Scott_Aiken"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Swords_Against_Cthulhu_II:_Hyperborean_Nights"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>January 2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crouch_End_%28episode%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MediaAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Crouch End (episode)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Crouch end is an episode of nightmares &amp; dreamscapes: from the stories of stephen king . Based on the stephen king short story of the same name . Stars claire forlani and eoin bailey as lonnie and doris .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crouch_End"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>July 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nightmares_Beneath_the_Lonely_Plateau">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nightmares Beneath the Lonely Plateau</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Thomas van den Brink Thomas van den Brink Christina Duijnstee English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Release Date February 2024 33 + extras is a scenario supplement for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game, written by Thomas van den Brink and featuring artwork by van den Brink and Christina Duijnstee. It was published digitally in February 2024 via DriveThruRPG's Miskatonic Repository initiative . Overview References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Thomas van den Brink</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>33 + extras</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>February 2024</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Behind_the_Mask">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Behind the Mask</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>In 1928, the library at miskatonic university receives a collection of rare occult books from the recently deceased amos tuttle . It serves as a direct sequel to august derleth 's short story " the return of hastur " . In the story, tuttle's assistant, bryant hoskins, discovers a copy of the exceedingly rare r'lyeh text . In it, he finds references to the plateau of leng, and</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Phaeton">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Phaeton</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft United States English Arkham House Something About Cats and Other Pieces Date of writing August 1918 date 1949 " " is a poem by the late American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Although it was written in August 1918, it did not see print until its inclusion in the 1949 Arkham House collection Something About Cats and Other Pieces . History Something About Cats and Other Pieces (1949) Collected Poems (1963) The World of H. P. Lovecraft (1971) Fungi from Yuggoth and Other Poems (1971) The Californian: 1934-1938 (1977) The Ancient Track: The Complete Poetical Works of H. P. Lovecraft (2001, 2013) References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Something_About_Cats"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Pieces</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1949</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>August 1918</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Third_Eye">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Third Eye</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jeffrey Thomas English Imelod date July 1997 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by American Jeffrey Thomas . It was first published in the Todd H. C. Fischer -edited fanzine Imelod in July 1997. Synopsis A young boy grows up watching his father, an officer in the Arkham Police Department , slowly lose his mind from the bizarre things he has seen, finally deciding to use any means at his disposal to fight back against the supernatural forces ranged against mankind. However, the mystical texts he reads cause a horrific mutation to begin, and the man ends up taking his own life, As an adult, the boy follows in his father's footsteps, also vowing to fight the minions of the dark gods. However, he has something his father did not: a protective amulet bearing the sign of the gods… History Since it’s first appearance, "" has also appeared in the fanzine Tales of Lovecraftian Horror (1997) and the collection of Thomas's own works Unholy Dimensions (2005).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Imelod"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 1997</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#20,000_Years_Under_the_Sea">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crossovers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>20,000 Years Under the Sea</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The madness of cthulhu: volume two is a short story by kevin j. anderson . It features captain nemo and the submarine from the works of jules verne . The story uses the same backstory for nemo that anderson invented for the novel captain nemo: the fantastic history of a dark genius .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kevin_J._Anderson"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Madness_of_Cthulhu:_Volume_Two"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2015</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Three_Galaxies">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosInspiredWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Three Galaxies</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The are a small cluster of galaxies from the fictional universe of the rifts roleplaying game by palladium . The are crisscrossed by a vast network of ley lines, which are full of magical energy . Dominating the are two intergalactic powers, the democratic consortium of civilized worlds (ccw) and the totalitarian .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
