  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Color_Out_of_Space">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleFilmAndTelevisionAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Color Out of Space</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Based on " The Colour Out of Space " Richard Stanley Daniel Noah Josh C. Waller Elijah Wood Lisa Whalen Richard Stanley Scarlett Amaris Nicolas Cage Joely Richardson Elliot Knight Madeleine Arthur Q'orianka Kilcher Tommy Chong Colin Stetson Steve Annis Brett W. Bachman Production Company SpectreVision RLJE Films Release date January 24, 2020 Running time 111 minutes United States English $6-12 million Box office $1 million is a 2019 film adaptation of H. P. Lovecraft 's story " The Colour Out of Space ," directed by Richard Stanley and Nicholas Cage. Cage plays the character Nathan Gardner, a farmer outside the town of Arkham . A meteorite that crashes into his property produces increasingly bizarre phenomena, deranging and eventually mutating his family.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasWriterW>Richard Stanley Scarlett Amaris</ex:hasWriterW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Colour_Out_of_Space"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2020 January 24</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Recognition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#BrianLumleyWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Recognition</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Aristocrat gathers team of occult specialists to identify and expel a malignant force . When he hears its voice, he calls it "a monstrous presence" and flees . Medium jason lavery produces an "insane cough, whistle, and stutter of harshly alien syllables" another medium makes an "automatic sketch" of an intrusive entity .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Weirdbook 15</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1981</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>January 1977</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Breaking_Point">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Breaking Point</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sam Stone English Genre(s) Horror Dark Regions Press Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror date 2017  " " is a Lovecraftian short story by British Sam Stone . Synopsis In a ruined post-apocalyptic city, a pair of women are forced to submit to the carnal attentions of hybrid Old One monstrosities in order to earn food with which to feed their "children": in actuality the hellish offspring of these couplings. Characters Kerys , a strong-willed survivor of the return of the Old Ones. Mai , Kerys' friend, a woman on the verge of losing her sanity. History "" was included in the Dark Regions Press anthology Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror in 2017.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Sam Stone</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lo%C3%AFc_Muzy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Loïc Muzy</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Artist France French Notable Works EXP : Malleus Monstrorum (2020) is a prolific French artist who has had a hand in a large number of Lovecraftian and Cthulhu Mythos projects. Although perhaps best known in the English-speaking world for his work on roleplaying games in general, and Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu horror roleplaying game in particular, he has also provided both cover art and interior work for several French-language collections of H. P. Lovecraft 's works, as well as for a host of other traditional games. Muzy is currently a Staff Artist at Chaosium . Selected Works Collections Cthulhu: Le mythe (2015) Cthulhu: Le mythe - Livre II (2015) Cthulhu: Le mythe - Livre III (2016) Les contrées du rêve (2018) Cthulhu: Le mythe (2012) Cthulhu: Le mythe - Livre II (2015) Les contrées du rêve (2018) Gaming Supplements Malleus Monstrorum (2020) Malleus Monstrorum (2020) A Time to Harvest (2021) Call of Cthulhu: Arkham (2024, contributor) See Also Images by External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at RPGGeek at BoardGameGeek References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#France</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>French</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isKnownForR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Malleus_Monstrorum"/>
  </rdf:Description>
