  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wayne_Barlowe">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wayne Barlowe</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Wayne Douglas Barlow Connection to the Mythos Artist Author Birth Date 6 January 1958 Glen Cove, New York , USA United States https://waynebarlowe.com/ Wayne Douglas Barlowe (born January 6, 1958) is an American science fiction and fantasy illustrator, film concept designer, and author; probably most well-known for his book Expedition: Being an Account in Words and Artwork of the 2358 A.D. Voyage to Darwin IV (1990); which was later made into the documentary Alien Planet (2005). Barlowe illustrated and wrote about the Elder Things in Barlowe's Guide to Extraterrestrials (1979), and the Gugs in Barlowe's Guide to Fantasy (1996). He also designed the Lovecraft -inspired Ogdru Jahad for Guillermo del Toro's Hellboy (2004). External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>New York USA Glen Cove</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Wayne Douglas Barlow</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://waynebarlowe.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>6 January 1958</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#EOD_%28fanzine%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>EOD (fanzine)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Eod was a sporadically-released australian horror fanzine which ran for nine issues between march 1991 and january 1994 . It sprang from a canberra-based horror zine titled the esoteric order of dagon . In 1990, discovering that this publication was about to fold, masters contacted its publisher, david tansey, and made arrangements to continue releasing it under the name eod .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Yith_Cycle">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Yith Cycle</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Robert M. Price , ed. Cover Artist Steven Gilberts English Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos Chaosium Release Date November 2010 507 : Lovecraftian Tales of the Great Race and Time Travel is an anthology of writings related to H. P. Lovecraft 's The Shadow Out of Time , including stories that inspired and were in turn inspired by it. Edited by Robert M. Price , it was published by Chaosium in 2010, part of the Call of Cthulhu Fiction series. Contents "Emanations from Yith" introduction by Robert M. Price The Purple Sapphire by John Taine (1924) "The Dreams of Yid" (poem) by Duane W. Rimel (1934) "Dreams of Yith" (poem) by Duane W. Rimel (1934) "The Jewels of Charlotte" by Duane W. Rimel (1935) " The Sealed Casket " by Richard F. Searight (1935) " The Warder of Knowledge " by Richard F. Searight (1992) The Shadow Out of Time by H. P. Lovecraft (1936) " The Challenge from Beyond " by Robert E. Howard , Frank Belknap Long , H. P. Lovecraft, A. Merritt and C. L. Moore (1935) "The Shadow Out of Space" by August W. Derleth (1957) " The Dark Brotherhood " by August W. Derleth (1966) "The Shadow from Yith" by Alan D. Gullette (1973) "The Horror from Yith" by Walter C. DeBill, Jr. (1974) "Beneath the Dunes" by Ted C. Pons (1975) "The Changeling" by Walter C. DeBill, Jr. (2002) "The Sands of Time" by P. Schuyler Miller (1937) "Countdown for Kalara" by Richard L. Tierney (1980) "The Winds of Yith" by W. H. Pugmire (1987)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>ed.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>507</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>November 2010</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
