  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shadows_of_an_Inner_Darkness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shadows of an Inner Darkness</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Golden Goblin Press Release Date 2019 is an anthology of Lovecraftian fiction edited by Brian Sammons . It was published by Golden Goblin Press in 2019; both paperback and digital editions were released. Overview Contents " The Parkland Experiments " by William Meikle "Carrion Crows" by Peter Rawlik "By Unknown Hands" by Edward M. Erdelac "A Ghastly Industry" by Lee Clark Zumpe "The Last Appointment" by Oscar Rios "Man of the House" by Christine Morgan "Heart Mountain" by Glynn Owen Barrass</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2019</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Journey_to_Unknown_Kadath_%28Call_of_Cthulhu_LCG%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Journey to Unknown Kadath (Call of Cthulhu LCG)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Journey to Unknown Kadath Fantasy Flight Games Publication Date 2008 Living Card Game Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game Journey to Unknown Kadath is an expansion pack for Fantasy Flight Games ' Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game . Overview The sixth and final Asylum Pack in the Dreamlands Cycle series of expansions, Journey to Unknown Kadath contains a total of 60 cards in the standard distribution of three sets of 20 unique cards. First released in 2008, it later received a revival through Fantasy Flights' in-house print-on-demand service, but was discontinued in 2015 with the demise of Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game . Contents Agency Bodyguard (Character; The Agency) The White Ship , Smooth and Silent (Support; The Agency) Twila Katherine Price, Queen of Unknown- Kadath (Character; Miskatonic University ) Dreaming of the Past (Support; Miskatonic University) Gregory Gry, Shadow of his Former Self (Character; Syndicate) Raking the Pot (Event; Syndicate) Mnomquah 's Serpent (Event; Cthulhu ) Mnomquah, The Moon God (Character; Cthulhu) Keeper of Dreams, Mind Breaker (Character; Hastur ) Magah Bird (Character; Hastur) Gug Sentinel (Character; Yog-Sothoth ) The Tower of Koth , Passage to the Underworld (Support; Yog-Sothoth) Dhole Ant-Lion (Character; Shub-Niggurath ) Dark Contagion (Support; Shub-Niggurath) Stealthy Zoog (Character; Neutral) The Cats of Ulthar (Character; Neutral) Nyarlathotep , The Black Pharaoh (Character; Neutral) The Light Side of the Moon (Event; Neutral) The Dark Side of the Moon (Event; Neutral) Unknown Kadath, Home of the Other Gods (Support; Neutral)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2008</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Terrors_From_Beyond">
