    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Recurring Nightmares</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Kara Centell-Dunk Nikki Valens Fantasy Flight Games Publication Date 2013, 2016 Mansions of Madness is an expansion pack for Fantasy Flight Games ' Mansions of Madness Cthulhu Mythos board game. Designed by Kara Centell-Dunk and Nikki Valens , it was first published in 2013 and re-issued in 2016. Overview</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2016 2013</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Slime_Girls">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Slime Girls</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Story is dedicated to real-life spice girl melanie chisholm, better known as mel c.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#James_Ambuehl"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Short Fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1998</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tatterman">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tatterman</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>First appearance ADJ : Pathfinder Adventure Path #109 Strange Aeons Created by Wesley Schneider The is a character which was created by Paizo Inc in 2016 for the Pathfinder roleplaying game. Background The is an entity who serves Hastur , operating for centuries in both Golarion and the Dimension of Dreams. It's a sorcerous predator who infiltrates sleeping minds, hunting and killing the dreaming mortals. At one time it was one of many beings that was worshipped by the Kellids.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Pathfinder Adventure Path #109 Strange Aeons</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Wesley Schneider</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecrafts_Iraq">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lovecraft's Iraq</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"followed by lovecraft in lockup" is a military fiction novel by american and former recon marine david rose . The book was released in paperback and digitally through amazon's kindle platform; the digital edition has since been removed from their library . The book was followed by a short story sequel, "lovecraft in lockup," which was included in the 2023 collection monsters in the bush .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_Rose"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Military fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>177</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>March 2022</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Victor_E._Bacon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Victor E. Bacon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1997</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Amateur journalist and editor of Bacon’s Essays, which published work by Lovecraft and Clark Ashton Smith, and Official Editor of the United Amateur Press Association (1925–1926).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1905</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Professor_Peabodys_Last_Lecture">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Professor Peabody's Last Lecture</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The sketch was written by series producer jack laird, directed by jerrold freedman, and stars carl reiner as the titular ill-starred academic . It is the final segment of the eighth episode of season 2 of rod serling's anthology show night gallery .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasWriterW>Jack Laird</ex:hasWriterW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1971 November 10</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Abigail_Prinn">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Abigail Prinn</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Abigail Abbie Prinn</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as abigail "abbie" prinn salem , massachusetts public unknown high priestess of nyogtha human first appearance circle : " the salem horror " created by henry kuttner and part of the cthulhu mythos inspired by the works of h. p. lovecraft .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Salem_Horror"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Kuttner"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lurker_in_Tunnel_13">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Lurker in Tunnel 13</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Swamp thing was on the run from batman when he encountered an old man who was being attacked by a grizzly bear in a cave . Not wanting to leave him in the cave, swamp thing carried the ezekiel's body in hopes of giving him a proper burial and notifying his family . After arriving in perdition, some of the locals mistook swamp thing for murdering ezekiel and attacked him until his son jason pointed out that it could not be the</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Len Wein</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>February 1974</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Rovagug">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Rovagug</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The rough beast is a monster in the fictional universe of the pathfinder pencil-and-paper roleplaying game by paizo inc. it is worshiped as the god of destruction on the world of golarion . Despite his imprisonment, he is restless and stirrings are increasing .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
