  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wade_Kearney">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wade Kearney</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Kearney is a fictional character created by american author ron shiflet for his cthulhu mythos stories . He made his debut appearance in the short story " unfinished business " in july 2006 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Unfinished_Business"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#D%C3%A4monen_bei_Tag">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RamseyCampbellWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dämonen bei Tag</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"demons by daylight" is an anthology of horror fiction by acclaimed british author ramsey campbell . It is a german- translation of his first published work, "demons by daylight . It was released by edition metzengerstein in a paperback format in october 1998 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ramsey_Campbell"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>Germany</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>250</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>German</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>October 1998</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Llunwy_of_Wales">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Llunwy of Wales</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>is a member of the Family tree of Azathoth who is an ancestor to both Owen Gwynedd and H. P. Lovecraft . ( HPL : Selected Letters 4.617) Behind the Mythos Lovecraft thought himself to be a "pure" anglo-saxon but he later discovered he had a Welsh ancestor in his genealogy. ( HPL : Selected Letters 2.302)</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Intelligent_Mollusk">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtinctSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdfs:label>Intelligent Mollusk</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sociocultural Characteristics Venus Real World Information First appearance EXP : The Transition of Titus Crow Created by Brian Lumley Intelligent mollusks are a telepathic race of creatures which inhabit the seas of Venus in the distant future. They are mentioned in Brian Lumley 's Cthulhu Mythos novel The Transition of Titus Crow . In the same book Titus Crow further states that ten million years later all life on Venus has died but it is unclear if the mollusks still survive elsewhere.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Transition_of_Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Keeper_of_the_Yellow_Sign">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Keeper of the Yellow Sign</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The keepers of the yellow sign are cultists who've sacrificed their souls to hastur . They are attracted to art, usually creations that are decadent and/or weird . They are able to pass off as humans though they have a disturbing aura .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Thrushmoor Terror</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>James Jacob</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Michelle Jones</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Tito Leati</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Xura">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalLocations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Xura</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Land of Pleasures Unattained</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dreamlands Also known as "Land of Pleasures Unattained" First appearance HPL : " The White Ship " Created by H.P. Lovecraft is a coastal region in the Dreamlands of Earth , also known as the "Land of Pleasures Unattained." Description From the sea the lily-lined coastline appears idyllic, with beautiful groves as far as the eye can see from which harmonic singing and snatches of laughter can be heard. However getting closer the wind carries the lethal, charnel odor of plague-stricken towns and uncovered cemeteries.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dreamlands"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_White_Ship"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Amanda_Sharpe">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Amanda Sharpe</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_University"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Student</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The student is a character created by fantasy flight games for their arkham horror cthulhu mythos setting . She is a human / deep one hybrid, although it's possible to stop her transformation in arkham horror second edition . Amanda is a 2-year student at miskatonic university during the late 1920s .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Horror_Second_Edition_Core_Set"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fantasy_Flight_Games"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#We_Are_Not_These_Bodies,_Strung_Between_the_Stars">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>We Are Not These Bodies, Strung Between the Stars</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A. c. wise english 01publishing whispers from the abyss vol. 2: the horrors that are &amp; shall be is a short story . It was first published in the kat rocha -edited anthology whispers from the abyss vol. 2 by 01publishing in october 2015 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#A._C._Wise"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Shall Be</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2015</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Astrophobos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Astrophobos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The united amateur date january 1918 is a poem by h. p. lovecraft . It has since seen inclusion in a number of collections, particularly those focusing on poetry .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_United_Amateur"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>January 1918</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Star-Seed">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Star-Seed</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Royceton university professor with an interest in the occult investigates an abandoned mansion in the woodlands near his hometown . He comes across a decaying library of dark knowledge, and a basement-dwelling plant-creature which he narrowly escapes . Using the protection of the elder sign and an incantation to summon yaggdytha, he is successful in ridding the planet of the being . Later comes to realise that it was not ei'lor itself</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#James_Ambuehl"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Cthulhu Codex #7</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 1996</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_House_Press">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SmallPress"/>
    <rdfs:label>Weird House Press</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Current Status Active Joe Morey https://www.weirdhousepress.com/ is a specialty publisher focused on literary horror, dark fantasy, and poetry. It was founded by Joe Morey , formerly editor and publisher of Dark Regions Press and Dark Renaissance Books. Selected Books Novels Dead Sea by Tim Curran The Red Stone of Jubbah by Donald Tyson The Revenant of Rebecca Pascal by David Barker and W. H. Pugmire Collections Her Wan Embrace by David Barker Mountain of Shadows and Other Tales of Alhazred by Donald Tyson Return to Isle of the Dead and Other Tales of Alhazred by Donald Tyson Something in the Water and Other Stories by Douglas Wynne The Brain Leeches and Other Eldritch Phenomena by Tim Curran The Howling Terror and Other Lovecraftian Horror Stories by Tony Richards (2022) The Skinless Face by Donald Tyson</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.weirdhousepress.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyghan_Grii">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ny'ghan Grii</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Invaders"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Dweller in the Hidden World</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Enemy</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Hidden Ones</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>In 1994, chaosium incorporated them into the role-playing game call of cthulhu . They are an extra-dimensional race of luminous spherical creatures with glossy ivory-yellow semi-translucent vine-like appendages ending in raw looking stumps covered in cilia .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Invaders"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Kuttner"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wendell_Willis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wendell Willis</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tcho-Tcho_people"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Willis is the last scion of a wealthy family with a sprawling estate outside of tenoka , texas . He was driven mad by the tribe of tcho-tcho people who took him in . After feeding human flesh to his horrified friend robert ballard, he fled to the shack of another of his old friends who happened to be a priest in service to the great old one yig . Fell foul of a trap laid by the wily cult</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Seven Serpents Waiting A God's Eye View</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#When_in_Leng..."/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Commentaries">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Commentaries</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various United States English Genre(s) Non-fiction SSR Publications Release Date August 1955 37 is a collection of non-fiction pieces centred on the works of Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Overview Edited by and Lovecraft scholar George T. Wetzel , contains five individual works and runs to a total of 37 . It was published by SSR Publications in August 1955, in a limited run of 75 numbered copies. is essentially a truncated version of Howard Phillips Lovecraft: Memoirs, Critiques &amp; Bibliographies which was published earlier the same year. Contents " Idiosyncracies of HPL " by E. A. Adkins " A Few Memories " by James F. Morton " Ave Atque Vale " by Edward H. Cole " The Cthulhu Mythos: A Study " by George Wetzel " The Lord of R'yleh " by Matthew H. Onderdonk</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Non-fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>37</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 1955</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Great_Old_Ones_%28Call_of_Cthulhu_supplement%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Great Old Ones (Call of Cthulhu supplement)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The great old ones: new adventures against the cthulhu mythos is a campaign supplement book for chaosium's horror roleplaying game call of cthulhu . The book's included adventures can either be played as stand-alone missions, or in sequence to form a loose campaign .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>176</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1989</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
