    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Eligos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Eligos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Demon is a minor demonic entity summoned by the necronomicon . Can control and manipulate individual's minds, can teleport short distances, and has telekinetic abilities . One such demon was summoned by ash to find out how to undo what the necronomicon had wrought .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Books from Beyond ( Ash vs. Evil Dead</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Episode 3)</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Season 1</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Sean Clements</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lurking_Fear_%28film%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleFilmAndTelevisionAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lurking Fear (film)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lurking fear is a low- horror film from c. courtney joyner . It is very loosely based on the h. p. lovecraft short story of the same name . Horror movie icon jeffrey combs is one of the lead actors in the film .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lurking_Fear"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>27 July 1994</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#ClarkAshtonSmithWorks">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Procyon_Project">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Procyon Project</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A guard at a weapons research facility during the second world war witnesses a tear in reality and the creatures which make their way through . Scientists explore the possibility of weaponising ancient grimoires such as the necronomicon and de vermis mysteriis . Characters finn , a former marine invalided out of the service and now working as a security guard at the facility .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tim_Curran"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#World_War_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>August 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecraftiana_Vol_1,_Issue_4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Periodicals"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lovecraftiana Vol 1, Issue 4</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Justell Vonk Maria Mitchell Emily Stepp Cover Artist Zuccarello English Rogue Planet Press Release Date January 2017 52  Lovecraftiana Vol 1, Issue 1 is an issue of the periodical Lovecraftiana , edited by Gavin Chappell and published by Rogue Planet Press in January 2017. Contents "Sub Niggurath Blues" by Thomas Idoine "The Offering" by Nigel Robert Felton "Many Miles Away" by B. Michael Stevens "The Reverend Dies" by John C Adams "Wolfé" by Franklyn Searight "The Oval Window" by Josef Desade "The Last Daughter of Leng" by Maria Mitchell</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>52</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>January 2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Abyss">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Abyss</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A group of university friends dabbling in the occult unwittingly summon a being of great power which offers one of their number to its masters . Dureen , a creature known as a seeker, sent forth by its masters the adumbrali to fetch them fresh playthings .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_A._W._Lowndes"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Stirring Science Stories</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 1941</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu_Hallowmas_1985">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Crypt of Cthulhu Hallowmas 1985</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist John Borkowski United States English Crypt of Cthulhu Cryptic Publications Release Date November 1985 64 is the 35th issue of long-running fanzine Crypt of Cthulhu . Running to a total of 64 , it was edited by Robert M. Price , featured cover art by John Borkowski, and was published by Cryptic Publications in November 1985 in an A5 format . Contents Editorial Shards by Robert M. Price "H. P. Lovecraft and the Cthulhu Mythos" by Robert M. Price "CAS to AWD" by Clark Ashton Smith "The Question of Shub-Niggurath" by Rodolfo A. Ferraresi "Narrathoth, the Forgotten" by Will Murray "What Was the Sussex Manuscript?" by Edward P. Berglund "Lovecraft on Eldritch Tomes" by Edward P. Berglund "The Cthulhu Mythology" by Francis T. Laney "The Fan Mythos: A Survey of the Cthulhu Mythos in the Small Press" by Randall D. Larson Reviews by Stefan Dziemianowicz and Will Murray Letters by Robert Bloch , Daniel Gobbett, Chris Gross, Kevin S. Hall, Richard L. Tierney , David F. Godwin, William Fulwiler, Laurence C. Bush, and Darwin Ortiz References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>64</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>November 1985</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Horrors_%26_Abominations:_24_Tales_of_the_Cthulhu_Mythos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Horrors &amp; Abominations: 24 Tales of the Cthulhu Mythos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mark McLaughlin Michael Sheehan, Jr. English Release Date December 2018 248 (print editions) 311 (digital edition) is a collection of stories by authors Mark McLaughlin and Michael Sheehan, Jr. , first published in 2018. Overview Consisting entirely of material reprinted from earlier collections, Horrors &amp; Abominations runs to a total of 248 (311 as an ebook) and was released in paperback (December 2018), hardcover (December 2021) and digital (December 2021) editions. It is divided into four thematic sections. Contents Aquatic Horrors " Coins From Y'ha-nthlei " " The Power of Azalareon " " That Tantalizing Taste You Will Never Forget " " Toadface " " The Sea-Spider " " The Lurker From the Kelp Forest " " The Testament of Cthulhu " " The Horror in the Water Tower " Nightmares From Carcosa " Glove: A Tale of The King In Yellow " " The Gateway to Carcosa " " Casino Carcosa " " Sea-Green Gown With Gold Buttons " Urban Monstrosities " The Curse of the Tillinghasts " " The Nightmare in Delapore Tower " " The Creature in the Waxworks " " The Thing From Beyond the Living Door " Egyptian Abominations " The Abominations of Nephren-Ka " " The Colossus in the Catacombs " " The Blasphemy in the Canopic Jar " " This Pulsing Mass That Serves as My Heart " " The Final Door " " Mrs. Dakhamunzu " " The Relic in the Egyptian Gallery " " Deathless Bride of the Crawling Chaos "</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_McLaughlin"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Michael Sheehan. Jr.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>248 311</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 2018</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Solar_Pons_and_the_Cthulhu_Mythos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Pastiches"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Solar Pons and the Cthulhu Mythos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Eric von Konnenberg Pierre de Hammais English The Solar Pons Gazette date December 2013 is a monograph written by Eric von Konnenberg and Pierre de Hammais. Overview The text focuses on the connections between August Derleth 's fictional detective Solar Pons and the expanded Cthulhu Mythos . As Derleth's detective is a pastiche of Sherlock Holmes, the monograph itself is a mock scholarly article much like those written concerning the Sherlock Holmes 'canon', albeit referencing actual details provided by Derleth in various Solar Pons writings. History The article appeared in the Solar Pons Gazette in December 2013.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Eric von Konnenberg</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Pierre de Hammais</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The Solar Pons Gazette</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>December 2013</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nightscapes_September_1997">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nightscapes September 1997</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Edward P. Berglund Release Date September 1997 Preceded by August 1997 Followed by October 1997 is the third issue of long-running online fanzine Nightscapes . It was edited by the late American and Lovecraft scholar Edward P. Berglund . Contents Fiction " Eibon Saith: The Apophthegmata of Eibon " by Robert M. Price " Tentacles " by Peter F. Guenther "The Last Laugh" by Ron Shiflet (later removed by 's request) " An Incarceration in Bh'Yhlun " by Ian Davey " Foundling " by Tim Waggoner "The Lords of Pain" by Richard L. Tierney Parodies " Finding God(s) " by James Ambuehl "Oh, Bury Me Not in Y'ha-nthlei" by Peter A. Worthy Poetry " Folks of Innsmouth: Golf Pro " by Franklyn Searight " The Folks One Meets In Innsmouth " by Ron Shiflet " Cthulhu Lies Dreaming " by Ron Shiflet " Dark Dreamer " by Chad Hensley " Music of Mi-Go " by Chad Hensley " In Ulthar " by Alan Peschke Reviews By James Ambuehl External Links full issue online at the Nightscapes website</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 1997</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dare">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
