  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Question_of_Blood">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Question of Blood</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Historywas released in the 2016 anthology black wings v: new tales of lovecraftian horror by ps publishing . One of the scientists involved in the development of the fertility treatment was stated to be herbert west .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_Hambling"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Black_Wings_V"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 2016</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatar">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CharactersIncorporatedFromFolkloreMythAndReligion"/>
    <rdfs:label>Avatar</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>An is a deliberate descent of a deity to earth, or a descent of the supreme being (e.g., vaishnavites) within the cthulhu mythos, an generally holds the same meaning . An is exponentially weaker but requires a considerable effort of will on the part of its deity to manifest .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Tales_August_2009">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Periodicals"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Arkham Tales August 2009</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Jeff Ward English Cold Fusion Media Empire Release Date August 2009 100 Preceded by Arkham Tales May 2009 Followed by Arkham Tales November 2009 was the fourth issue of Arkham Tales: A Magazine of Weird Fiction , a short-lived quarterly magazine edited by Nathan Shumate . It featured cover art by Jeff Ward. Contents Editorial: Keel and Lovecraft by Nathan Shumate "Haunt Squad" by Maurissa Guibord "A Tale of Two Wizards" by Larry Hodges "Adrift with a Bone Die" by Michael Anthony "In the Shadow of Uluru" by Paula R. Stiles "Lunchbox" by Alex Sivier "The Last Watcher" by Lee Pletzers "Signs and Hortense" by Fraser Sherman "Contributor Notes</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>100</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 2009</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cold_Harvest">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
