    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Selected Essays Volume I</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft United States English SSR Publications Release Date December 1952 26 is a collection of one short story and three non-fiction works by the late American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Running to only 26 , it was edited by early Lovecraft scholar George T. Wetzel and published by SSR Publications in December 1952 . Contents " Poetry and the Gods ", with Anna Helen Crofts " Idealism and Materialism—A Reflection " " A Confession of Unfaith " " Nietzscheism and Realism " External Links online at the Internet Archive References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>26</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 1952</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Reliquary">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Reliquary</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>C. P. Webster English Genre(s) Weird fiction Lovecraftiana Vol 5, Issue 1 date 2020 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by C. P. Webster. Synopsis The story begins with a letter from a Miskatonic University scholar introducing the of the second part: a French occultist with a gift for photography who was found dead of extreme fear in the early part of the 20th century. The journal entries which follow detail the man's experiments in photographing a medium, his discovery that some bizarre entity haunts the woman, and that it may in fact be coming for him. History "" was published in Vol 5, Issue 1 of the Lovecraftiana zine in 2020. Trivia The in which the entity speaks is clearly intended to be R'lyehian .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>C. P. Webster</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 1</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Eldritch_Skies">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Eldritch Skies</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The game is set in an alternate earth where human history diverged in the mid 20th century . Use of hyperspatial technology and traveling via hyperspace is risky to lifeforms as hyperspatial energies will mutate you . In the background is the ever present threat of a vampiric race of world destroyers, led by cthulhu .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Stephane Gesbert</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Role-play</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Sci-Fi</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Savage Worlds</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
  </rdf:Description>
