    <rdfs:label>Utatti Asfet</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Owen Guthrie Toivo Luick Earl Geier M. Wayne Miller United States English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Chaosium Release Date 1996 156 : The Eye of Wicked Sight is a contemporary globe-trotting scenario supplement for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Written by Owen Guthrie and Toivo Luick and featuring artwork from Earl Geier and M. Wayne Miller (credited on the cover as R. Wayne Miller), it runs to a total of 156 in a paperback format and was published in 1996 . Overview Gallery References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Owen Guthrie</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Toivo Luick</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>156</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1996</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#New_Orleans">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>New Orleans</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Louisiana features prominently in lovecraft's " the call of cthulhu " as a center of cthulhu cult activity . The city and state feature as a setting in lovecraft's fiction, and in other tales of the cthulhu mythos . The city is notable for its french heritage and for its vibrant creole culture .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Call of Cthulhu Through the Gates of the Silver Key</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>City</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Louisiana</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>United States</ex:isLocatedAtL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Family_Tradition">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Family Tradition</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Denny whateley visits frank nardi and relates the story of how his family raised his younger brother, a creature created through an unholy union with a dark god . The story ends with the investigators preparing to put a stop to junior's dark magic . Behind the mythoswas written by edward morris after a request by brian m. sammons for pieces centred around the arkham detective agency .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Edward_Morris"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Detective_Agency"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Satans_Servants">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Satan's Servants</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Something about cats and other pieces is a horror short story by robert bloch . It was written in 1935 and first published in the 1949 arkham house collection . It was the last story written with lovecraft's input to be published .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_Bloch"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Something_About_Cats"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Pieces</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1949</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>1935</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Edward_H_Cole">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Edward H Cole</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1966</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Longtime amateur associate of Lovecraft, living in the Boston area. Editor of the Olympian.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1892</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Atlanta_Radio_Theatre_Company">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#AmateurPress"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ContentCreators"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Atlanta Radio Theatre Company</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Current Status Active 1984 William L. Brown Patrick Stansbury United States Science Fiction Fantasy Horror https://artc.org/ The is a Georgia, US-based acting troupe who focus on the science fiction, horror and fantasy genres. in 1984, the ARTC have both recorded studio adaptations and performed at live venues including NecronomiCon ; they have adapted several of Lovecraft ’s stories into audio dramas in the style of the golden age of radio, and have even written some original Mythos material. Many of these are available as CD and digital download through their . Adaptations At the Mountains of Madness (1992) At the Mountains of Madness (2010) The Call of Cthulhu The Colour Out of Space The Dunwich Horror The Rats in the Walls The Shadow Over Innsmouth Mythos Originals The Dancer in the Dark Special Order</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://artc.org/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dunwich_Dungeon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dunwich Dungeon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The arkham detective is a hardboiled pseudo-noir novella by american and screenwriter byron craft . It was first published independently through the createspace platform in august 2017; both paperback and digital editions were released . Set in prohibition-era america (1920-1933), the story includes a number of historical inaccuracies .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Byron_Craft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>105</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Arkham_Detective"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Howler_on_the_Sales_Floor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Howler on the Sales Floor</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story was originally submitted for inclusion in the 2018 pickman's press anthology corporate cthulhu, but was not accepted . Despite containing no direct references to the works of h.p. Lovecraft, the story clearly implies that nya is in fact the outer god .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Jonathan Ficke</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Humour</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>L. Ron Hubbard Presents Writers of the Future. Volume 34</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>April 2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Jennifer_Morgue">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Jennifer Morgue</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The laundry files is the second full-length novel by author charles stross . It was first published in 2006 by golden gryphon press . The novel is set in 2005, and follows a pair of operatives on a mission to thwart an attempt to raise a soviet sub .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Charles_Stross"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>432</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Laundry_Files"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2006</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#To_Howard_Phillips_Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ClarkAshtonSmithWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>To Howard Phillips Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here Clark Ashton Smith United States English Genre(s) Poetry Weird Tales date July 1937 𝐓 " " is a poem by Clark Ashton Smith , written as a tribute to his friend and contemporary. It was first published in the July 1937 edition of Weird Tales , just a few months after Lovecraft 's death, and mentions several of the most well-known elements of Lovecraft's work, including Kadath , Cthulhu , Ulthar , and Arkham .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Clark_Ashton_Smith"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Poetry</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 1937</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
