  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#In_the_Dark_%28TMNT_Adventures%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crossovers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>In the Dark (TMNT Adventures)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"in the dark" is a story featured in issue #27 of teenage mutant ninja turtles adventures . It is one of two comics in the franchise to have the town of innsmouth as a setting . The "boogey-men" try to force april to drink more of the shake before they are defeated .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Doug Brammer</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 1991</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Elder_Key_%28Sigil%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Elder Key (Sigil)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Elder Key Used by Haon-Dor Protective ward Real World Information Lin Carter First Appearance EXP : " The Descent into the Abyss " The Elder Key is a fictional sigil in the Cthulhu Mythos . It is described as a symbol with piercing radiance that antehuman wizards used to ward off powerful creatures. ( EXP : " The Descent into the Abyss ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeA>Protective ward</ex:hasTypeA>
    <ex:isUsedByA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Haon-Dor"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Descent_into_the_Abyss"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ashes_and_Others_by_H._P._Lovecraft_and_Divers_Hands_Yuletide_1982">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ashes and Others by H. P. Lovecraft and Divers Hands Yuletide 1982</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Robert M. Price United States English Crypt of Cthulhu Miskatonic University Press Release Date December 1982 64 Preceded by Hallowmas 1982 Followed by Candlemas 1983 was the tenth issue of Robert M. Price 's long-running Lovecraftian fanzine Crypt of Cthulhu . Edited by Price, who also supplied the cover art, it ran to a total of 64 in an A5 format, and was published by Miskatonic University Press in December 1982. In his introduction, Price states that " The present collection does not follow the format of an ordinary issue of Crypt of Cthulhu, but it counts as Volume 2, Number 2, in the " . Contents Introduction by Robert M. Price " Ashes " by C. M. Eddy, Jr. and H. P. Lovecraft " The Sealed Casket " by Richard F. Searight "The Sorcery of Aphlar" by H. P. Lovecraft and Duane W. Rimel " Dreams of Yith " by H. P. Lovecraft and Duane W. Rimel "Dreams of Yid" by Duane W. Rimel " The Diary of Alonzo Typer " by William Lumley " The Automatic Executioner " by Adolphe de Castro "A Sacrifice to Science" by Adolphe de Castro "The Lord of Illusion" by E. Hoffmann Price References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>64</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 1982</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
