    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Folklore</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>136 is a background sourcebook produced by cubicle 7 entertainment as part of their cthulhu britannica line of roleplaying game supplements . Written by stuart boon , james desborough and others as part of cubicle 7's cthulhu britannica line of roleplaying game supplements .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#James_Desborough"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stuart_Boon"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>136</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu_Britannica"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2013</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Alone_Against_the_Tide">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Alone Against the Tide</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nicholas Johnson Cover Artist M. Wayne Miller United States English Chaosium Release Date 2020 Media Type Digital CD PDF 86 is a solo-play adventure module released by Chaosium for their Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Overview As with other solo-play scenarios, offers an adventure in the choice-tree style of the Choose Your Own Adventure or Fighting Fantasy books. The adventure involves the player travelling to the quiet lakeside town of Esbury to investigate a series of bizarre events, and allows for custom character creation using the Core Rules, although a pregenerated character, Miskatonic University 's Dr. Woods, is included for quick-start play. Publication Written by Nicholas Johnson with cover art supplied by M. Wayne Miller , was first released in 2020, and is currently only available in a digital format. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Nicholas Johnson</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>86</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2020</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Call_of_Cthulhu:_Prisoner_of_Ice">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Call of Cthulhu: Prisoner of Ice</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Prisoner of ice is a single-player puzzle solving game based on h.p. Lovecraft 's cthulhu mythos . The plot moves to argentina where it ties in with its predecessor game shadow of the comet . The game received a japanese release in 1997, where it was also ported to the sega saturn and playstation .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1995</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Enoch_Bowen">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Enoch Bowen</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Church of Starry Wisdom</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Archaeologist The Church of Starry Wisdom Human First appearance HPL : " The Haunter of the Dark " CIRCLE : " The Shadow from the Steeple " Created by H. P. Lovecraft Professor is a fictional character from H. P. Lovecraft 's 1936 short story " The Haunter of the Dark ", who also appears in Robert Bloch 's " The Shadow from the Steeple " (1950). He is depicted as an archeologist and occultist who finds the Shining Trapezohedron in Egypt and founds the Church of Starry Wisdom in Providence, Rhode Island . Overview In Lovecraft's story, all that is really learned about Bowen comes from the notes of the reporter Edwin M. Lillibridge , who died while researching the Starry Wisdom cult. His notes read: Lovecraft writes that Starry Wisdom was driven from Providence in 1877, but he does not indicate whether Bowen was still leading the cult at that point. Bloch's sequel does not add much to the legend: In the Expanded Mythos Leading Lovecraft scholar Robert M. Price 's short story " The Shining Trapezohedron " elaborates on Bowen's backstory, telling of his journey through the Egyptian desert, his encounter with the Black Pharaoh, and his transformation into a herald of Nyarlathotep .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shadow_from_the_Steeple"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Haunter_of_the_Dark"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#An_Eldritch_Legacy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>An Eldritch Legacy</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Golden Goblin Press Release Date December 2020 200 Preceded by Children of Lovecraft Country : The Cousins Come of Age is a thematic anthology of Cthulhu Mythos fiction. Edited by Brian M. Sammons and Oscar Rios , it was published by Golden Goblin Press in December 2020. Both print and digital versions were released. Overview Contents "Dreams and Nightmares" by Peter Rawlik "Warden of the Dark God" by Glynn Owen Barrass "Separate Lives" by Christine Morgan "A Dark Legacy" by Brian M. Sammons "George Weedon and the Secret of Infinite Horizons" by Lee Clark Zumpe "Blood and the Turning of the Tide" by Oscar Rios Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>200</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 2020</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Topographical_Man">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Topographical Man</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Background is an interstellar humanoid-like entity whose arms span light years and ends with a sun contained within each hand . It gets its energy from the insatiable karanada, which are entities consisting of a single grain of sand that have been imbued with his power . Only the strength of spirit and determination can defeat it, causing it to shrink to its initial size and power .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_M._Jones">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Richard M. Jones</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Scientist Human First appearance HPL : " The Green Meadow " Created by H. P. Lovecraft &amp; Winifred V. Jackson (as Elizabeth Neville Berkeley) is a minor fictional character created by H. P. Lovecraft and Winifred V. Jackson for their short story " The Green Meadow ". Overview Jones was the local scientific authority of Potowonket, Maine and the discoverer of the contents of the metallic rock-like object that fell from the sky on Wednesday, August 27, 1913, at approximately 8:30 PM. He collected and perused the book contained within, and thus set the stage for the meat of the story.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Green_Meadow"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Winifred_V._Jackson"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Belknap_Long">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#KalemClub"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftsCoAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftsCorrespondents"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Frank Belknap Long</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1994 (Aged 92) January 3</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>W. t. long was a prolific writer of horror fiction, fantasy, science fiction, poetry, gothic romance, comic books, and non-fiction . He is best known for his horror and science fiction short stories, including early contributions to the cthulhu mythos . He received the world fantasy award for life achievement and the bram stoker award for lifetime achievement .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>New York http://example.org/lovecraft#New_York_City Harlem Manhattan</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>American</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Leslie Northern Lyda Belknap Long</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Major Contributor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1901 April 27</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Naggoob">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Naggoob</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Father of Ghouls</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Behind the mythos was created by lin carter for his 1976 story " the horror in the gallery ", and classified as one of the lesser old ones . As the "father of ghouls", might be associated with shaurash-ho , a descendant of nug through cthulhu and the ancestor of yogash the ghoul .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_in_the_Gallery"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeremiah_Phillips">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSRelatives"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Jeremiah Phillips</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>29 August 1852</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lovecraft’s maternal great-grandfather.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isRelativeToR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1803</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Primitive_Snouter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonSapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Primitive Snouter</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Archirrhnos haeckelii</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Haeckel's Primitive Snouter</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a mouse-sized forest animal which can balance itself on its snout while feasting on its favorite food: cockroaches . It has been incorporated into the cthulhu mythos by the role-playing game call of cthulhu .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecrafts_Dreamlands"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Snouters</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Gerolf Steiner</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tond">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Planets"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tond</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Planetary Body Yarkdao First appearance EXP : " The Inhabitant of the Lake " EXP : " A Madness from the Vaults " Created by Ramsey Campbell Little is known of other than that it is an extra-terrestrial planet which is the homeworld of the humanoid Yarkdao , and that it orbits the binary stars Yifne and Baalblo . It is one of several planets that the Great Old One Glaaki visited before his arrival on Earth ( EXP : " The Inhabitant of the Lake ", Ramsey Campbell ).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Madness_from_the_Vaults"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Planetary Body</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yarkdao"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Inhabitant_of_the_Lake"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sthanee">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sthanee</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Children_of_Sthanee"/>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Lost One</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as The Lost One Great Old Ones Children of First appearance " Nyaghoggua " (mention) " When Wakes " (first appearance) Created by Robert A. W. Lowndes is a Great Old One created by the late American author Robert A. W. Lowndes . Description Manifesting as a gigantic marine horror with twelve serpentine limbs equipped with suckers similar to those found on an octopus, also has a beard of tentacles. It is served by a vicious race of merfolk known as the Children of who worship it as a god. Behind the Mythos is mentioned in Robert A. W. Lowndes ' short poem " Nyaghoggua " (1941), but its physical appearance was first depicted in the pages of Lowndes' comic book feature " When Wakes " (pp. 32-33) which was published in Scienti-Comics #2.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyaghoggua"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>When Sthanee Wakes</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_A._W._Lowndes"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sinbad_and_the_Great_Old_Ones">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crossovers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sinbad and the Great Old Ones</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sailor sinbad is drawn into a race against time to stop the evil sorcerer . The group pursue their quarry across the known - and unknown - world . Nearly all of his companions and the entirety of his crew meet a grizzly death .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gavin_Chappell"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>April 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Winged_Death">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Winged Death</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here Howard Phillips Lovecraft and Hazel Heald United States English Genre(s) Horror short story Weird Tales ← Previous Next → " Through the Gates of the Silver Key " with E. Hoffman Price " Out of the Aeons " with Hazel Heald 𝐓 " " is a short story co-written by Hazel Heald and H. P. Lovecraft . It was first published in Weird Tales in 1934.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hazel_Heald"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Howard_Phillips_Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Thing">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Thing</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The things are a fictional race expanded upon by chaosium in 1994 for the call of cthulhu roleplaying game . They are a deceitful race with the ability to shape shift into the form of any creature that they consume . They are technologically advanced race that possess intestellar ships, energy beam weapons, anti-gravity packs, and possibly time travel technology .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Call of Cthulhu</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Who Goes There</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>John W. Campbell</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Land_of_Fiction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dimensions"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalLocations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdfs:label>Land of Fiction</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Alternate Dimension Ruling Powers Gods of Ragnarok Gods of Ragnarok Fictional characters (folklore, mythology, and fiction) First appearance ADJ ​​: "The Mind Robber" Created by Peter Ling The is a dimension created by BBC in 1968 for Doctor Who . Background The first appeared in an adventure involving the second incarnation of The Doctor . It was later stated as having been created by the Gods of Ragnarok for their own entertainment, but eventually they grew bored of the and abandoned it. The dimension is inhabited by characters from various works of folklore, mythology, and fiction. External links ​ at the Doctor Who wiki ​</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Alternate Dimension</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Gods of Ragnarok Fictional characters (folklore</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>fiction)</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>mythology</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>ADJ ​​: The Mind Robber</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Sword_of_Spartacus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Sword of Spartacus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story is set in early summer, ad 27, in the italian town of fidenae . It involves the recruitment of simon of gitta, an enslaved gladiator . He is recruited into a scheme to obtain vengeance for the rebel spartacus .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_L._Tierney"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Swords Against Darkness III</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 1978</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Commercial_House">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Commercial House</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Arkham , Massachusetts Restaurant or Hotel First appearance HPL : " Herbert West--Reanimator " Created by H. P. Lovecraft The is a restaurant or hotel that has a bar where drinks are served, located in the fictional town of Arkham , Massachusetts and mentioned in the story " Herbert West--Reanimator " by H. P. Lovecraft . Herbert West and his friend, the unnamed narrator of the story, were drinking there after the funeral of Dr. Allan Halsey . They decided that night to steal his body from Christchurch Cemetery so they could attempt to reanimate it.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Restaurant or Hotel</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Massachusetts"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West--Reanimator"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Faceless_God">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Faceless God</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Revered by a branch Brotherhood of the Black Pharaoh</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Dark Messenger of Karneter</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>God of the Desert</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Lord of the Desert</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is an avatar of nyarlathotep described in a homonymous story by robert bloch . It is one of the multiple avatars of nyarlathotep related to the sphinx . His cult ended up being forbidden and his effigies abandoned in the desert, where they remain buried .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Faceless_God"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_Bloch"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Munchkin_Cthulhu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Munchkin Cthulhu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Thematic version of the popular munchkin card game, is a game in which players compete to gain "levels" in the form of points . Like all munchkin releases, it is 100% compatible with other sets . Has spawned a series of similarly-themed expansions and sets allowing players additional options without incorporating different themes .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Within_the_Mountain_of_Madness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Within the Mountain of Madness</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Roy Thomas Mike Docherty, Rudy Nebres English Marvel Comics Release Date November 1995 Media Type Comic book is a story in issue #4 of the 1st volume of Conan the Savage written by Roy Thomas . Synopsis Conan the pirate and the Black Corsairs end up in the Plateau of Leng where they encounter a Shoggoth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Roy_Thomas"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>November 1995</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Anthony_Wilcox">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Henry Anthony Wilcox</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Rhode Island School of Design</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Wilcox is a fictional character created by h. p. lovecraft . He makes his first appearance in the 1928 short story " the call of cthulhu " wilcox is an art student studying sculpture at the ri school of design .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Rhagorthua">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Rhagorthua</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Father of All Winds</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Great old one is a fictional deity created by david conyers for the delta green setting of chaosium 's call of cthulhu role-playing game . Background is a fiery great old one similar to cthugha , who is able to absorb nuclear radiation .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Handful_of_Dust"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_Conyers"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ferdinand_Ashley">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ferdinand Ashley</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_University"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ferdinand c. ashley is a fictional character created by h. p. lovecraft for his 1936 novella the shadow out of time . In both tales, he has a minor role .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_in_the_Gallery"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shadow_Out_of_Time"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Music_of_Erich_Zann_%28Nick_OGorman%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleComicBookAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Music of Erich Zann (Nick O'Gorman)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The music of erich zann is a comic book-format adaptation of the short story of the same name by canadian artist nick o'gorman . It was published through his independent label target destroyed comics in 2021 . The book was later included in the omnibus collection hpl vol. 1: comic adaptations the works of hp lovecraft .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nick_OGorman"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2021</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Elder_Valusia">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Elder Valusia</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Region Serpent people Created by Lin Carter is the name given to the land and kingdom of the serpent people lasting from its settlement after their flight from Shuggon , to the arrival and conquest of Valusia by Man.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Region</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Serpent people</ex:isInhabitedByL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Roy_Thomas">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Roy Thomas</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Roy William Thomas Jr. Connection to the Mythos Writer Birth Date 22 November 1940 Jackson, Missouri, USA United States Roy William Thomas Jr. is a prolific American comic book writer and editor, most notable to this wiki for expanding the world of Robert E. Howard 's character Conan the Barbarian - who has been retroactively incorporated into the Cthulhu Mythos since his early stories - in the 1970s. Selected Bibliography The Horn of Azoth (1990) " Within the Mountain of Madness " (1995)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Missouri Jackson</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Roy William Thomas Jr.</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Writer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>22 November 1940</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Thing_in_the_Pond">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Thing in the Pond</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A man relates the tale of how, as a boy, he witnessed the taking of one of his friends from a local pond by an unknown creature . His friend returned, reanimated and rotting, to try and entice the boy down to the city of tsath where he claimed to live in contented servitude . As an adult, the man comes back from the second world war lame and traumatised, and returns to the pond .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#John_R._Fultz"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Weirdbook Annual 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Arkham_Sampler_Summer_1948">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#AugustDerlethWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Periodicals"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Arkham Sampler Summer 1948</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Ronald Clyne United States English The Arkham Sampler Arkham House Release Date Summer 1948 100 Preceded by Spring 1948 Followed by Autumn 1948 was the second edition of short-running magazine The Arkham Sampler . Edited by August Derleth with cover art by Ronald Clyne, it ran to 100 and was published by Arkham House . Contents "A Kink in Space-Time" by H. Russell Wakefield "Night in the City" by Geraldine Wolf "The Novels of M. P. Shiel" by A. Reynolds Morse "No Stranger Dream" by Clark Ashton Smith " The Loved Dead " by C. M. Eddy, Jr. "On the Mount of Stone" by Clark Ashton Smith "Howard Phillips Lovecraft" by Samuel Loveman "A Letter to E. Hoffmann Price" by H. P. Lovecraft "Old Wives' Tale" by Leah Bodine Drake "Strangers from Hesperus" by Norman Markham "Further West Legends" by Robert Hunt The Dream Quest of Unknown Kadath (Part 3 of 4) by H. P. Lovecraft "Dr. Keller's Stories" by John Haley "Wit and Satire" by August Derleth "Studies in Murder" by August Derleth "Gremlins" by Leah Bodine Drake Reviews by John Haley, August Derleth, Leah Bodine Drake, and uncredited contributors External Links full issue online at the Internet Archive</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>100</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Arkham_Sampler"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>Summer 1948</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tom_Sullivan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tom Sullivan</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Illustrator Special Effects Artist United States Years Active 1978-present is an American special effects artist and illustrator. Overview A long-time friend of director Sam Raimi , worked as a special effects artist on all three of the Evil Dead films which draw inspiration from the works of horror maestro H. P. Lovecraft , and was responsible for bringing to life both the Book of the Dead and the Kandarian Dagger. Between 1982 and 1992, he supplied artwork for various supplements in Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game range. Selected Works Special Effects The Evil Dead (1981) The Evil Dead II (1987) Army of Darkness (1992) Concept Art The Cry of Cthulhu (unfinished project) Cover Art Cthulhu Now (1987) Illustrations Alone Against the Wendigo (1985) S. Petersen's Field Guide to Creatures of the Dreamlands (1989) Shadows of Yog-Sothoth (1982) The Great Old Ones (1989) Shadows of Yog-Sothoth (2004)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasYearsActiveR>1978-present</ex:hasYearsActiveR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Illustrator</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Special Effects Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Mountain_Walked">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Mountain Walked</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various United States English Genre(s) Weird fiction Centipede Press Release Date March 2014 636  is a Cthulhu Mythos anthology edited by noted Lovecraft scholar S. T. Joshi . Overview Containing 28 stories and running to a total of 636 , was released by Centipede Press in March 2014. A version with slightly different contents and order was published by Night Shade Press in 2015. Contents " The Lurking Fear " by H. P. Lovecraft " Pickman's Model " by H. P. Lovecraft " The Last Feast of Harlequin " by Thomas Ligotti " Far Below " by Robert Barbour Johnson " Spawn of the Green Abyss " by C. Hall Thompson " The House of the Worm " by Mearle Prout " The Deep Ones " by James Wade " The Franklyn Paragraphs " by Ramsey Campbell " Black Man with a Horn " by T. E. D. Klein " Where Yidhra Walks " by Walter C. DeBill, Jr. " Only the End of the World Again " by Neil Gaiman " The Phantom of Beguilement " by W. H. Pugmire " A Gentleman from Mexico " by Mark Samuels " The Black Brat of Dunwich " by Stanley C. Sargent " Sigma Octantis " by Rhys Hughes " Mandelbrot Moldrot " by Lois Gresh " ...Hungry...Rats " by Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. " Virgin's Island " by Donald Tyson " In the Shadow of Swords " by Cody Goodfellow " Mobymart After Midnight " by Jonathan Thomas " Man with No Name " by Laird Barron " John Four " by Caitlín R. Kiernan " " by Gemma Files " The Wreck of the Aurora " by Patrick McGrath " Thirteen Hundred Rats " T. Coraghessan Boyle " Beneath the Beardmore " by Michael Shea " Rupa Worms from Outer Space " by Denis Tiani " Excerpts from a Notebook " by Drazen Kozjan Dark Regions Press Edition: " The House of the Worm " (1933) by Mearle Prout " Far Below " (1939) by Robert Barbour Johnson " Spawn of the Green Abyss " (1946) by C. Hall Thompson " The Deep Ones " (1969) by James Wade " The Franklyn Paragraphs " (1973) by Ramsey Campbell " Where Yidhra Walks " (1976) by Walter C. DeBill, Jr. " Black Man with a Horn " (1980) by T. E. D. Klein " The Last Feast of Harlequin " (1990) by Thomas Ligotti " Only the End of the World Again " (1994) by Neil Gaiman " Mandelbrot Moldrot " (2012) by Lois Gresh " The Black Brat of Dunwich " (1997) by Stanley C. Sargent " The Phantom of Beguilement " (2001) by W. H. Pugmire " ...Hungry...Rats " (2014) by Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. " Virgin's Island " (2014) by Donald Tyson " In the Shadow of Swords " (2014) by Cody Goodfellow " Mobymart After Midnight " (2013) by Jonathan Thomas " A Gentleman from Mexico " (2007) by Mark Samuels " The Man with the Horn " (2014) by Jason V. Brock " John Four " (2014) by Caitlín R. Kiernan " Sigma Octantis " (2014) by Rhys Hughes " " (2014) by Gemma Files " The Wreck of the Aurora " (2014) by Patrick McGrath " Beneath the Beardmore " (2014) by Michael Shea Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>636</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>March 2014</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Doors_to_Heaven">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Doors to Heaven</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sarah Saltiel Cover Artist Phil Stone English ', The Yellow King Genre(s) Roleplaying game Pelgrane Press Release Date 2022 38 is a scenario supplement for Pelgrane Press 's Yellow Mythos roleplaying game The Yellow King . Written by American games designer Sarah Saltiel , it was published through DriveThruRPG as a free digital download in 2022 . Overview contains a complete stand-alone scenario for The Yellow King which takes place in Paris, a city central to the game. External Links at DriveThruRPG at RPGGeek References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sarah_Saltiel"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>38</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>'</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>The Yellow King</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2022</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Black_Kiss">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Black Kiss</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The short story was originally published in the june 1937 issue of weird tales . It features kuttner's occult investigator character, michael leigh .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Kuttner"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_Bloch"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>June 1937</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kevin_L._OBrien">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Kevin L. O'Brien</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Editor Author United States is an American author and editor whose works deal primarily with the fantasy and alternate future genres. With regards to this wiki, he edited the thematic anthology Eldritch Blue: Love &amp; Sex in the Cthulhu Mythos , and has written a number of stories based within the setting. He has cited Ramsey Campbell as one of his major influences. Selected Bibliography Editor Eldritch Blue: Love &amp; Sex in the Cthulhu Mythos Author " October Surprise " (2005) " Far Sight " (2006) " Let There Be Darkness " (2006) " Euchred " (2007) "A Fidus Aranea" (2020) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Editor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_Repository">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Miskatonic Repository</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Online print-on-demand roleplaying game is a player-driven resource initiative for the call of cthulhu roleplaying game . It allows creators to offer free or for-sale their own resources for the game with the parent company's blessing . For any content which is sold through drivethrurpg, 50% is payable to the creator, with the other 50% divided between chaosium and drivethrurpg .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yhashtur">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yhashtur</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Worm-God of the Lords of Thule</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as The Worm-God of the Lords of Thule First appearance " Servants of the Coils " Created by Kevin Eric Sheridan is a worm-like Great Old One that dwells at Northern Polar latitudes. It is said to be a rival of the outer god Nyarlathotep , the Crawling Chaos.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Servants of the Coils</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Kevin Eric Sheridan</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Khalkru">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Khalk'ru</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>All-in-All</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Greater-than-Gods</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Is a fictional extra-dimensional creature created by abraham merritt for his novel dwellers in the mirage . Can be summoned from its native dimension by a mysterious ring bearing its image . Followers believe it is a force of chaos and entropy, antagonistic to the very principle of life .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isLocatedAtC>A valley in Alaska</ex:isLocatedAtC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dwellers_in_the_Mirage"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Abraham_Merritt"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Luke_Robinson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dreamers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Luke Robinson</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Dreamer</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The dreamer is a character who appears in several of fantasy flight games ' additions to the expanded cthulhu mythos . He was originally created to be an investigator for the kingsport horror expansion for the second edition of arkham horror . He has since made appearances in eldritch horror , arkham horror: the card game , and arkham horror third edition .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Kingsport Horror Deluxe Expansion</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Coeval_with_Nights_and_Chaos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Coeval with Nights and Chaos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cthulhu mythos story first appeared in the anthology swords against cthulhu ii: hyperborean nights in january 2017 . Raine poisons the guards, having one of the other servants dump their bodies in the mass grave which the temple of yhoundeh has become .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Charlie Walls</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Swords_Against_Cthulhu_II:_Hyperborean_Nights"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>January 2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Whisperer">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Whisperer</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Voice of Chthon</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional demon in the prime reality of the . Marvel universe of comics . Created in 1993 by chris cooper, first appearing in issue #12 of the 1st volume of . Darkhold: pages from the book of sins .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>1993</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Darkhold: Pages from the Book of Sins Vol 1 12</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Chris Cooper</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
