  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ash_vs_Evil_Dead">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ash vs Evil Dead</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Bruce Campbell Ray Santiago Dana DeLorenzo Lucy Lawless Production Company Starz Release date Ocrober 2015-April 2018 United States English is an American comedy-horror series created for Starz by Sam Raimi , Ivan Raimi, and Tom Spezialy . It is part of the Evil Dead franchise created by filmmaker Sam Raimi, and was broadcast in three series between October 2015 and April 2018 . Synopsis Set three decades after the original trilogy, follows the adventures of Ash Williams , who has seemingly wasted his life in the years since the events depicted in Army of Darkness , as he must once again do battle against the evil forces thrown against him by the demon-possessed Necronomicon Ex-Mortis . Future Although cancelled after its third series, in July 2022 actor Bruce Campbell, a long-time friend of Raimi's and the actor who has played Ash Williams in all of his screen appearances, announced that an animated show was in the works to continue the story begun in . External Links at Wikipedia at the Evil Dead Fandom wiki Gallery References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>Ocrober 2015-April 2018</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chronicles_of_the_Cthulhu_Codex_Winter_2000">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex Winter 2000</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Gervasio Gallardo English Fungoid Press Release Date December 2000 68 Preceded by Eastertide 1999 was the final issue in the long-running yet sporadically-released fanzine Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex . Edited by Pierre Comtois and featuring cover art by Gervasio Gallardo , it was published by Fungoid Press in December 2000. This issue was the first to be edited by Comtois and to bear the original name since Issue 4 , some thirteen years previously. Contents "Aqua Salaria" by Pierre Comtois "Against the Providence Point of View" by Ron Hilger "The Ebb of Reason" by Joseph Pulver " Some Thoughts on H. P. Lovecraft, the Cthulhu Mythos and the State of Weird Fiction " by Pierre Comtois " The Tulu Jar " by Ann K. Schwader "The Forgotten Ritual of Mnar" by Joseph Pulver "Clark Ashton Smith: Fantasiste or Science Fictioneer?" by Simon Whitechapel "The Mutual Doom of the Lord Hwepkath and the Lady Myopphwe" by Simon Whitechapel " Advice for the Weird Fictioneer " by H. P. Lovecraft "The Exorcism of Iagsat" by Joseph Pulver "The Phosphor Lamps of Clark Ashton Smith" by Ron Hilger and Donald Sidney-Fryer "Soliloquy in an Ebon Tower" by Clark Ashton Smith " The Passing of Cassilda " by Richard Tierney "Shadow Falls Needs Guitars" by R. J. Zimmerman "A Few Words from the Masters" by Robert E. Howard and H. P. Lovecraft and Clark Ashton Smith</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>68</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 2000</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Home_From_The_Sea:_Tales_of_Lovecraftian_Terror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Home From The Sea: Tales of Lovecraftian Terror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>William Meikle English Release Date April 2017 Media Type Print Digital 244 is a fourteen-story collection of works by prolific British-born William Meikle . Contents " SymbiOS " " The Island Of Doctor Munroe " " The Terror that Came to Dounreay " " Inquisitor " " The Tenants of Ladywell Manor " " The Larkhill Barrow " " The Invisible Menace " " The Colour that Came to Chiswick " " Ripples in the Ether " " The Doom that Came to Dunfield " " Home From the Sea " " Amoeboid " " From Between " " HashtagDreaming " Publication History First published in April 2017, was released in both print and digital formats. It runs to a total of 244 . Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>244</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>April 2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
