  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#He_Shall_Put_on_the_Semblance_of_Man">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>He Shall Put on the Semblance of Man</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The short story was first published in the anthology n , published by stygian fox in may 2021 . Behind the mythos althoughcontains hints but no explicit references to h.p. Lovecraft's works, the god is intended to be the outer god nyarlathotep .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Lovecraftian fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>N</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 2021</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Voormithadreth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Voormithadreth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mount Hyperborea Volcano (extinct) Tsathoggua Atlach-Nacha First appearance CIRCLE : " The Seven Geases " Created by Clark Ashton Smith Mount is an extinct volcano with four cones on the continent of Hyperborea , said to be the tallest peak in the Eiglophian mountains. The Great Old Ones Tsathoggua and Atlach-Nacha are both claimed to have at some point taken up residence there.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Volcano (extinct)</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Tsathoggua Atlach-Nacha</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hyperborea"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Seven_Geases"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Night-gaunt">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ServitorRaces"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Night-gaunt</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nodens"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Night-gaunts are a species of flying creatures in the cthulhu mythos . They first appeared in h. p. lovecraft's novella the dream-quest of unknown kadath . They revere and worship nodens as their lord and master .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Horror in the Museum Fungi from Yuggoth Feeders from Within</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dream-Quest_of_Unknown_Kadath"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#S.M.A.R.T">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdfs:label>S.M.A.R.T</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationO>National Security Agency</ex:hasAffiliationO>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The army of darkness is a fictional organization in the army of darkness universe by dynamicmite entertainment . It was founded in 1300 ad by the wise man, lord arthur, and sheila to protect the world from supernatural forces . It became widespread through history, and would eventually end up as a division of the national security agency .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Director Doctor Glen Friedrich Commander Alexis Digges</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasTypeO>Secret Society</ex:hasTypeO>
    <ex:wasCreatedBynO>Chad Bowers</ex:wasCreatedBynO>
    <ex:wasCreatedBynO>Chris Sims</ex:wasCreatedBynO>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Hunters_from_Beyond">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ClarkAshtonSmithWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Hunters from Beyond</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story's titular creatures were first incorporated into the cthulhu mythos in " the guardian of the book ", by henry hasse . The story's narrator is a professional writer of stories that often dealt with occult phenomena, with the weird and the spectral . The story has appeared in numerous collections of smith's work, including lost worlds (arkham house, 1944), the city of the singing flame (timescape/pocket books, 1981</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Clark_Ashton_Smith"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Strange_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 1932</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Apotheosis:_Stories_of_Human_Survival_After_the_Rise_of_the_Elder_Gods">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Apotheosis: Stories of Human Survival After the Rise of the Elder Gods</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Apotheosis is a thematic anthology of lovecraftian and cthulhu mythos fiction . Edited by jason andrew and featuring cover art by mark henry . Story "the caverns of al-shog qaleth" is not included in the kindle ebook edition .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>284</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>October 2015</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dunwich_Horror_%28Caedmon_Records%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleAudioAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dunwich Horror (Caedmon Records)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Dunwich Horror Based on " The Dunwich Horror " David McCallum Production Company Caedmon Records Release date 1976 Running time 59 minutes (approx.) United States English The Dunwich Horror is an audio reading of the Howard Phillips Lovecraft short story of the same name . Overview A "slightly abridged" version of the original tale, The Dunwich Horror was released as a vinyl LP by Caedmon Records in 1976, with vocal talent was supplied by British actor David McCallum . It runs to a total of 59 minutes. External Links The Dunwich Horror , available to listen at the Internet Archive.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dunwich_Horror"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1976</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kat_Rocha">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Kat Rocha</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Editor Author United States United States Weird fiction  is an author, artist, editor, and comic book creator, as well as the founder of independent publishing house 01Publishing . She has had a hand in a number of works related to the Cthulhu Mythos and Lovecraftian fiction in general, and is a founding member of the San Diego chapter of the Horror Writer’s Association. Selected Works Editor Whispers from the Abyss (2013) Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are &amp; Shall Be (2015) Casefile: Arkham- Nightmare on the Canvas (2016) Casefile: Arkham- Her Blood Runs Cold (2018) Author " The Jar of Aten-Hor " (2013) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>United States</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Editor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Awaiting_Strange_Gods">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Awaiting Strange Gods</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Darrell Schweitzer Tim Kirk Cover Artist Tim Kirk United States English Genre(s) Dark Fantasy Horror Fedogan &amp; Bremer Release Date September 2015 Media Type Hardback Trade Paperback 276 : Weird and Lovecraftian Fictions is an anthology of works by American and critic Darrell Schweitzer . Overview Collecting together 22 previously-published dark fantasy and horror stories from 1994-2015, also contains an introduction by noted Lovecraft scholar S. T. Joshi . It was published by Fedogan &amp; Bremer in September 2015 in both hardcover and paperback editions, features cover art and illustrations by Tim Kirk , and runs to a total of 276 . Contents Introduction by S. T. Joshi " Envy, the Gardens of Ynath, and the Sin of Cain " "Hanged Man and Ghost" " Stragglers from Carrhae " " The Eater of Hours " "The Runners Beyond the Wall" "On the Eastbound Train" "Howling in the Dark" "Sometimes You Have to Shout about It" "The Head Shop in Arkham" "Innsmouth Idyll" "Class Reunion" "Why We Do It" " The Warm " "Spiderwebs in the Dark" "The Corpse Detective" "Jimmy Bunny" "The Last of the Black Wind" "In Old Commoriom" "The Clockwork King, the Queen of Glass, and the Man with a Hundred Knives" "The Scroll of the Worm" " Those of the Air " "Ghost Dancing"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Darrell_Schweitzer"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Dark Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>276</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 2015</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
