  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Devils_Hop_Yard">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dunwich"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Devil's Hop Yard</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A man named sawyer and two members of the decayed branch of the whateley family conspire to conduct a ritual similar to that planned by the elder whateley ten years earlier . Using the elder whateley's daughter as a vessel for the offspring, they birth an abnormal and malevolent girl-child . Once the girl comes of age, the three conduct a ritual atop the blasted hill known as .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_A._Lupoff"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Chrysalis. Volume 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>August 1978</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Thul">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Thul</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ulthar Stonecutter Human First appearance HPL : " The Cats of Ulthar " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a resident of the town of Ulthar where he works as a stonecutter (stonemason). He was one of the town burgesses who helped pass the law that made it illegal to kill cats . ( HPL : " The Cats of Ulthar ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Cats_of_Ulthar"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#To_the_American_Flag">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>To the American Flag</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft United States English Arkham House Something About Cats and Other Pieces Date of writing 1937 date 1949 " " is a poem by the late American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Although written in 1937, it did not see until its inclusion in the Arkham House collection Something About Cats and Other Pieces in 1949, twelve years after Lovecraft's death . History Something About Cats and Other Pieces (1949) Collected Poems (1963) The Californian: 1934-1938 (1977) References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Something_About_Cats"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Pieces</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1949</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>1937</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Cthulhu_Codex_6">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Cthulhu Codex 6</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Cthulhu Codex #6 Various Cover Artist C. G. Porter English Fungoid Press Release Date January 1994 57 Preceded by January 1989 Followed by May 1996 The Cthulhu Codex #6 was an issue of the sporadic fanzine The Cthulhu Codex . Edited by Ron Hilger and Henry J. Vester, III , it featured cover art by C. G. Porter and was published by Fungoid Press in January 1994. The first and only issue of the zine to be named The Cthulhu Codex (having previously been titled Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex ), it was also the only issue to have Hilger on board as editor, and the last to be published by Fungoid Press until the final issue, some 6 years later. Contents "Necronomicon" by W. H. Pugmire "Immortal Remains" by W. H. Pugmire "Lottie Mae" by Stanley McNail "Lights Along the Road" by Stanley McNail "Pilgrimage 7" by Stanley McNail "Watson's Landing" by Stanley McNail "Nether Reaches" by Marc Laidlaw "Destruction" by Charles Baudelaire "The Recluse" by David Barker "The Companion" by Ann K. Schwader "Barrow-Walkers" by Ann K. Schwader "The Wind Beyond" by Ann K. Schwader "The Doom of Azederac" by Ronald S. Hilger "Midnight Visitant" by Donald Sidney-Fryer "The Country of the Wind" by Pierre Comtois "The Bells of R'lyeh" by Henry J. Vester, III</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>57</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>January 1994</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Summoned">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Summoned</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Redemption's heir is a young adult novel by anne m. pillsworth . It is set in both providence , r.i., and in lovecraft's fictional arkham, massachusetts . It introduces sean wyndham, a teenager with mythos-related magical powers .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Anne_M._Pillsworth"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Young Adult</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>318</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Redemption's Heir</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2014 June 24</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Carnacki:_Starry_Wisdom_and_Other_Stories">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Carnacki: Starry Wisdom and Other Stories</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>William Meikle English Genre(s) Horror Detective Dark Regions Press Release Date March 2021 170 is a thematic collection of short works by British-born William Meikle . Overview Containing a selection of Meikle's Thomas Carnacki stories (although by no means all of them) contains several tales which cross over William Hope Hodgson 's occult detective with the Cthulhu Mythos created by H. P. Lovecraft and expanded upon by many others. Although not all of the tales directly reference the Cthulhu Mythos, some of those which do not could be considered to be Lovecraftian in nature. Consisting of thirteen works, nine of which are new to this collection, and running to a total of 170 , was published in ebook format by Dark Regions Press in March 2021. Contents " The Lakeside Cottages " "The Hound" (non-Mythos) "The West Bow Townhouse" (non-Mythos) "Beneath the Greenwood Tree" (non-Mythos) " A Body in the Library " "The Lute in the Manor House" (non-Mythos) " Bats in the Belfry " "Strangers on the Shore" "The Grunting Man" "The Lock-Keeper's Cottage" "The Keys to the Door" "The Glasgow House" " Starry Wisdom "</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Detective</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>170</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>March 2021</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Tenants_of_Ladywell_Manor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Tenants of Ladywell Manor</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Historywas first published in the anthology cthulhu unbound, vol. 2 in 2009 . It has since appeared in the collections of meikle's own works dark melodies (2012) and home from the sea: tales of lovecraftian terror (2017) .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Cthulhu Unbound. Vol. 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 2009</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Traveler">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Traveler</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The travelers are a fictional species expanded upon by chaosium in 1994 for the call of cthulhu roleplaying game . They are a spacefaring race whom travel across space using translucent ships the size of basketballs . When approaching a planet they use meteor showers as cover . When detected the ship auto-destructs, creating an explosion large enough to take out a city block .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Autopsy</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Shea"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_University">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Miskatonic University</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mu is a fictional university located in arkham , named after the miskatonic river which flows through the town . The university appears in numerous cthulhu mythos stories by lovecraft and many other writers . In early works by lovecraft and others, miskatonic is an apparently ordinary university whose occult undercurrent only occasionally breaks the surface .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Whisperer_in_Darkness"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Festival The Colour Out of Space History of the Necronomicon The Dunwich Horror The Whisperer in Darkness At the Mountains of Madness The Shadow Over Innsmouth The Dreams in the Witch-House The Thing on the Doorstep The Shadow Out of Time Out of the Jar Call of Cthulhu</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Massachusetts"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Essex County</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West--Reanimator"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Disciples_of_Cthulhu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Disciples of Cthulhu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>258 (second revised edition) is a cthulhu mythos anthology edited by the late american and editor edward p. berglund . The first edition was released in paperback format by daw books in october 1976 . In february 1996, the call of cthulhu roleplaying game chaosium released : second revised edition as part of their cthulhu cycle . This version ran to 258 and featured brand new cover artwork by h. e.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>288 258</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu_Cycle"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>February 1996 October 1976</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu_Fhtagn%21">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cthulhu Fhtagn!</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cthulhu Fhtagn! Various Cover Artist Adolfo Navarro English Word Horde Release Date August 2015 312 Cthulhu Fhtagn! is an anthology of Lovecraftian fiction edited by Ross E. Lockhart and published by Word Horde in August 2015. It contains works by several prominent names in contemporary weird fiction. Overview Contents "In His House at R'lyeh ..." introduction by Ross E. Lockhart "The Lightning Splitter" by Walter Greatshell "Dead Canyons" by Ann K. Schwader "Delirium Sings at the Maelstrom Window" by Michael Griffin "Into Ye Smoke-Wreath'd World of Dream" by W. H. Pugmire "The Lurker In the Shadows" by Nathan Carson "The Insectivore" by Orrin Grey "The Body Shop" by Richard Lee Byers "On a Kansas Plain" by Michael J. Martinez "The Prince of Lyghes" by Anya Martin "The Curious Death of Sir Arthur Turnbridge" by G. D. Falksen "Aerkheim's Horror" by Christine Morgan "Return of the Prodigy" by T. E. Grau "The Curse of the Old Ones" by Jesse Bullington and Molly Tanzer "Love Will Save You" by Cameron Pierce "Assemblage Point" by Scott R. Jones "The Return of Sarnath" by Gord Sellar "The Long Dark" by Wendy N. Wagner "Green Revolution" by Cody Goodfellow "Don't Make Me Assume My Ultimate Form" by Laird Barron</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>312</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 2015</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Danger_Girl_and_the_Army_of_Darkness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Danger Girl and the Army of Darkness</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Andy Hartnell Cris Bolson English Dynamite Entertainment, IDW Publishing Release Date April 2011 - August 2012 Media Type Comic book is a 6-issue crossover mini-series written by Andy Hartnell. Synopsis The secret agents of Danger Girl team up with Ash Williams against the Army of Darkness .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Andy Hartnell</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>April 2011 - August 2012</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shadow_Out_of_Time_%28I._N._J._Culbard%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleComicBookAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Shadow Out of Time (I. N. J. Culbard)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Shadow Out of Time H. P. Lovecraft (original story) I. N. J. Culbard (adaptation) I. N. J. Culbard English Genre(s) Horror SelfMadeHero Release Date June 2013 128 The Shadow Out of Time is a comic book adaptation of the short story of the same name by Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Overview Adapted by I. N. J. Culbard who also provided the artwork, The Shadow Out of Time runs to a total of 128 in full colour. It was published by SelfMadeHero in June 2013. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#I._N._J._Culbard"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>128</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2013</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#isLocatedAtC">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label>isLocatedAtC</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
