  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Horror_Premium_Figures">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Arkham Horror Premium Figures</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A range of pre-painted miniatures released by fantasy flight as a part of their arkham horror files range . Originally only the investigator figures were available, but from 2012 the monsters made their appearance . These figures, whilst still listed on fantasy flight's website as of july 2019, are all marked as out of stock .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Order_of_the_Silver_Twilight_%28Call_of_Cthulhu_LCG%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Order of the Silver Twilight (Call of Cthulhu LCG)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The order of the silver twilight is a deluxe expansion pack for fantasy flight games' call of cthulhu: the card game . Released in 2010, it introduced an entirely new faction in the form of the order of the silver twilight . It contains a total of 165 cards (55 sets of three), of which 40 are unique to the silver twilight with the remainder split between the seven other factions .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu_Michaelmas_1987">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Crypt of Cthulhu Michaelmas 1987</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cover Artist Allen Koszowski United States English Crypt of Cthulhu Cryptic Publications Release Date September 1987 56 Preceded by Lammas 1987 Followed by Hallowmas 1987 Crypt of Cthulhu Hallowmas 1985 is the 50th issue of long-running fanzine Crypt of Cthulhu . Running to a total of 56 , it was edited by Robert M. Price , featured cover art by Allen Koszowski , interior work by Ramsey Campbell , and was published by Cryptic Publications in September 1987 in an A5 format . The issue was a special edition devoted almost entirely to the works of British horror maestro Ramsey Campbell. Contents "It Came from the Past" by Ramsey Campbell "The Haunted Manor" by Ramsey Campbell "The Oak Chest" by Ramsey Campbell "The Hollow in the Woods" by Ramsey Campbell "Things from the Sea" by Ramsey Campbell "The Grave in the Desert" by Ramsey Campbell "Accident" by Ramsey Campbell "The Friend" by Ramsey Campbell "The Devil's Cart" by Ramsey Campbell "Tem Bashish" by Ramsey Campbell "The Whirlpool" by Ramsey Campbell "The Whispering Horror" by Ramsey Campbell "Bradmoor" by Ramsey Campbell "Hybrid" by Ramsey Campbell "The Tower" by Ramsey Campbell "Conversation in a Railway Carriage" by Ramsey Campbell "The Mask" by Ramsey Campbell "Premonition" by Ramsey Campbell Reviews by Stefan Dziemianowicz Letters by Mike D. Mason , Mike Ashley, Maryanne Snyder, Bruce Walker, Sean Branney , Robert Bloch , and Tani Jantsang References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>56</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 1987</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Great_Old_One_%28Doctor_Who%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Great Old One (Doctor Who)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Death Lords</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Early Ones</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Great old ones are a pantheon of malevolent entities in the doctor who universe . First time appearance of the great old ones in doctor who was in 1993 novel white darkness . Powers displayed by the great old ones varied depending on the individual .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Web Planet</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Counting,_Colors_and_Cthulhu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Storybooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Counting, Colors and Cthulhu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jason Ciaramella Joshua Janes United States English Genre(s) Childrens Educational ComixTribe Release Date 2021 is a children's educational book which takes its cue from H. P. Lovecraft 's Cthulhu Mythos . Overview Written by Jason Ciaramella and featuring artwork by Joshua Janes, contains images to aid children with numbers and colour recognition, as well as concept and development art. It was published by ComixTribe in 2021 in both board book and digital formats. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jason_Ciaramella"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Childrens</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Educational</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2021</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Heir_of_Darkness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Heir of Darkness</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>352 is a cthulhu mythos novel by glenn rahman set in the era of ancient rome . It is considered a simon of gitta story, despite not featuring that character . It is a prequel to the simon of gitta novel the gardens of lucullus, co-written by rahman and richard l. tierney .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Glenn_Rahman"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Sorcery</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Sword</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>352</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Simon_of_Gitta"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>February 1989</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Revelations_from_Yuggoth_1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Revelations from Yuggoth 1</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Revelations from yuggoth #1 was the first issue of the short lived lovecraftian fanzine revelations from yuggoth . Edited by shawn ramsey, it featured cover art by david t. pudelwitts, ran to 48 in an a5 format, and was published by cryptic publications in november 1987 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>48</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Revelations_from_Yuggoth"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>November 1987</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Gentleman_Caller">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Gentleman Caller</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Historywas first published in the anthology return of the old ones: apocalyptic lovecraftian horror in 2017 . It was also included in a collection of snyder's own works, garden of eldritch delights .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lucy_A._Snyder"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gray_Weaver">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ServitorRaces"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gray Weaver</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Atlach-Nacha"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sociocultural Characteristics Atlach-Nacha Notable members Tch'tkaa Real World Information First appearance EXP : " The Descent into the Abyss " Created by Lin Carter The Gray Weavers are a fictional species of monstrous beings created by Lin Carter and Clark Ashton Smith for their 1980 "posthumous collaboration" " The Descent into the Abyss ". Description The Gray Weavers are a species of many-legged creatures which serve the Spider-God Atlach-Nacha . Their leader is called Tch'tkaa .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Descent_into_the_Abyss"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dreadful_Machine">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dreadful Machine</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Martin James Hunter English 01Publishing Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are &amp; Shall Be date October 2015  " " is a short story by Martin James Hunter, first published in the anthology of Lovecraftian fiction Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are &amp; Shall Be by 01Publishing in October 2015. Synopsis The story describes the activities of the workers who serve a hellish, malevolent machine, the force which powers their city during a continent-spanning war. A new worker on the job cannot cope with what he sees, and is fed to the machine to keep it working, along with hundreds of other unfortunate souls.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Martin James Hunter</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Shall Be</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2015</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecraft_Annual">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lovecraft Annual</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a long-running periodical published by hippocampus press . First issued in 2007 and has since been released every august . Consists of essays on the works of lovecraft by a wide variety of modern-day contributors .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#F._Paul_Wilson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>F. Paul Wilson</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Francis Paul Wilson Pseudonym(s) Colin Andrews Paul F. Wilson Paul Wilson (I) Connection to the Mythos Author Birth Date 17 May 1946 Jersey City, New Jersey, US United States Science Fiction Horror Francis Paul Wilson (17 May 1946) is an American author of science fiction and horror and also a qualified medical doctor. He has cited the late Howard Phillips Lovecraft as one of his greatest influences . According to Wilson: Selected Bibliography Novels The Keep (1981) Short Fiction " The Barrens " (1989) External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction at Goodreads References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#New_Jersey Jersey City US</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Francis Paul Wilson</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Colin Andrews</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Paul F. Wilson</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Paul Wilson (I)</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>17 May 1946</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nuberus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nuberus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaos"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Nuberus the Seducer</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Bringer of Darkness</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Great One</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Keeper of Souls</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Many-Tongued</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Whisperer</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as The Many-Tongued The Keeper of Souls The Whisperer The Bringer of Darkness The Great One the Seducer Chaos Demon  is a Lovecraftian -like demonic entity in the fictional universe of the Vampirella comic book by Warren Publishing and Harris Comics. Background (aka, The Many-Tongued, the Keeper of Souls, the Whisperer, the Bringer of Darkness, the Great One, and the Seducer) is the greatest of Chaos ' servants and slumbers in the Nether-Void and the Alabaster City. When he entered Earth's reality, he enthralled the inhabitants of the world with dreams of their deepest desires being fulfilled. His return to Earth brought darkness, the eternal night that heralds the return of Chaos. After a pitched battle, Vampirella defeated and slew in Washington D.C. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_End_of_History">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
