  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#California">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>California</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The state was originally inhabited by indigenous peoples, including the yurok, pomo, miwok, and chumash . It was seized by the united states in 1846 during the mexican-american war, and became a state in 1850 . Since 1962, it's been the most populous state in the union .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>State</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#United_States_of_America"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nick_OGorman">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nick O'Gorman</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Nicholas O'Gorman Pseudonym(s) Nick OG Connection to the Mythos Comic book creator Canada Nicholas "Nick" O'Gorman , who often goes by the professional name of "Nick OG", is a Canadian comic book creator and storyboard artist based in Ottawa, Ontario. He has written several original comic books, and has also adapted a number of H. P. Lovecraft stories into the visual format. He is the founder of independent publishing Target Destroyed Comics, through which he publishes these works, usually after obtaining funding via Kickstarter crowdfunding campaigns. Selected Works Collections HPL Vol. 1: Comic Adaptations of the Works of HP Lovecraft (2023) Adaptations Beyond the Wall of Sleep (2019) HPL 1920 (2020) The Music of Erich Zann (2021) Herbert West: Reanimator (2022) Yule Horror (2023) External Links at LinkedIn at Comic Vine</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Nicholas O'Gorman</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>Canada</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Nick OG</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Comic book creator</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cytharion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalLocations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cytharion</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Cytharion of the Seven Suns</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Outer space (speculative) Also known as of the Seven Suns Realm Benevolent deities , favored mortals First appearance HPL : " The Crawling Chaos " Created by H. P. Lovecraft , also known as of the Seven Suns , is a mystical realm located somewhere "beyond the Milky Way and the Arinurian Streams ", mentioned in the story " The Crawling Chaos " by H. P. Lovecraft . is somewhere adjacent to the realm of Teloe , both of which are described as beautiful utopias inhabited by benevolent deities and favored mortals. and Teloe were part of an apocalyptic vision of the future experienced by the unnamed narrator of the story under the influence of opium, so their literal existence may or may not be taken for granted in the context of the Mythos . Behind the Mythos According to The Whisperer in Darkness and other sources, Nyarlathotep also dwells in a "world of Seven Suns", which is named Abbith in the expanded Mythos. However, Nyarlathotep is not mentioned in "The Crawling Chaos" (despite the story's title matching one of his most common aliases ).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Realm</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Benevolent deities</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>favored mortals</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Outer space (speculative)</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Crawling_Chaos"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Opener_of_the_Way_%28story%29">
