  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stanley_C._Sargent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Stanley C. Sargent</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>2018 March 6</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author Artist Birth Date 1950 Beavercreek, Ohio, USA Death Date March 6, 2018 San Francisco, CA, USA United States Years Active 1994-present was an American author and artist. Overview Born in Ohio, United States in 1950, began writing for publication at age 44. The majority of his works fall within the Lovecraftian horror genre, although he also wrote stories of fantasy, science fiction and other horror. His artistic output includes both cover and interior work for a number of periodicals, again mostly those of the horror genre. Selected Works Collections Ancient Exhumations (1999) The Taint of Lovecraft (2002) Short Stories "Just a Tad Beyond Innsmouth" (1997) " All Things Come... " (1997) " When the Stars Are Ripe " (1997) " The Black Brat of Dunwich " (1997) " The Tale of Toad Loop " (1998) " Nyarlatophis, A Fable of Ancient Egypt " (2002) Poetry "Old "Man" Cthulhu" (1996) "Wilbur's Helpless Brother" (1996) "Night Gaunts" (1997) "In The Mountains of Madness" (2002) Artist Mythos Tales &amp; Others (1996) Al-Azif (1998) Dreams of Lovecraftian Horror (1999) See Also Images by External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Ohio Beavercreek</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasYearsActiveR>1994-present</ex:hasYearsActiveR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1950</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Eldritch_Tales_%28Magazine%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Eldritch Tales (Magazine)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Eldritch tales is a fanzine specializing in weird tales -style fiction . It was originally conceived as a companion to the non-fiction fanzine dark messenger . It was revived in 2017 by robert price, initially under the aegis of necronomicon press .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Death_on_the_Arkham_Express">
