    <rdfs:label>Big Trouble in Billy's Basement</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The bad book is an episode from the first season of the animated television series the grim adventures of billy &amp; mandy .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2002 October 11</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lomar">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalLocations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lomar</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The shadow out of time created by h. p. lovecraft is a nation in the dreamlands besieged by the armies of the inutos and an encroaching northern ice sheet . Notable features olatho - a great marble city on the plateau of sarkis between the mountains noton and kadiphonek .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Quest of Iranon The Other Gods The Mound The Horror in the Museum Through the Gates of the Silver Key The Shadow Out of Time</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Commander Alos</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>The Dreamlands</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Polaris"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Vespergaunt">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Vespergaunt</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Outer Gods</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sociocultural Characteristics Outer Gods Real World Information First appearance ADJ : Inner Sea Bestiary Created by Paizo, Inc Vespergaunts were created by Paizo Inc in 2012, appearing in the Inner Sea Bestiary sourcebook for the Pathfinder roleplaying game. Background Vespergaunts are the emissaries and tools of the eldritch gods of the Dark Tapestry. Who are found mainly on Aucturn , operating as spiritual conduits for those who need to contact the Great Old Ones . Creatures that are eight feet tall and six feet wide, collecting and relaying to the dark gods those prayers which they've deemed worthy. They also prepare inhabited worlds for the coming of the Dominion of the Black.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Inner Sea Bestiary</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Inc</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Paizo</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Black_Eons">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#JamesAllisonCycle"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RobertEHowardWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Black Eons</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A pair of archaeologists, allison and brill, unearth a temple in the egyptian desert which allison believes dates from the hyborian age . Later that evening, allison dreams that he is a warrior sacking the city in which the temple once stood . Awakening to find himself within the tomb, allison realises that he is the owner of the warrior's soul, destined to once again face down the priest .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_E._Howard"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>June 1985</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Butterfly-Dragon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonSapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Butterfly-Dragon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Butterfly-dragons are found almost exclusively in the land of sona-nyl in the magical dimension known as the dreamlands . When threatened, a will release a cloud of pheromones which render those they infect profoundly deaf . This effect is so powerful that it can even cross worlds, with those affected in the dreamlands still suffering from hearing loss upon awakening .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ye_Booke_of_Monstres_II"/>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>Multicoloured wings</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#S._Petersens_Field_Guide_to_Creatures_of_the_Dreamlands"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chthon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ElderGods"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Chthon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Elder Gods (sometimes mentioned as part of the Great Old Ones )</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Great Shadow God of Chaos He Who Sleeps Demon of the Darkhold What Walked Once The Sleeper Beneath Dark Majesty Who Has Slept Since Before Man Crawled From the Sea He Who Holds the Darkness The Sleeper What Dwells Beneath Sleeping God Dark Master The Other Keku</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The character was created by marv wolfman, yong montano &amp; bill mantlo . Made its first appearance in marvel chillers #1 (under the name "the other") would not officially appear as until a few years later in avengers #186 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Marvel Chillers #1 (as The Other) Avengers #186 (as Chthon)</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Bill Mantlo</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Marv Wolfman</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Yong Montano</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Man_of_Leng">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Man of Leng</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Denizen of Leng</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Men of leng first appeared in h. p. lovecraft's the dream-quest of unknown kadath . Later featured prominently in brian lumley's 1978 novel the clock of dreams .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Clock_of_Dreams"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dream-Quest_of_Unknown_Kadath"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yhidothrus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yhidothrus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>aka, the Ravager Worm , Lord of Time ) is a Lovecraftian -like demonic entity from the fictional universe of the Pathfinder pencil-and-paper roleplaying game by Paizo Inc. Background is a qlippoth lord who became a demon lord. It's a massive worm that has a maw full of teeth. It's tail is so unspeakably horrifying, that anyone that sees it goes mad. The further you go down its body the more ancient it becomes, and its tail is rooted deep within a qlippoth-ruled Abyssal ream. It's rumored that it's body is simply the tongue of an unimaginably vast monster.</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_High">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#StoryCycles"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Miskatonic High</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>English Danger Dads November 2021 https://miskatonichighcomic.com/ is an ongoing comic book series set in the expanded Cthulhu Mythos begun with the works of H. P. Lovecraft . Written by Mike Shea and illustrated by Ryan Mendoza, the first issue made its debut in November 2021; as of February 2024, the series comprised 17 issues, one collection, and a single one-shot spin-off/prequel. Premise The main story follows five students, Sarah, Alex, Ren, Simon, and Matt, who work together in the same school-run community outreach program. Their various activities bring them into contact with various supernatural and Cthulhu Mythos forces, including Abdul Alhazred , Deep Ones , and demonic Aswang. They also visit locations as exotic and far-flung as Ancient Egypt , the Dreamlands , and Innsmouth , Issue Guide Main Series The City of Silence The Rats in the Orchard Ghost Stories Crash Mussing Pieces Monster's Ball The Legacy of Innsmouth- Part 1 The Legacy of Innsmouth- Part 2 Bad Habits The Dream Quest of Alex Davidson Reflections out of Time Stir The Other Side of the Mirror The Gift of the Diwata- Part 1 The Gift of the Diwata- Part 2 Utopia Little Girl Lost Collections Volume 1 (collects issues 1-6) One-Shot Specials Lady Lovecraft</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#isLocatedAtL">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label>isLocatedAtL</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yith">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Planets"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yith</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Great Race First appearance CIRCLE : " Dreams of " HPL : The Shadow Out of Time Created by Duane W. Rimel is a fictional planet, an earlier home of the Great Race of , a prominent species within the Cthulhu Mythos . ( HPL : The Shadow Out of Time ) The name first appeared in Duane W. Rimel 's poem cycle, " Dreams of "; Rimel had originally written "Yid", but Lovecraft changed that when revising the poems, noting that Rimel's word was also a derogatory word for Jews. The word "" appears only once in Lovecraft's fiction, when he notes in The Shadow Out of Time that "the minds of the Great Race sped across the void from that obscure trans-galactic world known in the disturbing and debatable Eltdown Shards as ."</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shadow_Out_of_Time"/>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>The Great Race</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dreams_of_Yith"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#S._Petersens_Field_Guide_to_Cthulhu_Monsters">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>S. Petersen's Field Guide to Cthulhu Monsters</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Call of cthulhu field guide is a background sourcebook for the roleplaying game by chaosium . Features an in-depth look at 27 of the most commonly-encountered monsters in the cthulhu mythos . Includes a full-colour painting of each and other details such as size comparison charts .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lynn_Willis"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sandy_Petersen"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>64</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1988</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wailing_Writher">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wailing Writher</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional entity believed to be an avatar of nyarlathotep . Made its first appearance in h. p. lovecraft's 1920 prose poem " nyarlathotep " chaosium later incorporated it into their call of cthulhu roleplaying game in the supplement escape from innsmouth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecraftiana_Vol_5,_Issue_4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Periodicals"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lovecraftiana Vol 5, Issue 4</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist James Toeken English Rogue Planet Press Release Date 2021  is an edition of the periodical Lovecraftiana edited by Gavin Chappell and published by Rogue Planet Press in 2021. Both physical and digital versions were released. It features a cover by James Toeken, interior artwork by Dean Wirth and Steven J. Alvarez (who both contributed stories) and was dedicated to the memory of Franklyn Searight . Contents " To Sea " by Josef Desade " Gate of the Gods " by Oliver Smith " Deadfall in the Parking Lot " by Francis Erdman " Acceleratrix " by Glynn Owen Barrass " Boat Trip " by David A. Riley " After the After Party " M. Stern " The Monomaniacal Pursuit of Glanvill's Will " by G. Large " Beneath the Pimple " by Bryn Fortey " My Family " by Matt Spencer " Nightjar " by Dean Wirth " Marble from the Void " Steven J. Alvarez " Lurker of the Woods " Matthew Wilson " Two Haikus " Michael Balleti</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2021</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#An_Exchange_of_Souls">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>An Exchange of Souls</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Barry Pain English Genre(s) Horror Eveleigh Nash Release Date 1911 is a horror novel by the late British Barry Pain . First published by Eveleigh Nash in 1911, it was later reprinted by Hippocampus Press in an omnibus edition with Henri Béraud 's Lazarus as part of Lovecraft's Library , a series which republishes stories H. P. Lovecraft was known to have read and admired. Synopsis The story revolves around a scientist who creates a machine which allows him to swap his consciousness with another; he uses it on his fiancé, with horrific consequences. Behind the Mythos has been suggested as a possible inspiration for H. P. Lovecraft's short horror story " The Thing on the Doorstep ".</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Barry_Pain"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1911</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Forbidden_Knowledge">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Forbidden Knowledge</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here Ron Shiflet United States English Publication date March 1997 " " is a short poem by American Ron Shiflet . Synopsis The poem is a cautionary work on the old trope of 'seeking knowledge which man was not meant to know.' Publication History "" was first published in the now-defunct fanzine Cthulhu Cultus #8 in March 1997. It later appeared in the zines Nightscapes ( January 1998 ) and Dark Legacy #3 (January 1999).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 1997</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Vrest_Orton">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Vrest Orton</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1986</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A late member of the Kalem Club. He was for a time an editor at the Saturday Review and later the founder of the Vermont Country Store. He compiled an early bibliography of Dreiser, Dreiseriana (1929).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1897</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Seen_and_the_Unseen">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Seen and the Unseen</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A man on vacation in a small coastal town decides to take a solo kayak trip out into the ocean . He bears witness to a colossal tentacled creature rising from the depths, snatching a whale up in its enormous appendages, and killing it . Discovered by a policeman on the shore many hours later, he is taken to the local station where his statement is taken . The officers, and a man revealed to be a high</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Tim Stevens</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Goodman_Simpson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Goodman Simpson</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Undertaker Human First appearance HPL : " The Tomb " Created by H. P. Lovecraft was an undertaker who, according to Jervas Dudley , robbed the recently dead body of Squire Brewster , stealing various articles of clothing before burying him in 1711. Jervas acquired this information from spirits with whom he conversed during one of his nightly visits to a local cemetery.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Tomb"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_Blake_Cycle">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#StoryCycles"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Robert Blake Cycle</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Weird Tales The is an informal title for the trilogy of short stories featuring the alter egos of H. P. Lovecraft and Robert Bloch . The three stories, in order, are " The Shambler from the Stars ", " The Haunter of the Dark " and " The Shadow From the Steeple ".</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Celestial_Toyroom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dimensions"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdfs:label>Celestial Toyroom</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a dimension created by the bbc in 1966 for doctor who . The realm of the great old one, the celestial toymaker . He resides in the "toy shop" which unlike the rest of the realm is actually connected to him .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Alternate Dimension</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Celestial_Toymaker"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>The Celestial Toymaker</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Alert">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#TechnologicalArtefacts"/>
    <rdfs:label>Alert</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Place of origin Dunedin, New Zealand Used by Members of the Cthulhu Cult Crew of the Emma Vehicle Transportation Real World Information H. P. Lovecraft First Appearance HPL : " The Call of Cthulhu " The was a heavily armored steam yacht which originated in Dunedin, New Zealand, and at one point was manned by "a queer and evil-looking crew of Kanakas and half-castes," in addition to being members of the Cthulhu cult . The crew of the was slain in retaliation for attacking the schooner Emma , and upon being discovered by the Vigilant , the was towed to Sydney, Australia where it was sold for commercial use. ( HPL : " The Call of Cthulhu ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasFunctionA>Transportation</ex:hasFunctionA>
    <ex:hasPlaceOfOriginA>Dunedin New Zealand</ex:hasPlaceOfOriginA>
    <ex:hasTypeA>Vehicle</ex:hasTypeA>
    <ex:isUsedByA>Crew of the Emma</ex:isUsedByA>
    <ex:isUsedByA>Members of the Cthulhu Cult</ex:isUsedByA>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Cthulhu"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Carnivorous_fish">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonSapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Carnivorous fish</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sociocultural Characteristics The Dreamlands Aquatic Physical Characteristics Skin colour Silver scales Real World Information First appearance HPL : The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath Created by H. P. Lovecraft The is a species of water-dwelling animal which was made passing mention of in H. P. Lovecraft 's novel The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dream-Quest_of_Unknown_Kadath"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Night_of_Dagon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Night of Dagon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The lovecraft mysteries is the first book in the lovecraft mysteries series . It is the story of private investigator devlin macky, who takes on a job to steal an artefact with magical powers . He finds himself embroiled in a plot to summon forth the voracious great old one dagon .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brandon_Berntson"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>198</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lovecraft_Mysteries"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2018</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Mannikin">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Mannikin</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Simon maglore has an "earnest belief in the occult and esoteric" his family has an "interest in sorcery" going back to italy at the time of the medici . When maglore is found dead, his secret is revealed: the lump on his back was actually a conjoined twin .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_Bloch"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>April 1937</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Whisper_Man">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Whisper Man</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Intelligence</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Whisper men are featureless beings who serve the great intelligence . They could morph into the appearance of walter simeon and appeared to be unreal, hollow on the inside . When hit they evaporated and reformed, and were able to pass their limbs into the flesh of others without leaving any visible wounds .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Name of the Doctor</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Steven Moffat</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Emerald_Tablet">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Emerald Tablet</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story first appeared in the august 2017 issue of strange sorcery (#24) it is a genuine occult text from the middle ages, regarded by islamic and european alchemists as the foundation of their art . The story is set in 33 a.d., after the events of tierney's novel the drums of chaos .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Strange Sorcery #24</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>August 2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_King_Perkins,_II">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Richard King Perkins, II</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Poet Weird fiction Years Active 2014-2017  is an author and poet who has written a handful of pieces inspired by the works of Howard Phillips Lovecraft and the Cthulhu Mythos . His works have been published in various magazines, webzines and anthologies, including the 2015 James Ward Kirk collection Lovecraft after Dark . Selected Works Poetry " Follower from the Depths " (2015) " Inscrutable Alien " (2015) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasYearsActiveR>2014-2017</ex:hasYearsActiveR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Poet</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#hasAuntR">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label>hasAuntR</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#hasNephewOrNiece"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Yog-Sothoth_Cycle">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Yog-Sothoth Cycle</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Robert M. Price English Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos Ramble House Release Date November 17, 2022 503 is an anthology of Cthulhu Mythos stories relating to the entity Yog-Sothoth , edited by Robert M. Price and published by Ramble House in 2022. The describes the book as "the long-awaited culmination of the infamous ' Cycle ' series pioneered by Chaosium , Inc." As an indication of how long the volume has been awaited, Price's introduction is dated 2004. The book is dedicated to the late Richard L. Tierney , two of whose complete novellas appear in the anthology. Contents Lords of Pain , Richard L. Tierney "Ophiucus," by Don Webb "The Threshold of Beyond," by Stephen Mark Rainey "The Sending," by Charles Garofalo "The Ultimate Ultimatum," by Robert Bloch " The Church in High Street ," by J. Ramsey Campbell "Glimpses," by A. A. Attanasio "The Deviltry of Elemental Valence," by Edward Lee "Out of Space, Out of Time," by David Langford The Winds of Zarr , by Richard L. Tierney</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>503</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2022 November 17</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Edith_Miniter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Edith Miniter</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1934</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Amateur author who also professionally published a novel, Our Natupski Neighbors (1916), and many short stories. Lovecraft was guest at her home in Wilbraham, Massachusetts, in the summer of 1928.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1867</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lost_Spirits_of_Shuma-Gorath">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lost Spirits of Shuma-Gorath</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shuma-Gorath"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The lost souls are the forged-souls of shuma-gorath forming an unreal abyss of pure suffering . Mere contact with them can shred a mortal's reality and are even able to damage powerful hell lords . They can be commanded to perform various functions, from forming a tornado-like barrier to attacking specific targets .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Doctor Voodoo: Avenger of the Supernatural Vol 1 #1</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Jefte Palo</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Rick Remender</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Swarog">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CharactersIncorporatedFromFolkloreMythAndReligion"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Swarog</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Great Old Ones First appearance " Jahrhundertsommer " Created by Jan Christoph Steines , is a hideous being appearing as a dark, gigantic, legless bird-like horror swathed in dark flames, with its long neck topped by a black lump, half of which endowed with a big glowing eye and the other being covered in innumerable tentacles. It was revered by Slavic and Viking folks as the Solar god Svarog, though sharing almost nothing with the traditional deity. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jahrhundertsommer"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Jan Christoph Steines</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Taint">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#BrianLumleyWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Taint</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Brian Lumley English Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos Weird Shadows over Innsmouth date 2005 "" is a Cthulhu Mythos story by Brian Lumley , written in December 2002/January 2003, and first published in Weird Shadows Over Innsmouth ( Fedogan &amp; Bremer , 2005). Synopsis A retired American doctor who once worked in Innsmouth comes to live at a seaside village in Cornwall where some of the locals have a familiar genetic condition. History After its initial appearance in Weird Shadows Over Innsmouth , "" was reprinted in The Mammoth Book of Best New Horror 17 (Carrol &amp; Graf/Robinson, 2006), and served as the title story for Lumley's collection and Other Novellas ( Subterranean Press , 2007).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Shadows_over_Innsmouth"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2005</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Muvians">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Muvians</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>They were the inhabitants of a land they called mu . They were seen as a threat to the rest of the world by the atlanteans . Their civilisation disappeared 10,000 years ago .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Vampirella_vs._Reanimator">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crossovers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Vampirella vs. Reanimator</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A four-issue crossover mini-series pits the superhero vampirella against the demented doctor herbert west . The story itself is rendered almost entirely in black-and-white, including only a few splashes of colour here and there . The trade paperback collecting all issues was released in august 2019 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Blacky Shepherd</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Cullen Bunn</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 2018 - April 2019</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OuterGods"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nyarlathotep</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>EXP ) Outer Gods ( EXP )</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Other Gods ( HPL ) Great Old Ones ( AWD</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>See his list of aliases</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>avatars</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The crawling chaos is a fictional outer god in the cthulhu mythos . He is the spawn of azathoth , and acts as the outer gods' "soul and messenger" also appears in numerous subsequent stories by lovecraft .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Rats in the Walls The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath The Last Test The Mound Fungi from Yuggoth The Whisperer in Darkness The Dreams in the Witch-House The Man of Stone The Shadow Out of Time The Haunter of the Dark The Isle of Dark Magic The Faceless God The Shadow from the Steeple Strange Eons The Dweller in Darkness The Clock of Dreams October Surprise Demonbane Haiyore! Nyaruko-san (as Nyaruko ) Cthulhu Saves the World It Hides in the Village</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasCharacterMateC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yhoundeh"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtC>World of Seven Suns</ex:isLocatedAtC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
