    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dark Origins</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Collected Novellas Volume 1 Various Cover Artist Anders Finér English Arkham Horror Fiction Aconyte Release Date October 2021 512 : The Collected Novellas Volume 1 is a collection of previously-published Arkham Horror Fiction novellas, first issued by Aconyte in October 2021; paperback and digital editions were released. In February 2022, Tantor Audio also issued an audio version of the book in multiple formats. Overview Contents Hour of the Huntress , by Dave Gross The Dirge of Reason , by Graeme Davis Ire of the Void , by Richard Lee Byers The Deep Gate , by Chris A. Jackson</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>512</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Horror_Fiction"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>October 2021</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dead_Thing">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dead Thing</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Frank Forte English Asylum Press Beyond Lovecraft date September 2020  " " is a Lovecraftian short story by American Frank Forte , first published in his collection Beyond Lovecraft by Asylum Press in September 2020. Synopsis When an inquisitive young boy discovers the carcass of a bizarre creature deep in the forest, his investigations result in a strange substance squirting out to cover his arm. Over the next few years, whatever he had been infected by claims his entire body, forcing him into the life of a recluse, and claiming the lives of his parents. Eventually, the larvae which he had been impregnated with emerge from his mutated body, and he finds himself transformed into a "mother" creature for these new beings.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Forte"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beyond_Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>September 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Rlyeh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>R'lyeh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Arlyeh ( The House of Cthulhu )</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Relex ( The Mound )</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Ryah (Something from Out There)</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Ryche ( Something from Out There )</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cthulhu is a fictional island city created by h. p. lovecraft . It makes its first appearance in the 1928 short story " the call of cthulhu " is a sunken city located deep under the pacific ocean and is where the great old one cthulhu is interred . The city is extraordinarily ancient, having been built on dry land in the paleozoic era .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Electric Executioner The Mound Medusa's Coil The Whisperer in Darkness At the Mountains of Madness The Shadow Over Innsmouth The Man of Stone The House on Curwen Street The Black Island The Seal of R'lyeh The House of Cthulhu 24 Views of Mt. Fuji</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>by Hokusai The Three Stooges vs. Cthulhu Godzilla vs. Cthulhu: A Death May Die Story</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Sunken Island-City</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>47°9'S 126°43'W (Beneath the Pacific Ocean)</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>49°51'S 128°34'W</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Beneath the Baltic Sea</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Cthulhu"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Agents_of_Dreamland">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CaitlinRKiernanWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Agents of Dreamland</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Caitlin r. kiernan's tinfoil dossier is the first in a trilogy . It follows two agents from rival occult intelligence agencies . They investigate a cult using alien spores to instigate a fungal apocalypse .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caitlin_R._Kiernan"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>128</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tinfoil_Dossier"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tales_from_Wonderland">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tales from Wonderland</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>various various English Zenescope Entertainment Release Date Aug 2008 - Sept 2010 Media Type Comic book is a ten-issue comic book series of one-shot comics in 2008-2010 which were published by Zenescope Entertainment. Which are tales starring one or two protagonists or antagonists of the realm of madness, Wonderland . One-Shots Queen of Hearts The Mad Hatter Alice Cheshire Cat The Red Queen Tweedle Dee and Tweedle Dum The Mad Hatter II, The White Knight The Red Rose Queen of Hearts vs. Mad Hatter</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>Aug 2008 - Sept 2010</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
