    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cynthia Ward</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author Birth Date 1960 Oklahoma, USA United States http://www.cynthiaward.com/ 𝐓 is an American author and critic from Oklahoma. Her works have appeared in a wide range of publications, including Asimov's SF Magazine and Weird Tales , and Wildside Press 's Cthulhu: Weirdbook Annual 2 . Selected Bibliography Short Fiction " Ancient Astronauts " (2019) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Oklahoma</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://www.cynthiaward.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1960</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sheb-Teth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sheb-Teth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Devourer of Souls</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as Devourer of Souls First appearance " Once Men " (RPG adventure) is an eyeless alien humanoid entity, massively overgrown with both flesh and machinery. It appears in Once Men , a fan created sourcebook for the Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game published under their "Monograph" line, a third party licensing program run by Chaosium .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Once Men (RPG adventure)</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gorgon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SpeciesIncorporatedFromFolkloreMythAndReligion"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gorgon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The gorgons are a trio of sisters in greek mythology: the two immortals stheno and euryale and the mortal medusa . Who had living venomous snakes for their hair, turning those who viewed their visage into stone . They first appeared in marvel comics in u.s.a. comics #6 (december, 1942), written and penciled by syd shores and al avison .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_in_the_Museum"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>U.S.A. Comics #6</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Iliad</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Al Avison ( EXP )</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Syd Shores</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Resurrection_of_Nicholas_Scratch">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Resurrection of Nicholas Scratch</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa Valentine De Landro , Matt Banning English Marvel Comics Release Date Feb 2006 - April 2006 Media Type Comic book is a 3-part story arc in issues #25–27 of Marvel Knights 4 , written by Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa. Synopsis The resurrected sorcerer Nicholas Scratch attempts to bring the Great Old One Shuma-Gorath to Earth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>Feb 2006 - April 2006</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Magnum_Innominandum">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OuterGods"/>
    <rdfs:label>Magnum Innominandum</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Milk of the Void</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>N'yog-Sothep</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Nyog'Sothep</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Nameless Mist</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The nameless mist is an outer god . It is the progenitor of several other cosmic entities, including the outer god yog-sothoth . Its powers include possible omnipresence, reality warping, acausality, spacetime manipulation, immortality .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Whisperer in Darkness The Shambler from the Stars</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Selected Letters of H. P. Lovecraft 2.303</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Selected Letters of H. P. Lovecraft 4.617</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Deprogrammer">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Deprogrammer</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>History was first published in the september 1989 edition of the magazine deathrealm . It later appeared in the anthologies quick chills ii (april 1992) and blasphemies &amp; revelations (november 2008)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Deathrealm</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>September 1989</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chad_Hensley">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Chad Hensley</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author Poet Denton, Texas, USA United States Horror Science Fiction is an American poet and author who has written a number of works set within the Cthulhu Mythos begun with the writings of H. P. Lovecraft and his close circle of friends. His works have been published in the Weirdbook anthology series by Wildside Press , as well as fanzines Cthulhu Codex , The Ancient Track , Dark Legacy , Tales of Lovecraftian Horror , and Nightscapes . Selected Bibliography Short Fiction "Sesqua Bud" (1998) Poetry " Dark Dreamer " (1991) " Music of Mi-Go " (1992) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Texas Denton</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Poet</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nodens">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CharactersIncorporatedFromFolkloreMythAndReligion"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ElderGods"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nodens</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>EXP )</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Elder Gods ( AWD</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Lord of the Great Abyss</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lord of the great abyss is a deity from celtic mythology, incorporated into the cthulhu mythos by h. p. lovecraft . He appears in the novel zanma taisen demonbane , as one of the elder gods who led her fleet against the vortex blaster .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Strange High House in the Mist The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath Fall of Cthulhu Haiyore! Nyaruko-san The House of Nodens Zanma Taisen Demonbane</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasCharacterMateC>Zehirete Nira Lythalia Lilith</ex:hasCharacterMateC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Celtic mythology</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caterpillar">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonSapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Caterpillar</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The caterpillars were a species of creature which appeared in brian lumley's novel the transition of titus crow . They were small animals measuring no more than eight to nine inches in length . They were attracted to heat, as the earth of the future was much colder than it is today .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Transition_of_Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Raphanasuan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Raphanasuan</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The One from the Sun Race</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as The One from the Sun Race Great Old Ones First appearance " What Hides and What Returns " Created by Bryan Thao Worra , The One from the Sun Race , is said to look like a six-armed demon. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>What Hides</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>What Returns</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Bryan_Thao_Worra"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Carnacki:_The_Lost_Cases">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Carnacki: The Lost Cases</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Ulthar Press Release Date June 2016 174 is an anthology of Thomas Carnacki short stories, a number of which are loosely connected to the Cthulhu Mythos . Edited by the late American and editor Sam Gafford , it was published by Ulthar Press in June 2016. Both paperback and digital formats were released. Contents "The Meeting" by John Linwood Grant "The Darkness" by A. F. Kidd " The Silent Garden " by Jason C. Eckhardt "The Shadow Suns" by John Howard "The Steeple Monster Case" by Charles R. Rutledge "The Moving Fur Case" by Paul R. McNamee "The Delphic Bee" by Josh Reynolds " A Hideous Communion " by James Gracey "The Dark Trade" by John Linwood Grant "The Grunting Man" by William Meikle " The Dark Light " by Robert M. Price "The Yellow Finger Experiments" by James Bojaciuk "The Gray Dog" by John Linwood Grant Trivia The opening story, "The Meeting" involves a fictional version of editor Sam Gafford purchasing a briefcase containing the other stories included in the collection.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>174</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Last_Ritual">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ArkhamHorrorFiction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Last Ritual</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>351 by s. a. sidor is a novel in the cthulhu mythos stories from fantasy flight games ' arkham horror setting for arkham horror fiction . It was adapted by graphic audio into an audio production with an entire cast of voice actors .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#S._A._Sidor"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>351 pages</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Horror_Fiction"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2020 November 3</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yeti">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ServitorRaces"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SpeciesIncorporatedFromFolkloreMythAndReligion"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yeti</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The abominable snowman, or migo, is a legendary creature and cryptid originating from the himalayan mountains . Popular culture often portrays them as having white fur, but this feature is rarely reported in actual sightings . In the cthulhu mythos, the is most commonly associated with the mi-go .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Delapore">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Delapore</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Alfred human is the main character and narrator of " the rats in the walls ", a 1924 short story by h. p. lovecraft . Created by lovecraft is the main character and narrator of " the rats in the walls ", a 1924 short story by lovecraft . Grew up a "stolid yankee", making a fortune in manufacturing .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Rats_in_the_Walls"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#M._R._James">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftsInspirationsAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosAdjacentAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>M. R. James</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Montague rhodes james was a scholar, story teller and writer . He is best known for his ghost stories and for developing some of the elements that are still used in that genre . Most of his ghost stories were originally written to be read aloud to friends . His writings influenced h. p. lovecraft , clark ashton , stephen king , ramsey .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Under_the_Shelf">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Under the Shelf</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Two sisters on an expedition discover a hidden valley inhabited by a deadly arthropod-like creature . The intervention of an ancient entity which has slept beneath the waves allows them to escape . First published in the titan books anthology the madness of cthulhu: volume 1 in october 2014 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Shea"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The Madness of Cthulhu: Volume 1</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Sisters_Love">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Sister's Love</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cthulhu mythos short story was published in the sword-and-sorcery anthology swords against cthulhu ii: hyperborean nights by rogue planet press in january 2017 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stephen_Hernandez"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Swords_Against_Cthulhu_II:_Hyperborean_Nights"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>January 2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Naacal">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ArtefactsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdfs:label>Naacal</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Pseudo-science of author james churchward is a language supposedly spoken on the lost continent of mu . Churchward claimed to have learned the language in india, where it was still spoken by only three people . The term first appears in the work of augustus le plongeon (1825-1908), a 19th century archaeologist .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasPlaceOfOriginA>http://example.org/lovecraft#Mu</ex:hasPlaceOfOriginA>
    <ex:hasTypeA>Language</ex:hasTypeA>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Hands_That_Reek_and_Smoke">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Hands That Reek and Smoke</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>W. H. Pugmire English German Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos Mythos Books Sesqua Valley and Other Haunts date October 2008 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by the late American W. H. Pugmire , first published in his collection Sesqua Valley and Other Haunts (2008, Mythos Books ) . Synopsis The narrator, a jaded and cynical artist, listens in contempt as his friends wax lyrical about a new personality on the scene, a mysterious man named Nyarlathotep . Finally persuaded to visit the newcomer and take him as their muse, the narrator falls under Nyarlathotep's spell as so many have before. However, on their return home, they witness what has become of one of their friends, and realises that there may be more to this charismatic stranger than meets the eye. History Sesqua Valley and Other Haunts (2008, Mythos Books ) The Tangled Muse (2010, Centipede Press) The Book of Cthulhu II (2012, 2022, Night Shade Books) The Strange Dark One: Tales of Nyarlathotep (2013, Miskatonic River Press ) Der dunkle Fremde (2018, Blitz) An Imp of Aether (2019, Hippocampus Press ) Die lauschende Leere (2022, Bärenklau Exklusiv) References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#W._H._Pugmire"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>German</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sesqua_Valley"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Haunts</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2008</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Varcolac">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Varcolac</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Chthon Wolf Man</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Lord of Werewolves</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Wolf Demon</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Vârcolac is a fictional character in the marvel universe which first appeared in 1988 in issue #2 of the 2nd volume of the werewolf by night comic book series . He was a demon of great power that possessed a variety of powers including a psychic connection to all vampires, superhuman speed + agility + strength, shape shifting, and making those werewolves under its influence more feral and murderous .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Werewolf by Night Vol 2 2</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Paul Jenkins</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Graham_Walmsley">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Graham Walmsley</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Games designer United Kingdom Roleplaying games http://www.grahamwalmsley.net/news/ is an English games designer who has written a number of Cthulhu Mythos -related works. These include supplements for the Pelgrane Press roleplaying game Trail of Cthulhu , as well as Stealing Cthulhu , a book providing hints and tips on how to give roleplaying games a more Lovecraftian feel. Walmsley is also the author of Cthulhu Dark , a rules-light game based in the Mythos. Selected Works Cthulhu Dark Cthulhu Dark (2017) Trail of Cthulhu The Dead White World (2011) The Apocalypse Machine (2011) Slaves of the Mother (2014) The Final Revelation (2014) Cthulhu Apocalypse (2015) Miscellaneous Stealing Cthulhu (2011) External Links at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://www.grahamwalmsley.net/news/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Games designer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Burrowers_Beneath">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#BrianLumleyWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CrossroadPress"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Burrowers Beneath</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The transition of titus crow is a cthulhu mythos novel by brian lumley . It follows occultists titus crow and henri-laurent de marigny as they uncover a plot by the chthonians and their masters against the people of great britain . The two eventually join up with the wilmarth foundation , a group of humans with knowledge of the cthulhu cycle deities . They participate in an operation to</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United Kingdom</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror Modern Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1975</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Answering_the_Call">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Answering the Call</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ngo Binh Anh Khoa English Rogue Planet Press Lovecraftiana Vol 5, Issue 3 date 31 October 2020 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos poem by Vietnamese writer Ngo Binh Anh Khoa, first published in Vol 5, Issue 3 of the Lovecraftiana zine in October 2020. Overview The fourteen lines describe the world as it appears after the rise of the Great Old One Cthulhu from his slumber in sunken R'lyeh .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Ngo Binh Anh Khoa</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 3</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>31 October 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Anders_Fager">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Anders Fager</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Swedish horror writer and game designer has described his fiction as "what would happen if james ellroy took on h.p. Lovecraft" he is best known for his short-story collection, svenska kulter . He began his game career in 1982 at the age of 18, when he traveled around sweden to demonstrate the first swedish role-playing game .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>Sweden Stockholm</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Anders Fager Johansson</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>Swedish</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Game Designer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1964 March 3</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Best_of_Dark_Legacy,_Volume_2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Best of Dark Legacy, Volume 2</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dark legacy volume 1 is an anthology of horror and weird fiction short stories . It was edited by ran cartwright and published by frogtown press in september 2016 . It ran to a total of 203 stories and featured cover art by jessica young .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>203</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dark_Legacy"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu_Unbound,_Vol._1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cthulhu Unbound, Vol. 1</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Permuted Press Release Date March 2009 280 Followed by Cthulhu Unbound, Vol. 2 is an anthology of Lovecraftian fiction edited by Thomas Brannan and John Sunseri. Running to a total of 280 , it was published in a paperback format in March 2009 by Permuted Press . Overview Contents "Noir-Lathotep" by Linda Donahue "The Invasion Out of Time" by Trent Roman "James and the Dark Grimoire" by Kevin Lauderdale "Hellstone and Brimfire" by Doug Goodman "Star Crossed" by Bennet Reilly "The Covenant" by Kim Paffenroth "The Hindenburg Manifesto" by Lee Clark Zumpe "In Our Darkest Hour" by Steven Graham "Blood Bags and Tentacles" by D. L. Snell "Bubba Cthulhu's Last Stand" by Lisa Hilton "Turf" by Rick Moore "The Menagerie" by Ben Thomas "The Patriot" by John Goodrich "The Shadow Over Las Vegas" by John Claude Smith "Locked Room" by C. J. Henderson References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>280</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>March 2009</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Black_Wings:_New_Tales_of_Lovecraftian_Horror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Black Wings: New Tales of Lovecraftian Horror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>S. T. Joshi (editor) Cover Artist Jason Van Hollander English Black Wings Genre(s) Lovecraftian Horror PS Publishing Release Date April 2010 427 Followed by Black Wings II Black Wings: Tales of Lovecraftian Horror is an anthology of Lovecraftian horror edited by S. T. Joshi , published by PS Publishing in 2010. It was reprinted by Titan Books as Black Wings of Cthulhu: Twenty-One New Tales of Lovecraftian Horror in 2012. The anthology was followed by five Black Wings sequels, numbered II-VI. Contents "Introduction" by S. T. Joshi " Pickman's Other Model (1929) " by Caitlín R. Kiernan "Desert Dreams" by Donald R. Burleson "Engravings" by Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. " Copping Squid " by Michael Shea "Passing Spirits" by Sam Gafford "The Broadsword" by Laird Barron "Usurped" by William Browning Spencer "Denker's Book" by David J. Schow "Inhabitants of Wraithwood" by W. H. Pugmire "The Dome" by Mollie L. Burleson "Rotterdam" by Nicholas Royle "Tempting Providence" by Jonathan Thomas "Howling in the Dark" by Darrell Schweitzer "The Truth About Pickman" by Brian Stableford "Tunnels" by Philip Haldeman "The Correspondence of Cameron Thaddeus Nash" by Ramsey Campbell "Violence, Child of Trust" by Michael Cisco "Lesser Demons" by Norman Partridge "An Eldritch Matter" by Adam Niswander "Substitutions" by Michael Marshall Smith "Susie" by Jason Van Hollander</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>S. T. Joshi (editor)</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Lovecraftian Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>427</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Black_Wings"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>April 2010</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hideous_Interview_with_Brief_Man">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hideous Interview with Brief Man</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nick Mamatas United States English 01Publishing Whispers from the Abyss date 2013  " " is a short story by American Nick Mamatas . It is told in the form of an interrogation, although the actual questions asked are never revealed, only the responses. History "" was published in the Lovecraft -inspired anthology Whispers from the Abyss by 01Publishing in 2013. Trivia H. P. Lovecraft, At the Mountains of Madness , and the Mi-Go are all discussed as if the story takes place in our world rather than a fictional one.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nick_Mamatas"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Whispers_from_the_Abyss"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2013</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wilmarth_Foundation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wilmarth Foundation</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>General Information The Elimination of Cthulhu Cycle Deities from Earth United Kingdom Notable Members Wingate Peaslee Titus Crow Henri-Laurent de Marigny Real World Information First appearance EXP : The Burrowers Beneath EXP : The Transition of Titus Crow EXP : Spawn of the Winds Created by Brian Lumley The is an organization based in Arkham , MA dedicated to combating the Great Old Ones with hundreds of agents and connections all over the world. During the 1960s they organised both the Great Britain Project and the American Project to drive out the Cthulhu Cycle Deities from their respective countries. The Great Britain Project was particularly successful, clearing the island of subterranean monstrosities and resulting in the death of the creature referred to as Cgfthgnm'o'th .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henri-Laurent_de_Marigny"/>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wingate_Peaslee"/>
    <ex:hasPurposeO>The Elimination of Cthulhu Cycle Deities from Earth</ex:hasPurposeO>
    <ex:isLocatedAtO>United Kingdom</ex:isLocatedAtO>
    <ex:wasCreatedBynO rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
