  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gahan_Wilson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gahan Wilson</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>21 November 2019</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Gahan Allen Wilson Connection to the Mythos Artist Birth Date 18 February 1930 Evanston, Illinois, United States Death Date 21 November 2019 Scottsdale, Arizona, United States United States https://gahanwilson.net/ Gahan Allen Wilson (18 February 1930-21 November 2019) was an American cartoonist, illustrator and author. Overview In addition to his work as a cartoonist, Wilson also contributed cover art for books such as The Horror in the Museum and Other Revisions . In 1975 he created a bust of H. P. Lovecraft for the World Fantasy Awards; this bust was used as a trophy given to winners of the award for the next forty years, until controversy over Lovecraft’s racist leanings caused it to be retired in favour of a less culturally-offensive design. Selected Works Cover Artwork Crypt of Cthulhu #72 &amp; #75 (1990) The New Lovecraft Circle (1996) Interior Art Miskatonic U. Graduate Kit (1987) See Also Images by External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>United States Illinois Evanston</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Gahan Allen Wilson</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://gahanwilson.net/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>18 February 1930</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Egg_of_Coot">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Egg of Coot</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The was originally a humanoid, or possessed humanoid, but has lost all human shape . It is now an immense ball of quivering gray flesh covered in patches of moss-like fur, eyes and mouths . The , despite its mouths, feeds off the ego of living intelligent beings .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Call_of_Cthulhu_%28Video_Game%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Call of Cthulhu (Video Game)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Call of cthulhu is a survival horror video-game developed by . Cyanide and published by focus home interactive in 2018 . The game is based on the call of cthulhu role-playing game by chaosium . It follows an original story loosely inspired by the shadow over innsmouth and " the call of cthulhu " by howard phillips lovecraft .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2018 (Microsoft Windows 2019 (Nintendo Switch) October 30 October 8 PlayStation 4 Xbox One)</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Messages_from_a_Dark_Deity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Messages from a Dark Deity</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story was published in the 2017 thematic anthology return of the old ones: apocalyptic lovecraftian horror by dark regions press . It tells the story of a reporter who witnessed something unknown entity during his time covering the war in iraq .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stephen_Mark_Rainey"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Les_contr%C3%A9es_du_r%C3%AAve">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Les contrées du rêve</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft Loïc Muzy Cover Artist Loïc Muzy France French Bragelonne Release Date August 2018 307 (English: The Lands of Dreams ) is a French- collection of the works of American H. P. Lovecraft . Running to a total of 307 , it was published by Bragelonne in August 2018 and featured cover and interior art by Loïc Muzy . Contents "Polaris" (" Polaris ") "Le bateau blanc" (" The White Ship ") "La malédiction de Sarnath" (" The Doom That Came to Sarnath ") "L'arbre" (" The Tree ") "Les chats d'Ulthar" (" The Cats of Ulthar ") "Les autres dieux" (" The Other Gods ") "Céléphaïs" (" Celephaïs ") "La quête d'Iranon" (" The Quest of Iranon ") "Hypnos" (" Hypnos ") "Memory" (" Memory ") "Le témoignage de Randolph Carter" (" The Statement of Randolph Carter ") "La clé d'argent" (" The Silver Key ") "À travers les portes de la clé d'argent" (" Through the Gates of the Silver Key ", with E. Hoffman Price ) "À la recherche de Kadath" ( The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath ) "L'étrange maison haute dans la brume" (" The Strange High House in the Mist ") "Ex oblivione" (" Ex Oblivione ") References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#France"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>307</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 2018</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Last_Lovecraft:_Relic_of_Cthulhu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Last Lovecraft: Relic of Cthulhu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The last lovecraft was written by devin mcginn, directed by henry saine, and released in the united states on 3 october 2009 . It has a total runtime of 78 minutes .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasWriterW>Devin McGinn</ex:hasWriterW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>3 October 2009</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West%E2%80%94Reincarnated">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Herbert West—Reincarnated</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Rod Heather Brian McNaughton Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. Robert M. Price C. J. Henderson Michael Cisco English Herbert West Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos Crypt of Cthulhu date November 2000 "" is a round-robin story that appeared in the Hallowmass 2000 issue of Crypt of Cthulhu (#106). It features the character Herbert West from H. P. Lovecraft 's " Herbert West—Reanimator " (1922), a continues the storyline of a similar round-robin sequel, " Herbert West—Reanimated " (1989). Overview The story is told in six chapters, each written by a different : "Colluding Cosmos" by Rod Heather "The Horror of the Holyland" by Brian McNaughton "In the Devil’s Garden" by Joseph S. Pulver, Sr. "The Thing from the Ovens" by Robert M. Price "The Fear in the Waiting" by C. J. Henderson "The Chaos into Time" by Michael Cisco History After its initial appearance in Crypt of Cthulhu, "" was reprinted in Legacy of the Reanimator ( Chaosium , 2015)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_McNaughton"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#C._J._Henderson"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Cisco"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Joseph S. Pulver. Sr.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Rod Heather</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 2000</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Olkoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OuterGods"/>
    <rdfs:label>Olkoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Outer Gods</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The God of the Celestial Arcs</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Created by user danto on the call of cthulhu roleplaying game website tentacules.net . Appears as a demoniacal deity with the ability to manifest in the form of a human if certain conditions are met . Has appeared in the short story "beneath the pimple" by bryn fortey .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Voice of Christ</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Danto (Tentacules.net)</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Great_Old_One">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Great Old One</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Great_One"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Ancient One</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Old One</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The great old ones are a group of unique, malignant beings of great power in the fictional cosmology of the cthulhu mythos . They reside in various locations on earth and once presided over the planet as gods and rulers . They are often distinguished from the more cosmically placed entities such as azathoth , nyarlathotep , and yog-sothoth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Secrets_%28Call_of_Cthulhu%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Secrets (Call of Cthulhu)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>47 secrets is a modern-day scenario supplement for the call of cthulhu horror roleplaying game . Written by brian m. sammons, it features artwork by paul carrick and maps by drashi khendup . All necessary handouts are included but, unusually, no pre-generated investigator characters .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_M._Sammons"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>47</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1997</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Beard_of_Byatis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Beard of Byatis</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Historywas first published in the scott david aniolowski-edited anthology made in goatswood by chaosium in july 1995 . It later appeared in the collection of price's own works blasphemies &amp; revelations in november 2008 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
