  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ireland">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ireland</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>" the moon-bog " is an island in europe, the homeland of the irish people . It figures as a setting in lovecraft's fiction, most extensively in " the moon-bog " it is also significant to lovecraft as the home of one of his chief literary influences, lord dunsany .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Moon-Bog"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Island</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>The British Isles</ex:isLocatedAtL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Colour_Out_of_Space_%28ARTC_audio_drama%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleAudioAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Colour Out of Space (ARTC audio drama)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Colour Out of Space (ARTC audio drama) Based on " The Colour Out of Space " Production Company Atlanta Radio Theatre Company United States English "The Colour Out of Space" is an audio drama adaptation of the H. P. Lovecraft short story of the same name produced by the Atlanta Radio Theatre Company . It is available in compact disc and digital formats on the ARTC website.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Colour_Out_of_Space"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Reapers_%28Mass_Effect%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Reapers (Mass Effect)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Old Machines</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The reapers are a central antagonistic force in the mass effect franchise . They are a highly-advanced machine race of synthetic-organic starships . They follow a cycle of galactic extinction, wiping out advanced civilizations every 50,000 years .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Mass Effect franchise</ex:hasAppearanceC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Varnae">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Varnae</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tsathoggua"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Arch-Magnus Necromantic</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Baal</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Croatoan</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Lord of the Vampires</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Nosferatu Prime</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Steve bissette is a fictional character created by marvel comics . He first appeared in the story "tomb of dracula: the blood request" in 1982 . He was an atlantean sorcerer during the thurian age . He was worshiped by the undead for centuries .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Bizarre Adventures Vol 1 #33</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Steve Bissette</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Steve Perry</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Larry_DiTillio">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Larry DiTillio</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>16 March 2019</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lawrence ditillio (february 15, 1948 – march 16, 2019) was an american film, tv series, and tabletop role-playing game writer . His creations include he-man and she-ra, and the award winning masks of nyarlathotep for chaosium's call of cthulhu rpg . He also helped to popularise the broader cthulhu mythos for decades to come .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Lawrence G. DiTillio</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Games designer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>15 February 1948</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#With_Death_Comes_Life">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>With Death Comes Life</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Scott T. Goudsward English Genre(s) Horror April Moon Books The Dark Rites of Cthulhu date March 2014  " " is a short story by American Scott T. Goudsward . Synopsis Dan, who is reeling from the suicide of his girlfriend, discovers a mysterious book which she had been keeping from him. Soon the book, or perhaps something using the book, begins to communicate with Dan, and promises to reunite him with his girlfriend if only he will perform one small ritual … Characters Dan , an average man whose life has unexpectedly entered a downward spiral. Jessica , Dan's girlfriend who seems to have been leading a double life. History "" was published in the April Moon Books anthology The Dark Rites of Cthulhu in March 2014.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Scott_T._Goudsward"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dark_Rites_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ubb">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ubb</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Lesser Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Father of Worms</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as Father of Worms Lesser Old Ones Yugg First appearance EXP : " Out of the Ages " EXP : " The Thing in the Pit " Created by Lin Carter Father , or just , is a fictional monster created by Lin Carter in his Xothic Legend Cycle , where it is portrayed as the lord of the yuggs , and identified as one of the Lesser Old Ones . Overview A large, aquatic entity similar to a chthonian , is pale gray and slug-like with a large mouth full of horn-like teeth, ringed with tentacles. dwells in the cold fastness of the Pacific Ocean , with the rest of his race, the Yuggs . The Yuggs are said to guard their gods, the Great Old Ones Ythogtha and Zoth-Ommog , whose tombs, legend tells, lie in the Abyss of Yhe and at the bottom of an abyssal trench near the island of Ponape , respectively.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Thing_in_the_Pit"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Out_of_the_Ages"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shreds_of_a_Suit_on_a_Library_Floor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shreds of a Suit on a Library Floor</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>R. C. Mulhare English Rogue Planet Press Lovecraftiana Vol 5, Issue 2 date July 2020 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by American R. C. Mulhare . It was published in the Lammas Eve edition of Lovecraftiana by Rogue Planet Press in July 2020. Synopsis Elizabeth Corwin is a farm girl posing as a male student in order to be enrolled at the traditional-minded Miskatonic University , an institution which restricts the majority of its curriculum to men. During her journey to Arkham , she crosses paths with one Wil Whateley , and witnesses something which makes her suspect that all is not as it seems with the strange giant. Later that day, she is awoken in her dorm by the sounds of one of the campus guard dogs going berserk; she and another student take it upon themselves to rubberneck through the library window, and her suspicions about Wil are confirmed when she sees his putrescent corpse liquifying on the floor.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#R._C._Mulhare"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lurker_of_the_Woods">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lurker of the Woods</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Matthew Wilson English Rogue Planet Press Lovecraftiana Vol 5, Issue 4 date 2021 " " is a poem by Matthew Wilson , first published in Vol 5, Issue 4 of the Lovecraftiana zine in 2021. Overview The story tells of how as a child, the narrator took up the task of searching for Howard Phillips Lovecraft 's lost cat. However, when he finds it, it is not a cat at all, but a monstrous little creature. He remarks on how unsurprising it is that Lovecraft suffers from night terrors as he returns the thing and claims his dollar reward.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Matthew_Wilson"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 4</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2021</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Statement_of_Eeyore_Carter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Statement of Eeyore Carter</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>As can be guessed from the title, it is a retelling of h.p. Lovecraft 's " the statement of randolph carter ", with the characters swapped out for those of a.a. milne's children's series winnie-the-pooh . It was published in the april moon books anthology the call of poohthulhu in march 2022 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kevin_Wetmore"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Poohthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 2022</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Diana_Stanley">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Diana Stanley</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Arkham Chamber of Commerce</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Arkham Historical Society</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Silver Twilight Lodge</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Women's League</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Redeemed Cultist</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The redeemed cultist is a character in the cthulhu mythos series . She was created by fantasy flight games as part of their arkham horror files range of cthulhu-related content . Her backstory diverges into two different versions . In the first version, she is sent on a mission to expose the silver twilight lodge . In the second version, she is sent on a mission to panama .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Horror:_The_Card_Game"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Elder_Sign"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Feeders_from_Within"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mansions_of_Madness"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dunwich_Horror_Deluxe_Expansion"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fantasy_Flight_Games"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Allan_Halsey">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Allan Halsey</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>1905 August 14</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_University"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Dean Halsey</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dr. is a fictional character created by h. p. lovecraft for his story " herbert west--reanimator ", in which he serves as the dean of the medical school of lovecraft's miskatonic university . The character appears in adaptations of lovecraft's story--notably the 1985 film re-animator , where he is portrayed by robert sampson .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Re-Animator"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West--Reanimator"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yibb-Tstll">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OuterGods"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yibb-Tstll</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Night-gaunts</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Patient One</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Created by brian lumley ( the patient one ) is an obscure god, said to watch at the center of all time as the universe revolves . Its blood, the black , is a weapon which takes the form of black snowflakes that stick to and smother a victim .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Caller of The Black The Horror at Oakdeene The Night Music of Oakdeene</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Rising_with_Surtsey"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Strange_Doom_of_Enos_Harker">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Strange Doom of Enos Harker</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The fragment was published posthumously in the magazine crypt of cthulhu in 1989 . It is both a continuation of carter's " behind the mask " and tied into his xothic legend cycle . The finished version was published in the 1997 collection the xothic legend cycle: the complete mythos fiction of lin carter .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Crypt of Cthulhu (fragment)</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The Xothic Legend Cycle: The Complete Mythos Fiction of Lin Carter (completed)</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1989 (fragment) 1997 (completed)</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Selected_Letters_of_H._P._Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Selected Letters of H. P. Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Selected letters is a five-volume compilation of extracts of lovecraft's known correspondence published by arkham house . It includes letters to key contributors to the cthulhu mythos like clark ashton smith , robert e. howard , august derleth , frank belknap long , and robert bloch .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_House"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1965-1976</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>1911-1937</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Aylesbury">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Aylesbury</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAccessibilityL>Road</ex:hasAccessibilityL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dunwich is a fictional town created by the late american author h. p. lovecraft . It first appeared in the 1928 short story " the dunwich horror ." They are also mentioned in the sonnet sequence fungi from yuggoth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fungi_from_Yuggoth"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Township</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#New_England"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>United States</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dunwich_Horror"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Floating_Horror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Floating Horror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nyarlathotep the is an avatar of nyarlathotep usually associated with haitian voodoo . It appears as a colossal airborne jellyfish shot through with scarlet veins . During its incubation phase it parasitically occupies the body of a living human</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Innsmouth_Heritage_%28chapbook%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Innsmouth Heritage (chapbook)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Innsmouth Heritage Brian Stableford Jason C. Eckhardt Cover Artist Jason C. Eckhardt United States English Genre(s) Weird fiction Necronomicon Press Release Date May 1992 25 The Innsmouth Heritage is a chapbook containing the Cthulhu Mythos short story of the same name by British Brian Stableford . Overview Published in May 1992 by Necronomicon Press , The Innsmouth Heritage runs to a total of 25 and features cover and interior artwork by prolific Mythos artist Jason C. Eckhardt .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Stableford"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>25</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>May 1992</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cody_Goodfellow">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cody Goodfellow</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cody goodfellow is an american author, editor and screenwriter . He has written or co-written 12 novels set in the cthulhu mythos . He has appeared in numerous short films, tv shows, music videos and commercials .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA http://example.org/lovecraft#California San Diego</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.codygoodfellow.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>29 September 1970</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Resurrected_Volume_Two:_Of_Keys_%26_Gates">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Resurrected Volume Two: Of Keys &amp; Gates</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Overview of keys &amp; gates contains three stand-alone adventures for call of cthulhu including maps, but no pre-generated characters or player handouts . The included scenarios were originally published in issues #1 and #3 of the gaming magazine the unspeakable oath . The book was published as part of pagan's sporadically-released the resurrected .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chris_Klepac"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#John_Tynes"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>John H. Crowe. III</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1994</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_%28Call_of_Cthulhu%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
