    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1986 2005</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stephanie_McAlea">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Stephanie McAlea</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Artist United Kingdom Horror is an artist, games designer and owner of British third-party gaming content provider Stygian Fox . She has provided both interior and cover art for a number of their publications, including several supplementary works for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Selected Works Gaming Supplements Whatever Happened to Alicia Thorne? (2020) Artwork Autophagia (2019) The Dark Forest (2019) Station 'S' (2020) Eyes Like Red Balls of Flame (2020, alternative cover) Never Meet Again (2021) The Derelict (2016, cartography) Cold Warning (2017, maps) Autophagia (2019) Aspirations (2019) The Dark Forest (2019) Whatever Happened to Alicia Thorne? (2020) Eyes Like Red Balls of Flame (2020, cartography) Never Meet Again (2021) See Also Images by External Links at RPGGeek</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Thomas_M._K._Stratman">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Thomas M. K. Stratman</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Editor Games designer is an author, editor and games designer who has produced on a number of Lovecraftian works during the course of his career. These include roleplaying game modules for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu horror roleplaying game, and a tie-in anthology for that company's Call of Cthulhu Fiction line of products . Stratman's non- Cthulhu Mythos works include material for White Wolf Publishing's World of Darkness setting , and a handful of unrelated short stories. Selected Bibliography Editor Cthulhu's Heirs (1994) Gaming Supplements Courting Madness (1992, contributor) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Editor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Games designer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#It_Ends_Where_It_Began">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>It Ends Where It Began</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The happenings of december 13th, 2012" is a short story by troy young . It is the sixth instalment in the nyarlathotep cycle of cthulhu mythos stories . It was published in the other: encounters with the cthulhu mythos book 1 in 2020 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Troy_Young"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Nyarlathotep_Cycle"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Other:_Encounters_with_the_Cthulhu_Mythos_Book_1"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep_%28The_Darkest_of_the_Hillside_Thickets%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nyarlathotep (The Darkest of the Hillside Thickets)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nyarlathotep Full story online here The Darkest of the Hillside Thickets (with Cristina Rizen and Inanna Gruner) Publication date 6 June 2007 ← Previous Next → "Footnote: Downtown (In The Cenozoic)" "Sounds Of An Earthquake" " Appendix: Nyarlathotep ", is a song in the 2007 album The Shadow Out of Tim by Canadian rock band The Darkest of the Hillside Thickets . The English lyrics were translated to ancient Egyptian by Cristina Rizen and Inanna Gruner. It does not contribute to the main Timothy Voss story narrated in the album, as the name implies. The foreword indicate it may be narrated from Khephnes point of view. External links English lyrics</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Inanna Gruner)</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>The Darkest of the Hillside Thickets (with Cristina Rizen</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>6 June 2007</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_H._P._Lovecraft_Historical_Society">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SmallPress"/>
    <rdfs:label>The H. P. Lovecraft Historical Society</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Hplhs is an organisation that is devoted to the promotion of the works of lovecraft and the mythos . They created the cthulhu lives live action role playing (larp) game and produced film and audio pieces; usually adaptations of lovecraft stories . They also ran the strange eons fanzine .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.hplhs.org/index.php</ex:hasWebsiteR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tekeli">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tekeli</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Tooru Araizawa</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Miss Tekeli</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Tekeli-chan</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Tekeri</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>'s were created by the great old ones to be their servants . The servants eventually went on strike, which lead to their masters punishing by sealing her away beneath antarctica . Was freed in the present day after she was discovered by an archeologist .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Uchi no Meido ha Futeikei Volume 2 Haiyore! Nyaruko-san</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Uchi no Meido ha Futeikei Volume 1</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Open_Minded">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Open Minded</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Punktown is a dystopian dystopian setting by american author jeffrey thomas . It was first published in the anthology eldritch chrome: unquiet tales of a mythos-haunted future in october 2013 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Punktown"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Eldritch Chrome: Unquiet Tales of a Mythos-Haunted Future</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2013</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_Lee_Byers">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Richard Lee Byers</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Writer Birth Date 21 September 1970 Columbus, Ohio, USA United States Horror Fantasy is an American author and comic book creator. He has written several Cthulhu Mythos works, including two tie-in novellas for Fantasy Flight Games ' Arkham Horror line of Lovecraftian games, and a short story which takes place in Jeffrey Thomas 's Punktown milieu, a setting with strong ties to the Mythos . Byers' non-Mythos works include several tie-in novels for gaming franchises such as the Dungeons &amp; Dragons setting Forgotten Realms , Games Workshop 's Warhammer , and White Wolf's World of Darkness . Selected Bibliography Collections The Hep Cats of Ulthar and Other Lovecraftian Tales (2018) Novels X-Men: Soul Killer (1999) Ire of the Void (2018) Blood of Baalshandor (2020) Short Fiction " Kickstarter " (2015) External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Ohio Columbus</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Writer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>21 September 1970</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Punktown_%28gaming_supplement%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
