    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex 2</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex #2 Various English Release Date January 1986 60 Preceded by January 1985 Followed by January 1987 Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex #2 is an issue of the irregularly-released fanzine Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex . It was edited by Pierre Comtois and published by Fungoid Press in January 1986. Contents "Footsteps in the Sky" by P. R. McBride "Madness in Haiti" by Areth Bey and Lew Cthew ""Shortest Distance..."" by R. J. Zimmerman "The Tooth" by William H. Pugmire "Metachronos" by Paul Bastienne " Innsmouth Gold " by Henry J. Vester, III</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>60</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>January 1986</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Trail_of_Cthulhu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#AugustDerlethWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Trail of Cthulhu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>August Derleth United States English (original) French German Arkham House Release Date 1962 is an anthology of Cthulhu Mythos stories by August Derleth , featuring the protagonist Laban Shrewsbury , first published by Arkham House in 1962 and reprinted several times. The stories originally appeared in Weird Tales between 1944 to 1952. Contents The stories included in the volume include (with publication date in Weird Tales ): " The House on Curwen Street " ("") (March 1944) " The Watcher from the Sky " (July 1945) " The Gorge Beyond Salapunco " ("The Testament of Claiborne Boyd") (March 1949) " The Keeper of the Key " (May 1951) " The Black Island " (January 1952) The volume also includes an essay by Derleth called " A Note on the Cthulhu Mythos ". Publication History (1962, Arkham House) (1971, Beagle Boxer) Auf Cthulhus Spur (1972, Insel, German-) (1974 Neville Spearman) La trace de Cthulhu (1974, France Loisirs, French-) La trace de Cthulhu (1975, J'ai Lu, French-) (1976, Panther) (1976, Ballantine Books) (1988, Grafton) (1996, Carroll &amp; Graf) Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#August_Derleth"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>German</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1962</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
