  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Secrets_of_Arkham_%28Call_of_Cthulhu_LCG%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Secrets of Arkham (Call of Cthulhu LCG)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Secrets of arkham is a deluxe expansion pack from fantasy flight games for the call of cthulhu: the card game . First released in 2010, a revised edition was issued in 2014 and contained a total of 160 cards . The replacement of call of cthulhu: the card game with arkham horror: the card game caused the discontinuation of secrets of arkham .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2010 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Worshippers_of_Cthulhu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Worshippers of Cthulhu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The game was developed by mythic dawn studios and published by eldritch entertainment . It draws inspiration from h. p. lovecraft ’s cthulhu mythos, a collection of stories known for their themes of cosmic dread and existential horror . The game features turn-based strategy, resource management, and narrative-driven quests .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2024 October 21</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Zamans_Hill">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Zaman's Hill</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The "great hill" was a "green, tall, and wooded" summit that hung over "the old town" in "the ancient track," the hill is first a familiar landmark that reassures the narrator of his familiar haunts . In "the ancient track," the hill is first a familiar landmark that reassures him that he well knows the place .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fungi_from_Yuggoth"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Hill</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecraft_Country"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Ancient_Track"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_in_the_Genizah">
