    <ex:isPublishedAsW>E'ch Pi El #1</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 2008</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hydrophinnae">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ArtefactsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosBooksFictional"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hydrophinnae</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Created by Gantley Used by Titus Crow Real World Information Carl Jacobi First Appearance AWD : " The Aquarium " is a fictional book created by Carl Jacobi in the short story " The Aquarium ". Attributed to an author named Gantley, it is part of a set of books dealing with the mysteries of the sea found in the collection of Horatio Lear, who had a morbid fascination with molluscs. is said to have "some of the most hideous and horrible illustrations." The book is repeatedly mentioned in the Cthulhu Mythos stories of Brian Lumley , where it appears in the private libraries of people with an interest in "oceanic lore and legend"-- people like occultist Titus Crow of Blowne House (" Name and Number ," " De Marigny's Clock "); Julian Carstairs of The Barrows, near Haslemere, Surrey (" Lord of the Worms ") ; Gavin McGilchrist of Temple House in Lothian (" House of the Temple "); Jason Carpenter of Kettlethorpe Farm, County Durham (" Dagon's Bell "); and author Julian Haughtree (" Rising with Surtsey ").</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isUsedByA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Aquarium"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByA>Gantley</ex:wasCreatedByA>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hyborian_Age">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hyborian Age</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional time period created by robert e. howard which first appeared in "the phoenix on the sword" it is the setting for the his conan the barbarian stories . In many derivative works, the fictional supercontinent is referred to as hyboria .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>Mountains</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>arctic</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>deserts</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>forests</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>jungles</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>steppe</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Era of the Earth</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Deep Ones</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Serpent People</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Winged Ones</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>humans</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Earth"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>The Phoenix on the Sword</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Boojumverse">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Boojumverse</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional setting for a series of short stories written by elizabeth bear and sarah monette . The stories combine elements of the cthulhu mythos with the bestiary of lewis carroll in a space opera setting . The stories feature a number of alien creatures, some derived from the mythos, some with names from lewis carroll .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Alan_Nelson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Michael Alan Nelson</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Comic book creator Birth Date 6 June 1971 Portage, Indiana, USA United States (born 6 June 1971) is a prolific American comic book creator and author, most of whose work is published through Boom! Studios. In addition to the Cthulhu Mythos series Fall of Cthulhu , Hexed, and The Calling: Cthulhu Chronicles, he has also worked on such high profile comic books as 28 Days Later (inspired by the British zombie film), Superman , and Supergirl . Selected Works Novels Hexed: Sisters of Witchdown (2015) Comic Books Fall of Cthulhu Volume 1: The Fugue (2007) Fall of Cthulhu Volume 2: The Gathering (2008) Fall of Cthulhu Volume 3: The Gray Man (2008) Fall of Cthulhu Volume 4: Godwar (2008) Fall of Cthulhu Volume 5: Apocalypse (2009) Fall of Cthulhu Volume 6: Nemesis (2010) Hexed (2010, limited series) The Calling: Cthulhu Chronicles (2011, with Johanna Stokes) Hexed (2015, ongoing series) External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Indiana Portage</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Comic book creator</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>6 June 1971</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Picnic_at_the_Mountains_of_Madness">
