  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Child_of_Yog-Sothoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Child of Yog-Sothoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yog-Sothoth"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Son of Yog-Sothoth</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The children of yog-sothoth are mortal creatures infused with the outer god yog-sothoth 's essence . They notably emanate an unpleasant scent, typical among old ones and relations . They are not born evil and have complex morals, but since nearly all of them are raised by the cults that create them, they almost always have evil tendencies .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dunwich_Horror"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wonderland_Finale">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wonderland Finale</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Pat Shand Cover Artist Francesca Follini English Zenescope Entertainment Release Date Sept 2016 Media Type Comic book is a one-shot comic book written by Pat Shand in 2016 which was published by Zenescope Entertainment. Synopsis Calie Liddle and her daughter Violet are hiding from the realm of madness. Meanwhile the Queen of Spades builds up an army to conquer Wonderland and a new Mad Hatter is born.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>Sept 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Pillars_of_Melkarth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Pillars of Melkarth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story first appeared in space &amp; time #78, published in 1990 . It pits the character against worshippers of august derleth 's fire deity cthugha .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_L._Tierney"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Space</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Time</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 1990</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Into_the_Black:_Tales_of_Lovecraftian_Terror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Into the Black: Tales of Lovecraftian Terror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>William Meikle English Release Date May 2019 Media Type Print Digital Digital Audio Download 205  is a collection of twelve short Cthulhu Mythos works by noted British William Meikle . The stories have all been previously published in other anthologies. Contents " Into the Black " (2015) " Broadsword " (2014) " The Longdock Air " (2017) " The Color That Stole Christmas " (2015) " Outposts " (2017) " She Sleeps in the Depths " (2014) " The Call of the Deep " (2017) " On the Threshold " (2013) " A True Telling of the Terror That Came to Red Hook " (2016) " Vulcan's Forge " (2015) " The Wonderful Musician " (2015) " The Last Quest " (2017) Publication History Into the Black was first published in May 2019 and is available in print, digital and digital download audiobook formats. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>205</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>May 2019</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Anna_Tambour">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Anna Tambour</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Australian Weird fiction https://www.annatambour.net/ is a writer of weird fiction who lives in Australia . Her work has appeared in collections of Lovecraftian fiction like Lovecraft Unbound and The Leaves of a Necronomicon . Bibliography Novels Spotted Lily (2005) Crandolin (2012) Smoke Paper Mirrors: A Short Saga for Our Times (2017) Collections Monterra's Deliciosa &amp; Other Tales &amp; (2003) The Finest Ass in the Universe (2015) The Road to Neozon (2018)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>Australian</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.annatambour.net/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Petesouchi">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Petesouchi</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Real World Information First appearance " The Cairo Guidebook " Created by Marion Anderson The are a crocodilian race created for the Call of Cthulhu role-playing game. Description When young, the resemble average humans. It is only during puberty that they begin to manifest their crocodilian traits, which vary from sharper teeth to a full transformation.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Cairo_Guidebook"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Marion Anderson</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gompa_Bkog-tu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gompa Bkog-tu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Gompa bkgo-tu is a fictional monastery created in 2013 by chaosium for the call of cthulhu roleplaying game . Within are 300 hundred monks of the yellow hat (gelug) sect. Most of whom are warrior-monks skilled in the martial arts, the bow and arrow, and the spear .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Summoning_of_Tsathoggua">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Summoning of Tsathoggua</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here Ron Shiflet United States English Publication date February 1999 " " is a Cthulhu Mythos poem by Ron Shiflet . Synopsis A wizard summons the Great Old One Tsathoggua intending to ask of him a boon, but ends up becoming a meal for the hungry creature. Publication History "" was first published in Cthulhu Cultus #15 in February 1999. It has also appeared in Lovecraft's Disciples twice, in July 2011 and March 2015.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 1999</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Winifred_Virginia_Jackson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Winifred Virginia Jackson</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1959</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Poet and amateur journalist who worked extensively with Lovecraft (1918–1921); she was rumored to have amorous designs on Lovecraft.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1876</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lythalia">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lythalia</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Forest-Goddess</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as The Forest-Goddess Current location perhaps Betelgeuse or Bel Yarnak Relatives Nodens (mate) Vorvadoss (son) Yaggdytha (son) Istasha (sister) Great Old Ones First appearance "Necronomicon: The Dee Translation" Created by Lin Carter is a Great Old One who appears as a beautiful woman wrapped in vines and vegetation. She is thought by some to be the mate of the Elder God Nodens and mother of the twins Vorvadoss and Yaggdytha . She also has a cat-like sister called Istasha .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isLocatedAtC>perhaps Betelgeuse or Bel Yarnak</ex:isLocatedAtC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Necronomicon: The Dee Translation</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beneath_the_Tombstone">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Beneath the Tombstone</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Footsteps #4 is a short story by american and lovecraft scholar robert m. price . A man inherits his distant uncles' expansive property in the remote countryside . After perusing some of the books, the man unwittingly utters a phrase from one, condemning his uncle's soul to the monsters from which he had thought himself protected .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Footsteps #4</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 1984</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Angstrom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Angstrom</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>1925</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>1925 Human First appearance HPL : " The Call of Cthulhu " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a member of the marine vessel Emma of Auburn, as detailed in the short story " The Call of Cthulhu " although his role is uncertain. After Donovan is successful in opening the vault discovered by the crew in R'lyeh , Cthulhu emerges, killing , Guerrera and Donovan. Trivia is one of only three known characters in Lovecraft 's fiction known to have been directly killed by Cthulhu itself.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#John_Full_Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSRelatives"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>John Full Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>16 April 1877</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>First son of Joseph S. Lovecraft, he married Elenor Gaskin on 8 June 1833. He worked in Rochester as a carpenter until he opened his own mill on an island in the Genessee River in 1849.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isRelativeToR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1806</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#24_Views_of_Mt._Fuji,_by_Hokusai">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>24 Views of Mt. Fuji, by Hokusai</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Roger Zelazny English French Davis Publications Publication date July 1985 is a Cthulhu Mythos novella by the late American Roger Zelazny , which was first published in the July 1985 edition of Issac Asimov's Science Fiction Magazine . Overview The story uses mythos elements as a background device for establishing atmosphere rather than as a key plot element, a short background vignette about Shinto priests discovering a far older religion and the sunken city of R'lyeh . No revelations that most readers have not seen before, but we get it mentioned and done in one page, rather than occupying an entire story, which is more focused on the relationship between an AI and his wife. Publication History , has been reprinted numerous times over the years, most notably to this wiki in the 1995 Arkham House collection Cthulhu 2000: A Lovecraftian Anthology . It has also been translated into French.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Roger_Zelazny"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 1985</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Thing_from_the_Shore_%28Call_of_Cthulhu_LCG%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Thing from the Shore (Call of Cthulhu LCG)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Thing from the Shore Fantasy Flight Games Publication Date 2008 Living Card Game Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game The Thing from the Shore is an expansion pack for Fantasy Flight Games ' Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game . Overview The fifth Asylum pack for the Summons of the Deep Cycle , The Thing from the Shore consists of the usual mix of 20 unique cards in sets of duplicate threes, and focuses on expanding options during the Skill Check segment of the Story Phase . First released in 2008, it was discontinued with the demise of Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game in 2015. Contents Unorthodox Psychologist (Character; The Agency) Endless Interrogation (Event; The Agency) Literature Professor (Character; Miskatonic University ) Summer Classes (Event; Miskatonic University) Friend of the Family (Character; Syndicate) Tear Gas (Event; Syndicate) The Thing from the Shore (Character; Cthulhu ) Communal Shower (Support; Cthulhu) Shadow Company, Ghastly Regiment (Character; Hastur ) Vaporous Isle (Support; Hastur) Nebulous Ooze (Character; Yog-Sothoth ) Domestic Sacrifice (Event; Yog-Sothoth) Insect Swarm (Character; Shub-Niggurath ) Open Grave (Support; Shub-Niggurath) Samantha Grace, Incompetent Secretary (Character; Neutral) Campaign Chief (Character; Neutral) Obsessive Inmate (Character; Neutral) Parallel Universe (Support; Neutral) The Spawn of Madness (Event; Neutral) Unorthodox Tactics (Conspiracy; Neutral)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2008</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Miskatonic_Horror_Deluxe_Expansion_%28Arkham_Horror%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ArkhamHorror"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Miskatonic Horror Deluxe Expansion (Arkham Horror)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Miskatonic horror deluxe expansion is the eighth and final expansion set for fantasy flight games' board game of lovecraftian adventure, arkham horror . Instead of introducing a new scenario for investigators to play through, it functioned as an expansion for the previous expansions . Despite this, miskatonic horror did contain rules and components to add a new mechanic to the base game: institutions .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror Action Adventure</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Horror"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Frog">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Frog</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story is set in the small town of monk's hollow . Monk's hollow is a location featured in the cthulhu mythos story " the hunt " .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Kuttner"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Strange_Stories"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 1939</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Thomas_Carnacki">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Thomas Carnacki</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Carnacki is a character created by the late british author william hope hodgson for his carnacki series of detective stories . He is a highly intelligent upper-class englishman with a deep knowledge of the occult . He is also well-versed in certain magical arts, being aware of how to create defensive wards . Other universes he has crossed over with include the cthulhu mythos .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Hope_Hodgson"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dead_White_World">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dead White World</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Graham Walmsley Cover Artist Alessandro Alaia English Trail of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Pelgrane Press Release Date March 2011 54 is a scenario supplement for the roleplaying game Trail of Cthulhu . Written by Graham Walmsley , it runs to a total of 54 and was published digitally by Pelgrane Press in March 2011. The contents were also included in the book Cthulhu Apocalypse , also by Pelgrane, in 2015. Overview</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Graham_Walmsley"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>54</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Trail_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>March 2011</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Paighon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ElderGods"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Paighon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Elder Gods</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Andromeda galaxy Elder Gods (possibly) First appearance EXP : " Homecoming ", Walter C. DeBill Jr. EXP : " Homecoming ", Walter C. DeBill Jr. EXP : " Collector's Item ", Walter C. DeBill Jr. EXP : " The Barrett Horror ", Walter C. DeBill Jr. Created by Walter C. DeBill Jr. is a "nuclear force-creature" ( EXP : " The Barrett Horror "), possibly a Great Old One or an Elder God , featured in several of the works in the Mlandoth Cycle by Walter C. DeBill Jr. In "Collector's Item", the earliest of DeBill's works he appears in, is said to have come from the Andromeda galaxy to the Solar System and settled inside the core of the Earth soon after it formed. is the deadly enemy of Ngyr-Khorath and his servitor, 'Ymnar . ( EXP : " The Barrett Horror ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Collector's Item</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Homecoming</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Barrett Horror</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Walter C. DeBill Jr.</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Homecoming</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Walter C. DeBill Jr.</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Walter C. DeBill Jr.</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Children_of_Glaaki">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Children of Gla'aki</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A Tribute to Ramsey Campbell's Great Old One Various Cover Artist Daniele Serra United States English Genre(s) Horror Dark Regions Press Release Date January 2017 294 : A Tribute to Ramsey Campbell's Great Old One is a thematic anthology of Cthulhu Mythos stories. As it’s title suggests, the stories focus on Campbell 's Severn Valley denizen Gla'aki . Overview Consisting of 18 short stories - including " The Inhabitant of the Lake ", the first to feature Gla'aki - and a new afterword by Campbell himself, runs to a total of 294 . Edited by Brian M. Sammons and Glynn Owen Barrass , it was published in 2017 by Dark Regions Press in both physical and ebook formats. Contents Introduction by Glynn Owen Barrass and Brian M. Sammons " The Inhabitant of the Lake " by Ramsey Campbell " Mouse, City Mouse " by Nick Mamatas " Tribute Band " by John Goodrich " In Search of Lake Monsters " by Robert M. Price " The Collection of Gibson Flynn " by Pete Rawlik " The Secret Painting of Thomas Cartwright " by W. H. Pugmire " I Want to Break Free " by Edward Morris " The Spike " by Scott R. Jones " The Dawning of His Dreams " by Thana Niveau " The Lakeside Cottages " by William Meikle " Invaders of Gla'aki " by Orrin Grey " Scion of Chaahk " by Tom Lynch " Cult of Panacea " by Konstantine Paradias " Squatter's Rights " by Josh Reynolds " Beneath Cayuga's Churning Waves " by Lee Clark Zumpe " The Nature of Water " by Tim Waggoner " Night of the Hopfrog " by Tim Curran " Mirror Fishing " by John Langan "From the Depths of Time: Afterword" by Ramsey Campbell</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>294</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>January 2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Baoht_Zuqqa-Mogg">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Baoht Z'uqqa-Mogg</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Bringer of Pestilence</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Baoht is a powerful winged scorpion-like monstrosity with an ant-like head . It is worshipped by small conclaves of ghouls . Baoht also lived on shaggai</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Mysterious Manuscripts (RPG)</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Thomas_M._K._Stratman"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fenric">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Fenric</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Hastur the Unspeakable Aboo-Fenrán The Wolf The Hunger</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Hastur is a primordial cosmic entity created by the bbc for doctor who . Created by ian briggs is one of the most powerful creatures ever featured in show . Can manipulate time and space so as to "cause things to happen"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>ADJ Games Black</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Monsters The Wolves of Winter</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>White Gods</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Curse of Fenric</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Ian Briggs</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lovecraft_Necronomicon_Primer:_A_Guide_to_the_Cthulhu_Mythos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Lovecraft Necronomicon Primer: A Guide to the Cthulhu Mythos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>T. Allan Bilstad English Llewelyn Publications Release Date October 2009 is a reference work concerning the monsters and entities created by H. P. Lovecraft , written by T. Allan Bilstad. It was released in a paperback format by Llewelyn Publications in October 2009 . Overview References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>T. Allan Bilstad</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>October 2009</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kenneth_Bykerk">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Kenneth Bykerk</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author Horror  is a horror writer. His works have appeared in anthologies such as Write Like Hell: Lovecraft in a Time of Madness and Weirdbook Annual 2 . Selected Bibliography Short Fiction " Mercy Holds No Measure " External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nightscapes_August_1997">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nightscapes August 1997</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Edward P. Berglund Release Date August 1997 Preceded by June 1997 Followed by September 1997 is the second issue of the long-running online fanzine Nightscapes . It was edited by the late American and Lovecraft scholar Edward P. Berglund . Contents Fiction " MIBs " by Tim Waggoner " The Dig " by Sean Rodgers "The Key of the Poet" by Edward M. Kane " All Things Come… " by Stanley C. Sargent " The Green Decay " by Robert M. Price "The Doom of Enos Harker" by Lin Carter and Laurence J. Cornford "The Horror from the Well" by R. S. Cartwright "Dark Shapes Rising" by James W. Shoffner Non-Fiction "Tying Up a Few of HPL's Twisted Loose Ends" by Stanley C. Sargent Poetry " Folks of Innsmouth: Stranger on the Street " by Franklyn Searight " Ghouls " by Ron Shiflet " The Seven Gates of Slumber " by Ron Shiflet " A Pickman Inspired Dream " by Ron Shiflet Reviews By Peter A. Worthy and James Ambuehl External Links full issue online at the Nightscapes website</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 1997</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#They_Thrive_in_Darkness:_Mythos_and_Madness">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>They Thrive in Darkness: Mythos and Madness</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ron Shiflet United States English Tenoka Press Release Date June 2018 Media Type Print Ebook 274 is a collection of short Cthulhu Mythos works by American Ron Shiflet . Overview Containing a mix of both reprinted stories and new content, contains 19 stories set in the expanded Cthulhu Mythos. It was first published in both print and ebook formats by Tenoka Press in June 2008 and runs to 274 . Contents " They Thrive in Darkness " (2006) " Last Stand at Waltham's Cabin " (2018) " When in Leng " (1998) " Yellow Is the Color of Tomorrow " (2004) " Incident at Dagon Wells " (2007) " Atonement " (2018) " Unfinished Business " (2006) " Moths to a Pallid Flame " (2018) " The One That Got Away " (2001) " Seduced " (1997) " The Serpents of Tenoka " (1997) " Out of Her Gourd " (2018) " To Bare One's Soul " (2005) " Snake Fever " (2004) " A New King in Town " (2011) " Out of the Frying Pan " (2009) " Seven Serpents Waiting " (2000) " The Storm Cellar " (2018) " The Black Goat " (2005)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>274</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2018</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Notebook_Found_in_a_Deserted_House">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Notebook Found in a Deserted House</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story was first published in the may 1951 edition of pulp magazine weird tales . It features the first appearance of the creatures which would become known as the dark young of shub-niggurath .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_Bloch"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>Finnish</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 1951</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Screaming_Crawler">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Screaming Crawler</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Aristocrat lady clare heatherington and her faithful manservant jake morgan travel to the jungles of africa to put an end the cults of nyarlathotep . They befriend a tribe of pigmies in their long-running quest to put an end the cults of nyarlathotep which plague the world . However, they are beset by both the , a creature sent by their enemies to end their lives, and a group of colon</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_Conyers"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Dreaming in R'lyeh #1</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>January 2003</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ye_Booke_of_Monstres_II">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ye Booke of Monstres II</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>More nightmares for call of cthulhu is a supplement for the roleplaying game . It contains information on 59 creatures for storytellers to use in games . The beings include outer gods , great old ones and elder gods .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Scott_David_Aniolowski"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>64</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1995</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#George_T._Wetzel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonFictionAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Scholars"/>
    <rdfs:label>George T. Wetzel</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>10 November 1983</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Scholar Birth Date 1 June 1921 Baltimore County, Maryland, USA Death Date 10 November 1983 United States Non-fiction (1 June 1921 - 10 November 1983) was an American author, editor and early Howard Phillips Lovecraft scholar who wrote a number of works on both Lovecraft's works and his personal life. He also edited several collections of non-fiction on these subjects . Wetzel has been reported as having been a member of the Esoteric Order of Dagon amateur press association , and is reputed to have been something of a "difficult character," having allegedly sent malicious letters to the employers of those he took a dislike to . Selected Bibliography Author " On the Cthulhu Mythos " (1948) " The Cthulhu Mythos: A Study " (1955) " Amateur Press Works " (1955) Editor Selected Essays Volume I (1952) Howard Phillips Lovecraft: Memoirs, Critiques &amp; Bibliographies (1955) Commentaries (1955) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Baltimore County Maryland</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Scholar</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1 June 1921</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beholder">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Beholder</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The beholders are an aberrant race from the universe in the d&amp;d pencil-and-paper roleplaying game . They are malevolent abberations whose forms are that of an orb of flesh with a cyclopean eye and a maw full of sharp teeth . They despise all life, seeing themselves as the pinnacle of existence, and desire the extermination of all other lifeform</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tamash">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tamash</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Tamash of Illusions</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as of Illusions Great Ones First appearance HPL : " The Doom That Came to Sarnath " EXP : " The Crawler of Pnoth ", Mike Minnis Created by H. P. Lovecraft (or of Illusions ( EXP : " The Crawler of Pnoth " by Mike Minnis ) ) is a Great One dwelling on Kadath . was one of the chief gods worshipped in doomed Sarnath along with Lobon and Zo-Kalar . All three were depicted as graceful bearded men. ( HPL : " The Doom That Came to Sarnath ") Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mike_Minnis"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Crawler of Pnoth</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Doom_That_Came_to_Sarnath"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthaeghya">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cthaeghya</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Relatives Cthulhu (half-brother) First appearance EXP : " October Surprise " Created by Kevin L. O'Brien is the half-sister of Cthulhu . She is responsible for spawning the Cthulhi .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#October_Surprise"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kevin_L._OBrien"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Pickmans_Model_Kit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Pickman's Model Kit</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cliff Biggers English Ulthar Press Pickman's Gallery date 2018 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by Cliff Biggers. It was published in the Matthew Carpenter -edited thematic anthology Pickman's Gallery by Ulthar Press in 2018. Synopsis When avid model kit collector Danny discovers a " Pickman's Model " kit of a ferocious ghoul in a run-down antiques shop, he is delighted, and snaps up the bargain, immediately rushing home to build his new prize. Over the next couple of days, strange disappearances in his neighbourhood, along with subtle changes to the model which suggest it reacts in sympathy to the events, horrify Danny, and he attempts to destroy the artefact. However, this only succeeds in summoning a real ghoul who appears to be somehow linked to the model, and Danny quickly becomes its latest victim.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Cliff Biggers</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Pickmans_Gallery"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
