  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Experiments%E2%80%A6">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Experiments…</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"experiments... " is a short cthulhu mythos story by authors sergio palumbo and ernesto canepa . It was published in vol 5, issue 3 of the lovecraftiana zine in october 2020 . The inspiration for the genetic technology modifications gifted to robert andberg is clearly drawn from extremis .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ernesto_Canepa"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sergio_Palumbo"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 3</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sumners_Pond">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sumner's Pond</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Arkham , Massachusetts Pond First appearance HPL : " Herbert West--Reanimator " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a pond in the fictional town of Arkham , Massachusetts , mentioned in the story " Herbert West--Reanimator " by H. P. Lovecraft . When Herbert West and his friend, the unnamed narrator of the story, were experimenting with the reanimation of the dead, one of their early test subjects was a man who had drowned in the pond.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Pond</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Massachusetts"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West--Reanimator"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Catch_of_the_Day">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Catch of the Day</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Ed Nobody English Rogue Planet Press Lovecraftiana Vol 5, Issue 3 date 31 October 2020  " " is a Lovecraftian short story by Irish Ed Nobody, first published in Vol 5, Issue 3 of the Lovecraftiana zine in October 2020. Synopsis A man hears the tale of how the captain of a fishing boat and his crew claims to have encountered an eldritch horror while out making their living. The octopoid abomination became tangled in the boat's nets, nearly sinking it and driving the captain to the brink of madness - or perhaps even causing the very fabric of reality to unravel - before he was able to slay it with a kettle full of boiling water. The listener is understandably sceptical, but soon changes his mind when the captain shows him the corpse of the beast pinned to a nearby building.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Ed Nobody</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 3</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>31 October 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Andromeda_Among_the_Stones">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CaitlinRKiernanWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Andromeda Among the Stones</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Caitlin R. Kiernan English The Dandridge Cycle Subterranean Press Publication date 2003 ← Previous " Study for The Witch House " "" is a short story by Caitlin R. Kiernan , part of their Dandridge Cycle . It first appeared as a chapbook accompanying the anthology Embrace the Mutation ( Subterranean Press , 2003). Synopsis The story reveals the history of the Dandridge family: how Machen Dandridge found “a hole in the world" on the California coast and built a house there; how his wife, Ellen Douglas-Winslow Dandridge, died trying to stop the demons from "squeez in through the tear"; how their son Avery Dandridge tried to close the gate, even though "the one who wields the key cannot be a man," and was spit back "twisted and insane"; and finally how their daughter Meredith Dandridge becomes the creature on the rock who holds the line against "the moment when the stars wink out one by one and the sea heaves its rotting belly at the empty, sagging sky." Publication History "" was reprinted in The Mammoth Book of New Terror (Robinson/Carrol &amp; Graf, 2004) and The Book of Cthulhu (Night Shade Books, 2011). It also appeared in Kiernan's collections To Charles Fort, with Love (Subterranean Press, 2005), Two Worlds and In Between: The Best of Caitlin R. Kiernan (Subterranean Press, 2011), Houses Under the Sea: Mythos Tales (Centipede Press, 2018), and The Very Best of Caitlín R. Kiernan (Tachyon Publications, 2019).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caitlin_R._Kiernan"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dandridge_Cycle"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2003</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tales_Out_of_Innsmouth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tales Out of Innsmouth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Robert M. Price , ed. Dave Carson Cover Artist H. E. Fassl English Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos Chaosium Release Date September 1999 284 : New Stories of the Children of Dagon is an anthology of Cthulhu Mythos stories related to the imaginary setting of Innsmouth . It was edited by Robert M. Price and published by Chaosium in 1999. Contents "The One That Got Away" essay by Robert M. Price "The Weird Shadow Over Innsmouth" by John S. Glasby and H. P. Lovecraft "Understudy" by Gary Myers (1997) " The Doom That Came to Innsmouth " by Brian McNaughton "Return to Y'ha-nthlei" by John S. Glasby (1997) "The Old Ones' Signs" by Pierre Comtois "Fleas of the Dragon" by C. J. Henderson "Mail Order Bride" by Ann K. Schwader "The Idol" by Scott David Aniolowski "The Guardian of the Pit" by Franklyn Searight (1996) "Trust Me" by Stanley C. Sargent "Just a Tad Beyond Innsmouth" by Stanley C. Sargent (1997) "The Deep End" by Gregory Luce "It Was the Day of the Deep One" by Peter H. Cannon (1997)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>ed.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>284</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 1999</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Formless_Spawn">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ServitorRaces"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Formless Spawn</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Black Slime</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Fluid Ones</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Ichorous</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The are fictional creatures in the cthulhu mythos, originally created by clark ashton smith . They are polymorphic entities made of black ichor and look like amorphous goo . Being a living viscous liquid, they can ooze through small cracks, usually finding a way through any obstacle .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Mound"/>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>A living ooze able to take temporary forms</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>like a mass of undulating limbs</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>or a great sphere possessing many mouths.</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Tale_of_Satampra_Zeiros"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Clark_Ashton_Smith"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Turtle">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Turtle</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Neil Baker English Genre(s) Horror War Publication date 2014 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by British-Canadian Neil Baker . Synopsis An American soldier fighting in the War of Independence chooses to redirect the power of an experimental weapon against an insidious cult of fish-folk and their monstrous allies instead of against the British when he sees that humanity must unite against the common threat. Characters Sergeant Oliver Schulte/Sergeant Oliver Lee , an American chosen to pilot a revolutionary submersible dubbed (note: the character is introduced with the surname Schulte but is later exclusively referred to as Oliver Lee). Publication History "" was published in the thematic anthology World War Cthulhu by Dark Regions Press in 2014.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Neil_Baker"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>War</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Finn_Edwards">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Finn Edwards</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Bootlegger</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The bootlegger is a character created by fantasy flight games . He appears in several of their expanded cthulhu mythos lines . The character is expanded upon in graham mcneill's novel, ghouls of the miskatonic .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Innsmouth Horror Deluxe Expansion</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Scooby-Doo%21_Mystery_Incorporated">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crossovers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Scooby-Doo! Mystery Incorporated</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mystery incorporated is a children's television show based on the long running scooby-doo! Franchise . Unlike other entries in the series, it features an overarching storyline which continues throughout both seasons . The larger story involves professor pericles, a hyper-intelligent talking parrot, attempting to harness the power of the evil entity .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2010-2013</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Now_We_Are_Nine">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Now We Are Nine</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Joel Enos English 01Publishing Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are &amp; Shall Be date October 2015 " " is a short story by Joel Enos, published in the Kat Rocha -edited anthology of Lovecraftian fiction Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are &amp; Shall Be by 01Publishing in October 2015. Synopsis A man relates the story of how small entities enter his home through a "dark patch", each one needing something different from he and his wife. The creatures' demands become more and more traumatic, and the couple find themselves being slowly consumed, mind, body and soul.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Joel Enos</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Shall Be</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Whispers from the Abyss Vol. 2: The Horrors That Are</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2015</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#House_of_Strangers">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>House of Strangers</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Gail Simone Dale Eaglesham Tom Derenick English DC Comics Release Date December 2015 - March 2016 Media Type Comic book "" is a four-part story featured in issues #7-10 of Secret Six Vol 4, written by Gail Simone and published by DC Comics. Synopsis The supervillain team Secret Six risks bringing about the end times by the Elder Gods in an attempt to save the life of their youngest member, Black Alice.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Gail Simone</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 2015 - March 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecrafts_The_Dunwich_Horror_%28Ben_Granoff%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleComicBookAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>H. P. Lovecraft's The Dunwich Horror (Ben Granoff)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft's The Dunwich Horror H. P. Lovecraft (original story) Ben Granoff (adaptation) Ben Granoff English Genre(s) Horror Bag &amp; Board Studios Release Date 31 August 2016 H. P. Lovecraft's The Dunwich Horror is a comic book adaptation of the Howard Phillips Lovecraft short story of the same name . Overview Adapted by artist Ben Granoff, The Dunwich Horror was a single issue adaptation released by Bag &amp; Board Studios in August 2016.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Ben Granoff</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>31 August 2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Asphinxiation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Asphinxiation</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Frank Forte English Asylum Press Beyond Lovecraft date September 2020 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by American Frank Forte , first published in his collection Beyond Lovecraft by Asylum Press in September 2020. Synopsis Miskatonic University resercher Dr. Darius believes himself to be writing a cautionary work about the extraterrestrial dangers facing mankind, and relates the tale of how, after discovering a copy of the fabled Necronomicon , he was led to a chamber hidden below the Great Sphinx of Giza . Beneath the chamber he discovered a portal to the ruined city of R'lyeh , within which terrible forces were beginning to stir. Driven half mad, he fled before collapsing into unconscious. The story concludes with the revelation that Darius is in fact incarcerated in a mental health facility, and in his insanity believes that the doctors are his peers, come to hear his dire warnings.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Forte"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beyond_Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>September 2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dream_Cycle_of_H._P._Lovecraft:_Dreams_of_Terror_and_Death">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dream Cycle of H. P. Lovecraft: Dreams of Terror and Death</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft Cover Artist John Jude Palencar English Del Rey/Ballantine Release Date March 2003 387 is a collection of works by the late American H. P. Lovecraft . First published by Del Rey/Ballantine as a paperback in October 1995, it was reissued in a digital format in March 2003. It was subsequently re-released, although details on the dates of this edition are unclear . Overview Contents Introduction: Concerning Dreams and Nightmares by Neil Gaiman " Azathoth " " The Descendant " " The Thing in the Moonlight " with Jack Chapman Miske " Polaris " " Beyond the Wall of Sleep " " The Doom That Came to Sarnath " " The Statement of Randolph Carter " " The Cats of Ulthar " " Celephais " " From Beyond " " Nyarlathotep " " The Nameless City " " The Other Gods " " Ex Oblivione " " The Quest of Iranon " " The Hound " " Hypnos " " What the Moon Brings " " Pickman's Model " The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath " The Silver Key " " The Strange High House in the Mist " The Case of Charles Dexter Ward " The Dreams in the Witch-House " " Through the Gates of the Silver Key " with E. Hoffmann Price References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>387</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>March 2003</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Once_Men">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
