  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu_Eastertide_1983">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Crypt of Cthulhu Eastertide 1983</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Robert M. Price Richard L. Tierney Cover Artist Nick Petrosino United States English Crypt of Cthulhu Release Date April 1983 48 Preceded by Candlemas 1983 Followed by Roodmas 1983 was the twelfth issue of Robert M. Price 's long-running Lovecraftian fanzine Crypt of Cthulhu . Edited by Price, it ran to a total of 48 in an A5 format and was published in April 1983. Price also supplied interior artwork, along with Richard L. Tierney , and the issue featured a cover by Nick Petrosino. Contents Editorial Shards by Robert M. Price "My Debt to H. P. Lovecraft" by Robert Anton Wilson "H. P. Lovecraft, Prose Stylist" by Steve Mariconda "The Chesuncook Witch-Cult" by Will Murray "A Lovecraftian Taxonomy" by Robert M. Price "H. P. Lovecraft on the Screen: Or, Yog-Slob and Other Disasters" by Denise Dumars "Godzilla Vs. Cthulhu: What Would Happen If Toho Studios Ever Discovered Lovecraft" by Crispin Burnham "Crypt-o-Cthulhu-Gram" (puzzle game) by Carol Selby "Lovecraft and Antarctica" by Ralph E. Vaughan "What Face Wears Nyarlathotep?" by Edward DeGeorge "Limericks from Yuggoth" by Lin Carter "Kadath" by Brian Lumley "Fun Guys from Yuggoth: The Nameless Bookseller" by Scott D. Briggs Reviews by Sam Gafford , Larry Baker, Ronald Shearer, Robert M. Price, Scott D. Briggs, and John Anthony (I) Letters by Richard L. Tierney , Richard Fawcett, Steve Kane, Edward P. Berglund , David E. Schultz , and Steve Behrends</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>48</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>April 1983</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Horrific_Journeys">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Horrific Journeys</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Kara Centell-Dunk Fantasy Flight Games Publication Date 2018 Mansions of Madness is an expansion set for the second edition of Fantasy Flight Games ' Cthulhu Mythos board game Mansions of Madness . Designed by Kara Centell-Dunk , it was published in 2018. introduces investigators Silas Marsh , Agnes Baker , Jim Culver , and Trish Scarborough to Mansions of Madness . Overview Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tyrannon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tyrannon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The conqueror is an incredibly powerful dimensional lord whose ultimate goal is to conquer the multiverse, so he can absorb every dimension until only he remains . His true form is a 200 ft tall eldritch tree that has heads growing out of it's branches like fruit . He has an army of billions, and his greatest rival for multiversal supremacy is the beautiful and brilliant empress istvatha v'han .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Narrative_of_Arthur_Gordon_Pym_of_Nantucket">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Narrative of Arthur Gordon Pym of Nantucket</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Arthur gordon pym is considered a major influence on lovecraft's at the mountains of madness . The novel tells the story of a young man who travels further and further south . The phrase "tekeli-li" reoccurs in the novel .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Edgar_Allan_Poe"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1838</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Hymn">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#BrianLumleyWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Hymn</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Brian Lumley English Genre(s) Cthulhu Mythos H. P. Lovecraft's Magazine of Horror Date of writing July/August 2003 date Fall 2006 "" is a Cthulhu Mythos story by Brian Lumley , written in July/August 2003, that first appeared in the Fall 2006 issue of H. P. Lovecraft's Magazine of Horror . It is one of the last of Lumley's Mythos stories to appear, and serves as something of a final statement on the genre. Synopsis As part of a secret government experiment, two individuals with psychic powers are housed in an underground chamber, constantly exposed to an eldritch artefact. History After its initial appearance in H. P. Lovecraft's Magazine of Horror , "" was reprinted in Lumley's collection Haggopian and Other Stories ( Subterranean Press , 2008). References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecrafts_Magazine_of_Horror"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>Fall 2006</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>August 2003 July</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Stalker_in_the_Snows">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Stalker in the Snows</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A small expedition goes into the mountains of minnesota to try and catalog wolves . A member of the party begins to spontaneously spout mythos lore . After being unwillingly exposed to mythos lore, the survivor of the expedition becomes a raving cannibal .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#James_Ambuehl"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu_Codex_Eastertide_1997"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>April 1997</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
