  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Yig_Cycle">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Yig Cycle</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Jason Eckhardt English Ramble House Release Date 2021 404 is a thematic anthology of Lovecraftian fiction. Edited by Robert M. Price and featuring cover art by Jason Eckhardt , it was published by Ramble House in 2021. Both print and digital editions were released. Overview Contents The Allegory of Yig, introduction by Robert M. Price " The Curse of Yig " by H. P. Lovecraft "The Automatic Electric Executioner" by Adolphe de Castro and H. P. Lovecraft "The Vengeance of Yig" by Lin Carter " Under the Mound " by Robert M. Price "The Trial" by Peter H. Cannon "The Horror at the Lake" by Donald R. Burleson "Beyond the Wall of Time" by Brian McNaughton "A Movement in the Grass" by Walter C. de Bill, Jr. "The Temple in the Swamp" by Larry Brasington "The Shadow in the Valley" by Larry Brasington "The Shortest Distance ..." by R. J. Zimmerman "The Artifacts from Quivira" by Ross F. Bagby "The Shadow Over Uxmal" by Will Murray "The Dreams of Yig" by Pierre Comtois and Henry J. Vester, III "The Sad Saga of Mad Jake Roberts" by Adam Niswander "The Tulu Metal Disc" by Allen Mackey "Scales of Justice" by Allen Mackey "The Return of Yig" by Frederick Stansfield "From Darker Heavens" by Stanley C. Sargent " The Snake Farm " by James Ambuehl "The Blue Light People" by Michael Szymanski "The Rattle of Her Smile" by Stanley C. Sargent "The Jest of Yig" by Don Webb "The Mark of Yig" by Robert M. Price "One Fang" by Scott A. Cupp Story Notes by Robert M. Price</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>404</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2021</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Steampunk_Cthulhu:_Mythos_Terror_in_the_Age_of_Steam">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Steampunk Cthulhu: Mythos Terror in the Age of Steam</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Daniele Serra United States English Chaosium Release Date June 2014 309  is a collection of Lovecraftian short stories published by Chaosium as part of their Call of Cthulhu Fiction line in June 2014. Edited by Glynn Owen Barrass and Brian M. Sammons , both print and digital versions were released. Overview Contents Introduction by Glynn Owen Barrass and Brian M. Sammons "Those Above" by Jeffrey Thomas "The Blackwold Horror" by Adam Bolivar "No Hand to Turn the Key" by Carrie Cuinn "The Reverend Mr. Goodworks &amp; the Yeggs of Yig" by Edward M. Erdelac " Carnacki—The Island of Doctor Munroe " by William Meikle "Pain Wears No Mask" by John Goodrich "Before the Least of These Stars" by Lee Clark Zumpe "The Promised Messiah" by DJ Tyrer "Unfathomable" by Christine Morgan "The Flower" by Christopher M. Geeson "Tentacular Spectacular" by Thana Niveau "Fall of an Empire" by Glynn Owen Barrass and Brian M. Sammons "The Baying of the Hounds" by Leigh Kimmel "Mr. Brass &amp; the City of Devils" by Josh Reynolds "The Source" by D. L. Snell "Happy Birthday, Dear Cthulhu" by Robert Neilson "The Strange Company" by Pete Rawlik</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>309</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2014</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
