  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kingsport">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Kingsport</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Innsmouth is a fictional seaside town created by . H. p. lovecraft , an integral part of lovecraft country . It is also the name of the supernatural town featured in carl jacobi 's short story "chameleon town", published in the board game .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Festival The Strange High House in the Mist The Silver Key At the Mountains of Madness The Shadow Over Innsmouth Through the Gates of the Silver Key The Thing on the Doorstep</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>Cliffs</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Massachusetts"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Terrible_Old_Man"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Out_of_the_Black">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Out of the Black</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>William Meikle English Angelic Knight Press Fading Light: An Anthology of the Monstrous date August 2012  " " is a Lovecraftian short story by British William Meikle . It was first published in the anthology Fading Light: An Anthology of the Monstrous by Angelic Knight Press in August 2012. Synopsis An explorer searching for life-giving ores on a dying Earth discovers a seemingly-derelict habitation of other humans which his instruments indicate hold a cache of the material. However, when he enters the complex, he finds humans devolved into a feral state, their minds shattered by the star-dotted blackness of the infinite sky. Returning to his own warren, he deletes the coordinates of the site, begging his friends not to go in search of that cursed place, before realising that the madness which had infected the others has also taken root in his own mind… History Fading Light: An Anthology of the Monstrous (2012) Green Grow the Rashes and Other Stories (2015, 2019) The Keeper of the Gate (2019)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Fading Light: An Anthology of the Monstrous</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>August 2012</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Elysia">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dimensions"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Elysia</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAccessibilityL>Time Clocks Possibly Other Means</ex:hasAccessibilityL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The home of the ancient and inscrutable elder gods is impossible to describe in its entirety . It features many cities which hover above its varied landscape, each as individual as the god or race which inhabits them . It is an incredibly difficult dimension to locate . This may be due to the fact that it is protected by the unimaginably vast powers wielded by the elder gods .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>Kthanid 's Palace Tiania 's Sky Quarters The Lithard Lake The Mountain-Island of the Dchichi</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasTypeL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dimension"/>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Kthanid Tiania Titus Crow Lithards Dchichi Esch</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Transition_of_Titus_Crow"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Scourge_of_BMoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Scourge of B'Moth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story's titular entity has since been incorporated into the cthulhu mythos by henry hasse in " the guardian of the book ", and would go on to be portrayed as an avatar of cthulhu in the role-playing game call of cthulhu . A psychiatrist named randall is called by his eminent friend and colleague, doctor prendergast, to assist in an unusual case . On the way to the hospital, the road seems to</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Bertram Russell</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Weird_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 1929</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jason_Thompson">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Jason Thompson</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Jason Bradley Thompson Connection to the Mythos Comic Book Adaptor Supplementary Contributor Birth Date 13th October 1974 San Francisco, California United States http://mockman.com/ Jason Bradley Thompson is an American artist and comic book creator whose output includes a graphic novel collecting several of H. P. Lovecraft 's Cthulhu Mythos stories, along with role-playing game material for use in the setting. Selected Works The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath and Other Stories , a graphic novel including comic book adaptations of several of Lovecraft's works along with a map of the Dreamlands . The stories featured are: The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath The White Ship Celephaïs The Strange High House in the Mist Hyperborea: The Tale of Satampra Zeiros , an adaptation of Clark Ashton Smith 's " The Tale of Satampra Zeiros ". The Club of the Seven Dreamers , a roleplaying module for the D20 system set in the Dreamlands. The Dreamland Poster , a comprehensive map of the Dreamlands.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#California http://example.org/lovecraft#San_Francisco</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Jason Bradley Thompson</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://mockman.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Comic Book Adaptor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Supplementary Contributor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>13th October 1974</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Tattered_Lady">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Tattered Lady</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The thing in the customs house" is a short cthulhu mythos story by canadian troy young . It is the sixth episode in his nyarlathotep cycle . It is published in the collection the other: encounters with the cthulhu mythos book 2 in 2020 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Troy_Young"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Nyarlathotep_Cycle"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Other:_Encounters_with_the_Cthulhu_Mythos_Book_2"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
