  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yuggoth_on_the_Rim">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yuggoth on the Rim</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here Alan Peschke English Genre(s) Horror Nightscapes #7 date April 1998 " " is a Cthulhu Mythos poem by Alan Peschke . Synopsis The six four-line verses describe an encounter with the alien Mi-Go , and end with the statement that the narrator will shortly join them on their homeworld of Yuggoth . History "" was first published in the online Mythos zine Nightscapes #7 in April 1998, and saw physical print in Imelod #11 in October of the same year.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Alan Peschke</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Nightscapes #7</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>April 1998</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Marc_A._Michaud">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonFictionAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Scholars"/>
    <rdfs:label>Marc A. Michaud</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Scholar United States Non-fiction Years Active 1976-present is an American author, editor and scholar whose focus is weird fiction in general, and the works of H. P. Lovecraft in particular. He is also founder of indie publisher Necronomicon Press , which he began in 1976 to distribute those works of Lovecraft which had never previously seen print. The majority of his writings are non-fiction, and he has collaborated with several other scholars in these; his co-authors include S. T. Joshi , Donald R. Burleson and Steven J. Mariconda . Michaud was also a member of the Providence Pals , an informal group of H. P. Lovecraft enthusiasts and scholars active from the late 1970s through to the 1990s. Selected Works Editor H. P. Lovecraft in "The Eyrie" (1979, with S. T. Joshi ) Uncollected Prose &amp; Poetry Volume 2 (1980, with S. T. Joshi) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasYearsActiveR>1976-present</ex:hasYearsActiveR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Scholar</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Delta_Green:_The_Role-Playing_Game">
