  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Euchred">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Euchred</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>In lovecraft's shadow #1 date march 2007, which has also been published as "eucred", is a short cthulhu mythos story by kevin l. o'brien . It was first published in ron shiflet 's short-lived fanzine in lovecraft's shadow in march 2007 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kevin_L._OBrien"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>In Lovecraft’s Shadow #1</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 2007</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Throne_of_Achamoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Throne of Achamoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story first appeared in the autumn 1985 issue of weirdbook (#21) it was co-written by richard l. tierney and robert m. price . The story is set in the autumn of 32 a.d., starting out in antioch .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Richard_L._Tierney"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_M._Price"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Weirdbook 21</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 1985</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Disciples_of_the_Rapine_Storm">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cults"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Disciples of the Rapine Storm</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationO rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hastur"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional organization in the cthulhutech pencil-and-paper roleplaying game by wildfire llc . It is a cult under the control of hastur which emerged from the plateau of leng . Its armies have destroyed and depopulated huge swaths of asian and european territory .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isLocatedAtO>Plateau of Leng Asia Eastern Europe</ex:isLocatedAtO>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Alskali">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Alskali</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep"/>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Outer Gods</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The are a species of inhuman creatures created by theatre of the mind . They are about ten feet tall with squat, heavily-muscled bodies . Each has a single black glossy eye in the centre of their otherwise human faces .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasDistinctionC>Cyclopean</ex:hasDistinctionC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Pursuit_to_Kadath"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The All-Seeing Eye of the Alskali scenario</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lurking_Fear">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Lurking Fear</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the houndthe rats in the walls" is a short story by h. p. lovecraft in the horror fiction genre . Written in november 1922, it was first published in the january through april 1923 issues of homebrew . Like "herbert west--reanimator", it was solicited by editor george julian houtain to be published as a serial .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mythos_Collector">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Mythos Collector</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Brian Lingard Brian Lingard Fanzine English Dark Tree Press Irregular June 2001 Final Publication December 2004 was a sporadically-released fanzine which ran for six issues between June 2001 and December 2004. Focussing on many aspects of Lovecraftiana, it featured a mix of interviews, fiction, non-fiction, buyer's guides, and reviews. Published by Dark Tree Press, it was edited for its entire run by Brian Lingard, and cover art for later issues was supplied by Cthulhu Mythos regular Allen Koszowski . Issue Guide 2001 Summer (June) 2002 Winter (February) Summer (June) Fall (November) 2003 Spring (May) 2004 Winter (December) Gallery External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Ballad_of_Black_Bart">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Ballad of Black Bart</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The stranger is a monstrosity disguised as a man who uses the power of the necromicon against its enemies . Despite being filled with lead, the stranger is unharmed and uses an arcane ritual to tear away bart's soul . A man named doc jones counters his magic with a protective spell, casting the entity back to the abyss from wherece it came .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#James_Ambuehl"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Nightscapes #16</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2006</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cities_in_Ruin">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cities in Ruin</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nikki Valens Fantasy Flight Games Publication Date 2017 Board game Eldritch Horror is an expansion set for the Eldritch Horror Cthulhu Mythos board game. Designed by Nikki Valens and featuring artwork by Cristi Balanescu, it was published by Fantasy Flight Games in 2017 . Overview External Links "Secrets Lie in Ruins Old and New" at the Fantasy Flight Games website Gallery References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Larry_Todd">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Larry Todd</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Larry S. Todd Pseudonym(s) Lou P. de Loupe Connection to the Mythos Artist Birth Date 6 April 1948 Buffalo, New York, USA United States Notable Works " Shadows From the Abyss " is an American cartoonist and illustrator, the majority of whose works have appeared through his involvement with the small press "underground comix" scene. He adapted the Howard Phillips Lovecraft novella The Shadow Out of Time into a comic strip. This was published as " Shadow From the Abyss " in August 1972 in the indie comic book Skull Comics #5. Notable Works " Shadow From the Abyss "</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>New York USA Buffalo</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Larry S. Todd</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Lou P. de Loupe</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isKnownForR>Shadows From the Abyss</ex:isKnownForR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>6 April 1948</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Hole_in_the_Wall_Gang">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crossovers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Hole in the Wall Gang</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The real ghostbusters is an episode of the animated series written by science fiction author david gerrold and first aired in 1987 . It is one of three episodes of the series connected to the cthulhu mythos . The episode takes place in the town of arkham , massachusetts .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Call_of_Cthulhu:_The_Card_Game">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Call of Cthulhu: The Card Game</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Living card game is a card-based game published by fantasy flight games before being replaced by arkham horror: the card game . Game involves two players, each in possession of a 60-card faction deck, who take turns playing cards in an effort to win rounds . Whoever wins the majority of three rounds wins the game .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2009</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._G._Wells">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosAdjacentAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>H. G. Wells</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Herbert g. wells (1866 - 1946) was a british author who contributed to a variety of genres . His most famous story, the time machine, was the first major work of science fiction to depict a time-traveling device . Some of wells' story lines and themes are paralleled in the cthulhu mythos .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Plateau_of_Tsang">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Plateau of Tsang</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is an area in central tibet, now part of the ü-tsang region . Was incorporated into the cthulhu mythos by frank belknap long in his novel . Explorers like steelbrath, talman, mcwilliams, henley and holmes died trying to cross it .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Plateau</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaugnar_Faugn"/>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mi-Go"/>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>his cultists</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Central Asia</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_from_the_Hills"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#X-Men">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OrganisationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdfs:label>X-Men</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The are a fictional team in the prime reality of the . Marvel universe of comics . They are a team of superheroes made of up of mutants (homo superior) they have defended humans from mutant supremacists, terrorists, killers, and criminals .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Archangel</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Beast</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Cyclops</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Iceman</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Jean Grey</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Jubilee</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Magneto</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Professor Charles Xavier</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Psylocke</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Rogue</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Shadowcat</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Storm</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasNotableMemberO>Wolverine</ex:hasNotableMemberO>
    <ex:hasTypeO>team</ex:hasTypeO>
    <ex:wasCreatedBynO>Jack Kirby</ex:wasCreatedBynO>
    <ex:wasCreatedBynO>Stan Lee</ex:wasCreatedBynO>
  </rdf:Description>
