  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Winter_Tide">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Winter Tide</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Focuses on aphra marsh, a deep one woman and one of only two survivors of innsmouth . In this book, she continues working with sympathetic fbi agent ron spector . This time she's trying to learn whether russian agents have used miskatonic's resources .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ruthanna_Emrys"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>368</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>The Innsmouth Legacy</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2017</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Stars_Are_Always_Right">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Stars Are Always Right</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Charles Lovecraft English Wildside Press Weirdbook Annual 2 date February 2019 " , or, The Evening Not Nice " is a poem by Australian Charles Lovecraft . Synopsis A trip through the galaxy terminating at the sunken city of R'lyeh . History "" was published in Weirdbook Annual 2 by Wildside Press in 2019.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Charles_Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Weirdbook Annual 2</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#When_She_Was_Very_Tired">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>When She Was Very Tired</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Lisa Cunningham English April Moon Books The Call of Poohthulhu date March 2022 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by Lisa Cunningham which blends the world of A. A. Milne's children's character Winnie-the-Pooh with the horror of H. P. Lovecraft . It was published in the April Moon Books anthology The Call of Poohthulhu in May 2022. Synopsis Kanga, an unwitting avatar of the Outer God Shub-Niggurath , lives her life quietly in Hundred Acre Woods, watching her friends re-enact the stories of "the Authors" daily, and listening to the whispering voices in her head. When her child Roo is mortally wounded in an accident, Kanga lets the little being die rather than heal it again, and with this act her consciousness drifts back to rejoin its source.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Lisa Cunningham</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_Poohthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 2022</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yokoth_%26_Glythur">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yokoth &amp; Glythur</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Yokoth and her offspring, the "faceless hordes", destroyed or consumed most of their universe, with the assistance of their offspring . In 1925 a rogue group of men of letters opened a rift to that universe, desiring to bring the old ones through to "cleanse the world of hate" yokoth came through and devoured most of the group, before they were able to close the rift and bound her . In</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Transition_of_Titus_Crow">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#BrianLumleyWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CrossroadPress"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Transition of Titus Crow</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Titus crow of the cthulhu mythos is a novel by brian lumley . Follows on from the events of the first book, the burrowers beneath . Crow managed to escape by unlocking the code of de marigny's clock .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United Kingdom</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror Cosmic Horror Action Adventure Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Titus_Crow"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1975</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Broodling_of_Eihort">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Broodling of Eihort</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Eihort"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Child of the Kingdom</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Children of the Bargain</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Labyrinth Kin</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Pale Ones</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Pale Spawn</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>White Death</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Broodlings of eihort are gestalt beings made up of millions of the tiny white spidery brood of eihort . When combined, broodling looks like a deathly pale, hairless human of average size . When attacked, each damage causes bits of broodling to come apart, falling off as globby masses of the white spidery brood . If its form is "killed", a broodling melts down into millions of individuals white spiders</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Before_the_Storm"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ramsey_Campbell"/>
  </rdf:Description>
