    <rdfs:label>Shaggai dog</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A is a sapient alien species created by darrell schweitzer for his comedic short story "the last horror out of arkham" their name is a play on "shaggy dog story", an expression used to refer to an intentionally pointless narrative . Their name is a play on "shaggy dog story", an expression used to refer to an intentionally pointless narrative .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Last Horror Out of Arkham</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Darrell_Schweitzer"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Baby_Its_Cold_Inside">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleComicBookAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Baby It's Cold Inside</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft (original story) English Genre(s) Horror Vault of Horror #17 date February 1951 " " is a story which appeared in The Vault of Horror #17 comic book in February 1951. It is an adaptation of H. P. Lovecraft 's short story " Cool Air ".</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Vault of Horror #17</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 1951</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Bel_Yarnak">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Bel Yarnak</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dis was a city created by h. p. lovecraft 's friend henry kuttner for his 1937 short story " the eater of souls " it was possessed of many silver spires and a single black minaret within which dwelled the wizards who acted as the priesthood of the city .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Jest_of_Droom-Avista"/>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>Towers</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:hasNotableFeatureL>minarets</ex:hasNotableFeatureL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Galaks</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>An unnamed planet in the The Gulf of Yarnak</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Betelgeuse system</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Eater_of_Souls"/>
    <ex:wasDestroyedOnL>Unknown but now the dead city of Dis</ex:wasDestroyedOnL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shining_Trapezohedron">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MysticalArtefacts"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shining Trapezohedron</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The trapezohedron serves as a window on all of space and time . Its wielder would summon nyarlathotep in his avatar as the eponymous haunter of the dark . In exchange for horrible sacrifices, the haunter of the dark would reveal other worlds and arcane knowledge .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Re-Animator_Productions">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Publishers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Re-Animator Productions</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>United States Horror http://www.re-animatorfilms.com/index.html is, according to their , " the entity that manages all Re-Animator films, products, and related interests. " It also manages public speaking appearances by Re-Animator film series producer Brian Yuzna .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://www.re-animatorfilms.com/index.html</ex:hasWebsiteR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Render_of_the_Veils">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RamseyCampbellWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Render of the Veils</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Kevin gillman is an average man with an interest in witchcraft . He allows stranger henry fisher to share his taxi for convenience . Gillman agrees to accompany fisher home to perform an unspecified ritual . He is driven insane by the ability to see in all dimensions .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ramsey_Campbell"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United Kingdom</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror Short Fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Inhabitant_of_the_Lake"/>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Less Welcome Tenants Cold Print</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1964</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
