    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Confession of Unfaith</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft United States English (original) French Genre(s) Non-fiction SSR Publications Selected Essays Volume I Date of writing February 1922 date December 1952 " " is a short non-fiction piece by the late American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Although it was written in February 1922, it did not see until December 1952, when it was included in the George T. Wetzel -edited collection Selected Essays Volume I . It has been reprinted a handful of times, and has also been translated into French . History Selected Essays Volume I (1952) To Quebec and the Stars (1976) Howard Phillips Lovecraft 3 (1992, 2016) Miscellaneous Writings (1995) References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Non-fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Selected_Essays_Volume_I"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>December 1952</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
    <ex:wasWrittenOnW>February 1922</ex:wasWrittenOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Call_To_Cthulhu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Storybooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Call To Cthulhu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Norm Konyu Norm Konyu English Titan Nova Release Date December 12, 2023 48 is a children's book published by Titan Nova in 2023. It was written and illustrated by Norm Konyu. Synopsis Cthulhu receives a phone call at the middle of the night, with the unknown caller insulting him and various stories from the Cthulhu Mythos . Afterwards, Cthulhu gets annoyed and decides to change his number again so no more humans can bother him. The stories referenced in this book include: " The Rats in the Walls " " The Nameless City " The Shadow Over Innsmouth " Nyarlathotep " " The Colour Out of Space " " The Cats of Ulthar " At the Mountains of Madness " The White Ship " " History of the Necronomicon " " The Terrible Old Man " " The Dunwich Horror " " Dagon " The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath " The Call of Cthulhu " Behind the Mythos Although some elements in the book do come off as a more lighthearted affectionate parody, it appears to have been primarily written due to the 's distaste towards H. P. Lovecraft 's racism .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Norm Konyu</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>48</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2023 December 12</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
