    <rdfs:label>Pnakotic Manuscripts</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>Etheldreda ( Demonbane )</ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>Pnakotic Fragments</ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The (or pnakotic fragments ) is a fictional grimoire from the cthulhu mythos . It first appeared in h. p. lovecraft's short story " polaris " . It was extensively expanded upon by . Lin carter .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceA>The Other Gods The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath The Whisperer in Darkness At the Mountains of Madness The Horror in the Museum Through the Gates of the Silver Key Out of the Aeons The Shadow Out of Time The Haunter of the Dark The Diary of Alonzo Typer The Return of Hastur The Whippoorwills in the Hills The Seal of R'lyeh The Acolyte of the Flame</ex:hasAppearanceA>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Polaris"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fred_Chappell">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Fred Chappell</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>4 January 2024</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Fred Davis Chappell Birth Date May 28, 1936 Canton, North Carolina, USA Death Date 4 January 2024 Greensboro, North Carolina, USA United States Notable Works Dagon  Fred Davis Chappell (28 May 1936 - 4 January 2024) is an American writer and poet who served as poet laureate of North Carolina, USA from 1997–2002 and taught English at the University of North Carolina for 40 years. His novel Dagon , which was named Best Foreign Book of 1968 by the Académie Française, blends the Southern Gothic genre with hints of the Cthulhu Mythos --opening with a quote from H. P. Lovecraft , "Ph'nglui mglw'nafh Cthulhu R'lyeh wgah'nagl ftagn." Chappell has written other fiction related to the Mythos, including the short stories "The Adder" and "In the Rue d'Auseil". Selected Works Novels Dagon (1968) Short Fiction "The Adder" (1989) "In the Rue d'Auseil" (2001) External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Canton North Carolina</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Fred Davis Chappell</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isKnownForR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dagon"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1936 May 28</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Daughter_of_Hounds">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CaitlinRKiernanWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Daughter of Hounds</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A 2007 novel by caitlin r. kiernan that explores the subterranean world of new england ghouls . It includes characters first encountered in kiernan's threshold (2001) and low red moon (2003) . Each has a secret origin that binds their fates together, and a special power that makes them a target of subterranean forces .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caitlin_R._Kiernan"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>January 2007</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Cats_of_Ulthar">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Cats of Ulthar</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The tryoutis a short story written by american fantasy writer h. p. lovecraft in june 1920 . In the tale, an unnamed narrator relates the story of how a law forbidding the killing of cats came to be in a town called ulthar .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Fantasy short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Tryout"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 1920</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
