    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Parapsychologist's Handbook</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A New Occupation for Call of Cthulhu Chris Jerome Simon Monk Jessica Billman Cover Artist Meghan McLean United States English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Chaosium Release Date November 2003 112 The : A New Occupation for Call of Cthulhu is a supplementary sourcebook for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Overview The contains background information on running both parapsychologists as player characters and a parapsychology-themed campaign. Included are a potted history of the discipline and a rundown on the basic tenets, a guide to common phenomena, plot seeds, new psychic feats, and a list of recommended reading. Behind the Mythos Running to a total of 112 , the Parapsychologist’s Handbook was written by Chris Jerome with cover art supplied by Meghan McLean and interior work by Simon Monk and Jessica Billman. It was published in November 2003 by Chaosium in both softcover and digital download formats.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Chris Jerome</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
