    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>27 October 1990</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Aphoom-Zhah">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Aphoom-Zhah</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Cold Flame The Flame Thing Lord of the Flame The Gray Flaming One The Gray Flame</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Spawned by cthugha on "a dim world" in orbit around the star fomalhaut . First appeared in short story " the acolyte of the flame " . Revered by the gnoph-keh, the voormi and his own race of minions: the spectral ylidheem .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isLocatedAtC>Mount Yarak</ex:isLocatedAtC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Acolyte_of_the_Flame"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Howling_Synchronicities">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Howling Synchronicities</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A man who has been used his whole life as a tool to aid in the return of the old ones watches from orbit as the world devolves into madness . However, he also witnesses the sparks of sanity which hide away to one day resurrect the human race .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Konstantine_Paradias"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Who_Stole_the_Necronomicon%3F">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Who Stole the Necronomicon?</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The arkham detective is a noir novella by american and screenwriter byron craft . The sixth in his arkham detective of mythos stories, it was self-published in 2020 . The detective is forced to face down a deranged descendant of the witch keziah mason, the actual ghost of mason herself, and the outer god azathoth .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Byron_Craft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Arkham_Detective"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2020</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Overcome">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Overcome</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jason Vandee English Simian Publishing Apotheosis: Stories of Human Survival After the Rise of the Elder Gods date October 2015  " " is a Lovecraftian short story by American Jason Vanhee. It was published in the Jason Andrew -edited thematic anthology Apotheosis: Stories of Human Survival After the Rise of the Elder Gods by Simian Publishing in October 2015. Synopsis Amongst the wreckage of a ruined city, a group of believers attempt to attend church, even although humankind's new masters forbid religion. Standing firm in the face of the human collaborators which deny them access, the group's sanity is shattered by the sudden appearance of one of the masters, which leaves them easy prey for the mortal enforcers.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Jason Vandee</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Apotheosis:_Stories_of_Human_Survival_After_the_Rise_of_the_Elder_Gods"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2015</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#These_Deities_of_Rarest_Air">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>These Deities of Rarest Air</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>W. H. Pugmire United States English Dark Regions Press Gathered Dust and Others date September 2011 " : A Prose-Poem Sequence " is a series of thematically-linked Lovecraftian vignettes and short stories by the late American W. H. Pugmire . It was published in his collection Gathered Dust and Others by Dark Regions Press in 2011. Amongst the Cthulhu Mythos staples mentioned in the seventeen sections are The Strange Dark One (one of Nyarlathotep's sobriquets), N'Kai , Innsmouth , the Al-Azif , ghouls , Shoggoths , De Vermis Mysteriis , Cultes des Goules , and Kingsport .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#W._H._Pugmire"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Gathered Dust</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Others</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>September 2011</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Planetfall_on_Yuggoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Planetfall on Yuggoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story was first published in the lovecraft tribute fanzine hpl in 1972 . It covers the landing of an expedition on pluto . One of the crewmen sent back a garbled radio message about " living fungi" the entire occurrence was dismissed as one of the perils of space travel .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#James_Wade"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>HPL</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 1972</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Elder_Spirit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Elder Spirit</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sociocultural Characteristics Extraterrestrial Notable members The Sleeper Beneath the Sands Real World Information Created by Marvel Comics The Elder Spirits are a Lovecraftian extra-terrestrial race from the fictional universe of Marvel by Marvel Comics . Background The Elder Spirits are a race of invisible shapeless aliens who crossed the void of space to reach Earth . For a time they ruled the Earth but upon the rise of man in Lemuria they retreated to Thuria and when man established its dominion there, they went into hiding, waiting for the time to reestablish their rule over the Earth. During the Hyborian Age , one of them which was known by the locals as the "Sleeper Beneath the Sands" was later encountered by Conan .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Marvel_Comics"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Esther_Phillips">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSRelatives"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Esther Phillips</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>29 August 1852</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Wife of Israel Cole, she gave birth to six children: Mary, Leonard, William, Olney P., Waite Ann, and an unnamed daughter.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isRelativeToR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1803</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Watchers_Out_of_Time_and_Others">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#AugustDerlethWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Watchers Out of Time and Others</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The stories were actually written by derleth, inspired by notes left by lovecraft after his death in 1937 . Many of the stories included had been previously published by arkham house in earlier anthologies . Initial run of 5,070 copies was given by derleth's specialist arkham house in 1974 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#August_Derleth"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1974</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fangarmer">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Fangarmer</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Tore Aurstad Norway Norwegian Genre(s) Horror Cappelen Damm Release Date 2016 286 is a Cthulhu Mythos novel by Norwegian Tore Aurstad. A sequel to Lovecraft 's " The Call of Cthulhu ", the name translates roughly to "tentacles". Synopsis Publication History was published in 2016 by Cappelen Damm. It runs to a total of 286 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Tore Aurstad</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>Norway</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>286</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>Norwegian</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2016</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Vikings_Doom">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Viking's Doom</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The tattered lady is a short cthulhu mythos story by canadian troy young . It is the fifth episode of book 2 in the nyarlathotep cycle .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Troy_Young"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Nyarlathotep_Cycle"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Other:_Encounters_with_the_Cthulhu_Mythos_Book_2"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2020</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Philip_Marsh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Philip Marsh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Pseudonym(s) Philip Obed Marsh Phil Marsh P. Marsh Connection to the Mythos Author Poet Amateur publisher is an author, poet and amateur publisher who works in the Lovecraftian and weird fiction genres. He has written several short pieces about the Cthulhu Mythos ; many of these have been in collaboration with Tani Jantsang . Marsh is also credited as publisher of the Cthulhu Cultus fanzine for the entirety of its run; however, given that this was described by Associate Editor James Ambuehl as " a bare-bones photocopied affair with no uniform print-style " it is uncertain what publication process was involved. Selected Bibliography Publisher Cthulhu Cultus (1995-2001)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>P. Marsh</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Phil Marsh</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Philip Obed Marsh</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Amateur publisher</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Poet</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_in_the_Stable">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Horror in the Stable</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>R. c. mulhare's short story was published in the anthology cthulhu christmas special and other lovecraftian yuletide tales in november 2017 . On christmas eve, dr. west is called to attend two badly-injured small children, molly and mickey dolan, who have been struck by an automobile . Deducing that the boy has little chance of survival, he nevertheless injects them both with his reagent under the gui</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#R._C._Mulhare"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Cthulhu Christmas Special</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Other Lovecraftian Yuletide Tales</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Void_%282016_film%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MediaAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Void (2016 film)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The void is a 2016 supernatural horror film from writers and directors steven kostanski and jeremy gillespie . Premise and imagery heavily influenced by elements of the cthulhu mythos .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Steven Kostanski Jeremy Gillespie</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>Canada</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror Supernatural Horror Mystery</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dora_McCain">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dora McCain</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shub-Niggurath"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dora is a beautiful young girl with long blonde hair who is apparently in her middle teens . She lives in a rickety old country shack with her father and at least four siblings . Her mother died when she was twelve, and a few weeks later she made the acquaintance of mother shub, a crazy old woman who lived deep in the forest . Mother shub taught her how to mix potions, make prophecies and even command the animals of the woods on occasion . When she</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Out of Her Gourd (2018)</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Seduced (1998)</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Song_for_Granite_Khronos">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Song for Granite Khronos</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Aaron Besson United States English Genre(s) Weird fiction Martian Migraine Press Chthonic: Weird Tales of Inner Earth date February 2018  " " is a short Lovecraftian story by American Aaron Besson. Synopsis A veteran sewer worker inducts a new start into the secrets which lie below the streets, explaining how they must work as caretakers of the bodies of dead primordial giants which lie petrifying in the bowels of the Earth. History "A Song for Granitte Khronos" was published in the thematic anthology Chthonic: Weird Tales of Inner Earth in February 2018. Behind the Mythos Although containing no direct references to either the works of H. P. Lovecraft or the greater Cthulhu Mythos , the entities described in "" and their negative effect on humanity even while in a death-like slumber is highly reminiscent of certain of Lovecraft's works, particularly " The Call of Cthulhu ".</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Aaron Besson</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Chthonic: Weird Tales of Inner Earth</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ramsey_Campbell">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ramsey Campbell</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>British horror writer ramsay campbell is considered by many to be one of the great masters of horror fiction . His early work was greatly influenced by the work of h. p. lovecraft . In 1973, he set out to be as unlike lovecraft as possible with the collection demons by daylight .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#England Liverpool</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>British</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Carl Dreadstone</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Jay Ramsay</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>Montgomery Comfort</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://www.ramseycampbell.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1946 4 January</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Johnathan_Orton">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Johnathan Orton</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>1926</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Avery Imports</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Silver Twilight Lodge</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Phillip Avery</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as phillip avery 1926 arkham , massachusetts . Created by peter j. evans, who later went by the name phillip avery . Appears in the 2013 horror novel feeders from within .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Feeders_from_Within"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Peter_J._Evans"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Solar_System">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Planets"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stars"/>
    <rdfs:label>Solar System</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Many of the planets in our are referenced in h. p. lovecraft's cthulhu mythos . Lovecraft was a passionate amateur astronomer and enjoyed inserting references to celestial bodies into his tales . At some point in time, mercury will be home to an intelligent species of "bulbous vegetable entities"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>star system</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Milky Way Galaxy</ex:isLocatedAtL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Bolton">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Bolton</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Incorporated in 1738, it has never been a large place; censuses from 1900 to 1940 each recorded a population in the 700s . In lovecraft's fiction appears first and most prominently in lovecraft's " herbert west--reanimator "</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>City</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Massachusetts"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>United States</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West--Reanimator"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Coleopteran">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Coleopteran</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>The Great Race of Yith</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Beetle Race</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sociocultural Characteristics Also known as The Beetle Race Earth (in the future) The Great Race of Yith Real World Information First appearance HPL : The Shadow Out of Time EXP : Malleus Monstrorum Created by Howard Phillips Lovecraft Following their mind transfer from their conic bodies to the beetle race , the Great Race would inhabit these new bodies. A member of this new Great Race of Yith is a hive-mind of thousands of coleopterans ( EXP : Malleus Monstrorum ) Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Malleus_Monstrorum"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shadow_Out_of_Time"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_City">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The City</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here H. P. Lovecraft United States English (original) French The Tryout date October 1919 " " is a poem by the late American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . It was first published in the October 1919 edition of amateur press magazine The Vagrant ; it has since been reprinted numerous times, and has also been translated into French . Synopsis The nine five-line verses describe the narrator's admiration for a long-abandoned city, and his dawning realisation of the terrifying calamity which befell the place. History Something About Cats and Other Pieces (1949) Weird Tales (1950, 1951) Collected Poems (1963) The World of H. P. Lovecraft (1971) Fungi from Yuggoth and Other Poems (1971) The Fantastic Poetry (1990) The Ancient Track: The Complete Poetical Works of H. P. Lovecraft (2001, 2013) Essais - Correspondance - Poésie - Révisions (2021) Write Like Hell: Lovecraft in a Time of Madness (2021) References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Tryout"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 1919</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
