  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dead_Mans_Tongue">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dead Man's Tongue</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The dark rites of cthulhu was published in the anthology the dark rites of cthulhu by april moon books in march 2014 . The story centers on an encounter with a rolang, a desiccated undead servitor with a killer temperament .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Josh_Reynolds"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dark_Rites_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Man-Bat">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Man-Bat</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Man-bats are a fictional race in the marvel universe which first appeared in 1983 in issue #153 of the 1st volume of the conan the barbarian comic book series . They were the ancient enemies of the bird-men of the floating city of akah ma'at, with whome they waged war for centuries .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Conan the Barbarian Vol 1 #153</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>John Buscema</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Michael Fleisher</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Other_Gods">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Other Gods</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the outsider" is a short story written by american horror writer h. p. lovecraft on august 14, 1921 . It was first published in the november 1933 issue of the fantasy fan . Barzai the wise is a high priest and prophet greatly learned in the lore of the "gods of earth", or the great ones . He attempts to climb the mountain of hatheg-kla in order to look upon their faces . But he finds that they are not there alone</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lake_of_Hali">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lake of Hali</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a cloud-lake near the city of carcosa on a world near the star aldebaran in the hyades . When the spawn of cthulhu wake and thrash about in the lake it is called "the time of the frothing" hastur is said to be "the sleeper beneath the lake"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>De Marigny's Clock</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Whisperer in Darkness The Isle of Dark Magic</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Hastur ( AWD )</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>The Spawn of Cthulhu (source)</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Somewhere in the Hyades star cluster</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_King_in_Yellow"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nug-Soth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nug-Soth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>In the story, is a magician who served "the dark conquerors" around 16,000 ad . They were the victim of a mind transfer with a member of the great race of yith . Their consciousness was sent back to 150,000,000 bc to meet with peaslee .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shadow_Out_of_Time"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Pickmans_Model">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Pickman's Model</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story revolves around a bostonian painter named richard upton pickman . Pickman's aesthetic principles of horror resemble those in lovecraft's essay . The narrator is taken on a tour of pickman's gallery, hidden away in a slum .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jupiter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Planets"/>
    <rdfs:label>Jupiter</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>Ylidiomph</ex:hasAlternativeNamesL>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The shadow out of time is the largest planet in the solar system . Referred to repeatedly in lovecraft's fiction . Also known as ylidiomph .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>Beyond the Wall of Sleep Through the Gates of the Silver Key The Shadow Out of Time</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Planet</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Solar_System"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Xena">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Xena</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Warrior Princess</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The warrior princess is a fictional character created by robert tapert and john schulian in 1995 . From 1995-2001 she starred as the protagonist of her own spin-off television show, : warrior princess . In 2008, dynamite entertainment published its first crossover starring and the mythos in the form of the necronomicon ex-mortis .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Army_of_Darkness"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Xena"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Army of Darkness: What...Again</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Xena: Forever... And A Day</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Xena: Why Not</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Warrior Princess ( Hercules S01E09)</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>John Schulian</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Robert Tapert</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gareth_Ryder-Hanrahan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gareth Ryder-Hanrahan</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Games designer Ireland Ireland Roleplaying games is an Irish games designer and author best known for his work in the pen-and-paper roleplaying game . His gaming material credits include supplements for Pelgrane Press 's Trail of Cthulhu and The Yellow Sign , Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu , and line development of The Laundry for Cubicle 7 , a roleplaying game based on Charles Stross 's humorous Cthulhu Mythos series The Laundry Files . In addition to these works, he has also written pieces for franchise roleplaying games such as Conan the Barbarian , Babylon 5 , and Middle Earth . Selected Works Call of Cthulhu Verboten! Operation: FAUST (2002) World War Cthulhu: The Darkest Hour (2013) Trail of Cthulhu Arkham Detective Tales (2009, 2010) Cthulhu Apocalypse (2015) Cthulhu City (2017) The Yellow Sign Black Star Magic (unknown year) Miscellaneous Stealing Cthulhu (2011, annotations) External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#Ireland</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>http://example.org/lovecraft#Ireland</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Games designer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kaiju_Girls_Black">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crossovers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosFilmAndTelevision"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Kaiju Girls Black</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Japan japanese is a 2018 japanese animated film directed by shuji katayama . It is a sequel to the kaiju girls anime, a spinoff of the ultra series . The film follows a high school girl named satsuki hiraga as she joins the black stars, an evil group of kaiju girls . She possesses the soul of alien pegassa, giving her the power to open vortexes to a pocket dimension known as the dark zone .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>Japan</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasWriterW>Kento Shimoyama</ex:hasWriterW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>Japanese</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2018 November 23</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Casino_Carcosa">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Casino Carcosa</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mark McLaughlin Michael Sheehan, Jr. English Genre(s) Horror Horrors &amp; Abominations: 24 Tales of the Cthulhu Mythos date December 2018 " " is a short story by Mark McLaughlin and Michael Sheehan, Jr. Synopsis A dying funeral director who secretly murdered his wife embarks on a bucket list trip to Las Vegas after pocketing a trinket from a body in his care. However, the Tattered King wants what is his, and after a nightmarish hallucinatory journey through a very special casino, the man is found dead, although how it occurred is left ambiguous. Characters Mason Schell , a corrupt mortician with a shocking crime on his hands. History "" was published in the 2018 collection Horrors &amp; Abominations: 24 Tales of the Cthulhu Mythos .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_McLaughlin"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Michael Sheehan. Jr.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Abominations: 24 Tales of the Cthulhu Mythos</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Horrors</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>December 2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Deep_Gate">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ArkhamHorrorFiction"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Deep Gate</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Behind the mythos is a novella written by fantasy flight games . It was first published as a hardback novella by fantasy flight games in june 2018 as part of their arkham horror fiction line of mythos-related literature . The antagonists of are the aquatic deep ones, despite silas himself being a hybrid member of the species .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chris_A._Jackson"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Action Adventure Horror Mystery</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_Horror_Fiction"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2018 17 June</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Koth-Shugoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Koth-Shugoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>ADJ</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>DC Comics : Dark Giants (aka</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Elder Gods</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Many-Sided Ones)</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Creeping Abyss</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Patrick olliffe is a great old one ( dark giant ) created by dc comics . He first appeared in " lost in memory ", spectre annual vol. 3 #1 (november, 1995), written by john ostrander and penciled by patrick olliffe .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Lost in Memory ( Spectre Annual Vol. 3 #1 )</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>John Ostrander</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Patrick Olliffe</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Joyce_Carol_Oates">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Critics"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosInspiredAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Joyce Carol Oates</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Oates is the winner of the 1969 national book award for her novel them . She has declared herself to be a longtime fan of h. p. lovecraft . Some of her short stories have been included in anthologies of lovecraftian fiction .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>New York USA Lockport</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Critic</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Editor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>16 June 1938</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Cairn_on_the_Headland">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RobertEHowardWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Cairn on the Headland</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A struggle between norse paganism and celtic christianity is given a lovecraftian twist . Two american academics, james o'brien and ortali, visit grimmin's cairn, a centuries-old monument at clontarf, near dublin, ireland . Ortali coerces o'brien into a plan to loot the historical site for treasure .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Robert_E._Howard"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Strange_Tales"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>January 1933</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Slaves_of_the_Flame_Undying">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Slaves of the Flame Undying</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The cult dates back to pre-roman egypt, where a secret priesthood worshiped cthugha under the name kathigu-ra . The most fanatical cult members are often marked with symbols sacred to cthugha . The cult continues with its activities to this day, doing everything possible not to attract attention and not carry out risky actions .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#hasGrandMotherR">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label>hasGrandMotherR</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#hasGrandChild"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hyperborea">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hyperborea</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The hyperborean continent is an imaginary prehistoric land created by clark ashton smith as a setting for the hyperborean cycle of stories . The name, meaning "beyond the north wind", is taken from greek mythology, where it appears as a land far to the north . Locations mhu thulan mhu thulan is a province in northern, separated from the rest of the realm by a mountain range .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL>The Mound (unnamed) At the Mountains of Madness Through the Gates of the Silver Key Out of the Aeons The Testament of Athammaus The Weird of Avoosl Wuthoqquan The Door to Saturn The Ice-Demon The Seven Geases The White Sybil The Dark Eidolon The Coming of the White Worm The Scroll of Morloc The Acolyte of the Flame The Flame in the Ice</ex:hasAppearanceL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Continent</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tsathoggua"/>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Voormis</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Tale_of_Satampra_Zeiros"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Vermont">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdfs:label>Vermont</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>'s population in 1930, the year lovecraft wrote his story, was 359,611 . 's largest city at the time was burlington, with 24,789 residents . 's capital is montpelier, which then had 7,837 people .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Whisperer_in_Darkness"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>State</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>United States</ex:isLocatedAtL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#A_Redress_for_Andromeda_%282001%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CaitlinRKiernanWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>A Redress for Andromeda (2001)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"a redress for andromeda (2001)" is a short story by caitlin r. kiernan . It first appeared in october dreams: a celebration of halloween, 2000 . The story is about a mysterious house on the coast of northern california . "a redress for andromeda" was reprinted in the weird: a compendium .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caitlin_R._Kiernan"/>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dandridge_Cycle"/>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>October Dreams: A Celebration of Halloween</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>January 2000</ex:isPublishedAsW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hastalyk">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hastalyk</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Bringer of Change</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Lord of Disease</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>the Living Contagion</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Hastalk is a gestalt entity composed of millions of microbial parts . It sweeps from planet to planet, amplifying and altering existing contagions . When a great old one awakens, hastalk could potentially be awakened as well .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Malleus_Monstrorum"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chad_Bowser"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Xitalu">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Xitalu</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Great Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Being of Higher Dimension</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as Being of Higher Dimension Great Old Ones First appearance INFL : " IZOMBIE #22-28 "  is a tentacles, multi-eyed, soul-devouring entity who dwells within dimensions.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>IZOMBIE #22-28</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Horrors_of_the_Trash_Island">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Horrors of the Trash Island</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mark McLaughlin Michael Sheehan, Jr. English Nightmares &amp; Tentacles: 13 Tales Of The Cthulhu Mythos " " is a short story by authors Mark McLaughlin and Michael Sheehan, Jr. Synopsis History "" was published in the collections Nightmares &amp; Tentacles: 13 Tales Of The Cthulhu Mythos and The Prisoner of Carcosa &amp; More Tales Of The Bizarre (2020).</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_McLaughlin"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Michael Sheehan. Jr.</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Nightmares</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Tentacles: 13 Tales Of The Cthulhu Mythos</ex:isPublishedAsW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ambrose_Dexter">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ambrose Dexter</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Haunter_of_the_Dark"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Doctor is a character who is first mentioned in the 1936 short story " the haunter of the dark " robert bloch 's 1950 sequel, " the shadow from the steeple ", expanded this brief mention into a full-fledged character . Dexter is said to be among those "inclined to take much of blake’s diary at its face value"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>The Shadow From the Steeple</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Haunter_of_the_Dark"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
