    <ex:hasAnnotation>Encompasses: Articles including information from the Derleth Cthulhu Mythos ‏‎ Articles including information from the Expanded Cthulhu Mythos ‏ Articles including information from the Greater Cthulhu Mythos Articles including information from the Mythos Influenced Works</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yilla">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Planets"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yilla</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>First appearance EXP : " The Oldest Dreamer " Created by Walter C. DeBill Jr. is a planet inhabited by the ocean dwelling Yorith . It is orbited by the moon Xithor , whose underground caverns are home to the dwarfish and malign Lloervs . ( EXP : " The Oldest Dreamer ", Walter C. DeBill Jr. )</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>The Oldest Dreamer</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Full_Fathom_Five">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Full Fathom Five</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Paul Fricker John Sumrow Lucy Fricker English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Roleplaying game Release Date August 2020 60 is a scenario supplement for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu horror roleplaying game written by British designer Paul Fricker . It was released through DriveThruRPG's Miskatonic Repository initiative in August 2020; both softcover and digital editions were made available. Overview The 60-page book provides a stand-alone scenario complete with pre-generated characters, maps, handouts, and advice for Keepers on how to run the story.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Paul_Fricker"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Roleplaying game</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>60</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 2020</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Qlippoth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Qlippoth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Qlippoths are an eldritch race of monstrous beings, whose sub-species come in a variety of forms with tentacles and fangs . Before there were demons, the ruled the abyss . The have one goal, to regain control of the abyss, exterminate the demons, and wipe out all mortals who can sin .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Pathfinder Roleplaying Game</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Paizo Inc.</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu_%28Jack_Ryan%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Crypt of Cthulhu (Jack Ryan)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Crypt of cthulhu is a novella by american author jack ryan . It consists of four short stories connected by a wraparound story . At the story's conclusion it is revealed that dr. ng is in fact nyarlathotep himself, and that accessing the minds of the comatose patients was a way to decipher the clues left by cthulhu . Gestalt must sacrifice his own life to</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jack_Ryan"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>October 2018</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yegg-Ha">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yegg-Ha</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Lesser Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Faceless One</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The master of the nightgaunts is a faceless bat-winged giant . It was "killed" by roman soldiers near hadrian's wall in britain, c.128 a.d. its connection as master of the nightgaunts is given in the necronomicon .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Descent_into_the_Abyss"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#An_Item_of_Supporting_Evidence"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
  </rdf:Description>
