  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dagon_November-December_1985">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dagon November-December 1985</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various United Kingdom English Carl T. Ford Release Date November 1985 was the tenth issue of the now-defunct fanzine Dagon . It was edited by the late British and occasional Carl T. Ford . Contents (incomplete) "Nearly Human" by Mark Morrison "Crime and Punishment" by K. Bailey "The Horror at Witches Hollow" (Part 1 of 3) by Robert J. Curran "Bugg-Shash the Terrible" (Part 2 of 2) by Andy Bennison</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United Kingdom</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>November 1985</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Rokon">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Rokon</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Relatives Yig (brother) Created by Llewellyn M. Cabos is the god-king of the serpent folk on the planet Zandanua (their place of origin). He is brother to Yig . and his followers constantly war with Nira and Nodens . Behind the Mythos With the description of as "brother" to Yig and the implication that their forms are identical or extremely similar, the further implication from this contribution to the Mythos would be that "Yig" is a member of a race or species and not a unique Great Old One . Following this train of thought, one could posit the same of Cthulhu and Kthanid .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Llewellyn_M._Cabos"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Castle_Freak_%281995_film%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MediaAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Castle Freak (1995 film)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Stuart gordon directed, dennis paoli and gordon screenwrote . Mythos stalwart jeffrey combs in the lead male role and barbara crampton in the lead female role . Remade in 2020, although this version adds in specific references to elements of the cthulhu mythos .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWriterW>http://example.org/lovecraft#Dennis_Paoli http://example.org/lovecraft#Stuart_Gordon</ex:hasWriterW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Outsider"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>November 1995</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Secrets_of_Japan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Books"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Secrets of Japan</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Michael Dziesinski English Call of Cthulhu Chaosium Release Date 2005 360 is an expansion book for the popular Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game by Chaosium . Overview Containing information on how to play games of Call of Cthulhu in modern-day Japan, contains a potted history of the country, a guide to culture and traditions, additional character occupations, spells and combat rules, monsters of Japanese folklore, three stand-alone scenarios, and two flavour stories. Written by Michael Dziesinski , it is a softcover book with full-colour cover and black and white interior, and runs to a total of 360 in length. Publication History First published in 2005 by Chaosium, is currently out of print. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Dziesinski"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>360</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2005</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
