  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Facts_Concerning_the_Late_Arthur_Jermyn_and_His_Family">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Facts Concerning the Late Arthur Jermyn and His Family</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>" the street " is a short story in the horror fiction genre written by h. p. lovecraft in 1920 . First published in the amateur press journal the wolverine in 1921 . Themes of the story are tainted ancestry, knowledge that human understanding finds intolerable .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Wolverine"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>June 1921</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Some_Thoughts_on_H._P._Lovecraft,_the_Cthulhu_Mythos_and_the_State_of_Weird_Fiction">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Some Thoughts on H. P. Lovecraft, the Cthulhu Mythos and the State of Weird Fiction</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Pierre Comtois English Fungoid Press Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex Winter 2000 date December 2000 " " is a short non-fiction piece by American Pierre Comtois . It was published in the final issue of long-running fanzine Chronicles of the Cthulhu Codex in December 2000.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Pierre_Comtois"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chronicles_of_the_Cthulhu_Codex_Winter_2000"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>December 2000</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecrafts_Untold_Stories_2">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lovecraft's Untold Stories 2</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Released on september 13, 2022, the game is available on multiple platforms, including pc (via steam), playstation, xbox, and nintendo switch . The game's art style is a mix of pixel art and hand-drawn visuals, giving it a distinct, eerie aesthetic . The story takes place after the events of the original game, where the protagonists must once again confront the encroaching horrors from beyond the veil of reality .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2022 September 13</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Liao">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MysticalArtefacts"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Liao</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The hounds of tindalos is a fictional substance created by frank belknap long . It is depicted as a drug that allows the user to mentally "travel" through time and space . The great philosopher laozi used it to see the tao, which permeates all things .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasFunctionA>Time-travel</ex:hasFunctionA>
    <ex:hasPlaceOfOriginA>Historic China</ex:hasPlaceOfOriginA>
    <ex:hasTypeA>Magical elixir</ex:hasTypeA>
    <ex:isUsedByA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Halpin_Chalmers"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Hounds_of_Tindalos"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Carl_Fox">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Carl Fox</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Carl Thomas Fox Connection to the Mythos Author Wales, United Kingdom United Kingdom https://fox492.wixsite.com/ctfauthor Carl Thomas Fox is a British author who has written a small number of works set in the expanded Cthulhu Mythos . These have been published in the Rogue Planet Press anthologies Swords Against Cthulhu (2015) and Swords Against Cthulhu II: Hyperborean Nights (2017), and the Lovecraftiana zine. In addition to his works of fiction, he has also penned a number of factual works on a variety of subjects. Selected Works Short Fiction " Fear of the Knight " (2017) External Links Carl Thomas Fox at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database (second entry detailing different works) at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>United Kingdom Wales</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Carl Thomas Fox</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://fox492.wixsite.com/ctfauthor</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ancient_Astronauts">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ancient Astronauts</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A teenage boy is kidnapped by a deranged cult and forced to undergo a mind-transfer . His two best friends must devise a plan to rescue him . Although the cultists are successful in calling forth an elder thing, the teens manage to defeat it and save their friend .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cynthia_Ward"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>February 2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Eye_of_Horus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Eye of Horus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cthulhu mythos anthologyis a short story by sebastian greaves . A yithian on a survey mission takes over the body of a pharaoh in ancient egypt . When the pharaoh is returned to his own body, the only thing he remembers is a mental image of an eye .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sebastian_Greaves"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Cthulhu Mythos Anthology</ex:isPublishedAsW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Wundagore_Mountain">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosInspiredWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RegionsTerritories"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#TechnologicalArtefacts"/>
    <rdfs:label>Wundagore Mountain</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mountain first appeared in 1966 in issue 134 of the first volume of the thor comic series . Created by stan lee and jack kirby . Part of the estate of the high evolutionary who with his partner jonathan drew established a citadel of scientific research . Genetically engineered the "new men", animals with human intelligence .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeA>Mountain</ex:hasTypeA>
    <ex:isLocatedAtA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Earth"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA>Thor Vol 1 134</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA>
    <ex:wasCreatedByA>Jack Kirby</ex:wasCreatedByA>
    <ex:wasCreatedByA>Stan Lee</ex:wasCreatedByA>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Misplaced_Masterpiece_of_Richard_Upton_Pickman">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Misplaced Masterpiece of Richard Upton Pickman</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story is told in the main part through the journal entries of a small-time art dealer who accidentally comes into possession of a previously-unknown painting . As the image begins to entrance him, his newfound paranoia leads him to believe that he is being monitored by government agents who wish to take it from him .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Troy_Young"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Nyarlathotep_Cycle"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Other:_Encounters_with_the_Cthulhu_Mythos_Book_3"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2021</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Swine_Person">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Swine Person</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Swine Folk</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Swine People</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Swine people are a fictional race expanded upon by chaosium in 1995 for the call of cthulhu roleplaying game . They are degenerate race of porcine humanoids, whom dwell underground . Have pig-like ears and snouts, hoofed hind legs, clawed hands, and very pale skin color .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Call of Cthulhu</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_House_on_the_Borderland"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Hope_Hodgson"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#At_Night_I_Dream...">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>At Night I Dream...</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>At Night I Dream... Full story online here Ron Shiflet United States English Publication date April 1998 " At Night I Dream... " is a short poem by American Ron Shiflet . Synopsis The piece is a series of unconnected verses which reference various names and themes of H. P. Lovecraft 's work. Publication History "At Night I Dream..." was published in Nightscapes in April 1998 and again in Imelod #11 in October of the same year.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>April 1998</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Cats_of_River_Street">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CaitlinRKiernanWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Cats of River Street</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>" (1925)" is a short story by caitlin r. kiernan . It first appeared in the july 2014 issue of sirenia digest (#102) the story was reprinted in the anthologies innsmouth nightmares and the year's best dark fantasy &amp; horror: 2015 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Caitlin_R._Kiernan"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sirenia_Digest"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>July 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Australian_H._P._Lovecraft_Centenary_Calendar_1990-91">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Australian H. P. Lovecraft Centenary Calendar 1990-91</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>B. J. Stevens (compiled by) Australia English Terror Australis Release Date August 1990 is a calendar compiled by New Zealand artist, editor and B. J. Stevens . It features artwork provided entirely by Australian artists , an introduction by Leigh Blackmore , and was published by Terror Australis in August 1990. References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>B. J. Stevens</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Australia"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>August 1990</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Space_Eater">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Space Eater</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The space eaters appear as massive luminous beings that can create temporary limbs . They have the ability to "eat through space", which they use to travel between planets . They can bore holes into the skulls of human victims to feed on the victims' brains .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC>Call of Cthulhu</ex:hasAppearanceC>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Space-Eaters"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Belknap_Long"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dead_of_Night">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dead of Night</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Anton zarnak is an occult detective based on river street, new york . He is asked to help her uncle, who has become weak and prematurely aged . After consulting excerpts from the book of iod, he discovers that the monster that don sebastian fears is in fact zushakon .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Anton_Zarnak_%28series%29"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crypt_of_Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>April 1988</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu_Codex_May_1996">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cthulhu Codex May 1996</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Allen Koszowski English Necronomicon Press Release Date May 1996 40 Preceded by January 1994 Followed by August 1996 was the seventh issue of the Necronomicon Press fanzine Cthulhu Codex . Running to a total of 40 , it was edited by Robert M. Price and featured cover art by Allen Koszowski . This issue was the first to have the title changed from The Cthulhu Codex to simply Cthulhu Codex , and the first to be edited by Price. Contents Editorial: From the Scriptorium by Robert M. Price "From Darker Heavens" by Stanley C. Sargent "An Ambient Darkness" by Chad Hensley "Literary Remains" by Mollie L. Burleson " The Baleful God " by Wilum Pugmire " The Star-Seed " by James Ambuehl "The Fillings of the Sky" by D. F. Lewis</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>40</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>May 1996</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dr._Fo-Lan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dr. Fo-Lan</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Doctor fo-lan is a character created by august derleth and mark schorer for their short story " the lair of the star-spawn ". He is incredibly knowledgeable in the matters of the cthulhu mythos and has even mastered the art of astral projection . When the tcho-tchos captured an american explorer named eric marsh and brought him to alaozar, fo-lan convinced them to spare the man's life .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lair_of_the_Star-Spawn"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#August_Derleth"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_Schorer"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gregory">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gregory</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>Early 20th century</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Crawford_Tillinghast"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Early 20th century Providence, Rhode Island Servant Crawford Tillinghast Human First appearance HPL : " From Beyond " Created by H. P. Lovecraft was a servant employed by the scientist Crawford Tillinghast . He was killed and his body disintegrated (along with the housekeeper Mrs. Updike ) by a malevolent alien entity that was summoned as a result of Crawford's experiments involving the opening of dimensional gates. ( HPL : " From Beyond ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#From_Beyond"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sefton_Asylum">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sefton Asylum</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sefton , Massachusetts Asylum Humans Allan Halsey First appearance HPL : " Herbert West--Reanimator " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a mental institution in the fictional town of Sefton , Massachusetts . After being captured in Arkham , the reanimated corpse of Dr. Allan Halsey was kept in the asylum at Sefton where it beat its head against the walls of a padded cell for sixteen years. A group of zombies , further products of Herbert West 's reanimation experiments, then arrived and broke Halsey out of the asylum, killing four attendants while doing so. ( HPL : " Herbert West--Reanimator ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Asylum"/>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Humans Allan Halsey</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Massachusetts"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sefton"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West--Reanimator"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Akurion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalLocations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Akurion</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sarnath Geographical feature First appearance HPL : " The Doom That Came to Sarnath " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a fictional created by the late American author Howard Phillips Lovecraft for his 1920 short story " The Doom That Came to Sarnath ." Overview is the name given by the people of the city of Sarnath to a tall grey rock that served as a tidal marker near the shore of the unnamed lake where Sarnath once stood. ( HPL : " The Doom That Came to Sarnath ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Geographical feature</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sarnath"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Doom_That_Came_to_Sarnath"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Visions_from_Yaddith">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Visions from Yaddith</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The latter a book of dream inspired poems by ariel prescott (18? ?-1927), printed privately in 1927 by charnel house, of london . Most copies were destroyed by prescott's relatives . The poems concern a dream travel to the planet yaddith .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shub-Niggurath_Cycle"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1988</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Obed_Marsh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Obed Marsh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>1878</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Deep Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Marsh was a sea captain from innsmouth . He learned from the inhabitants of a polynesian island a ritual to summon the deep ones .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Shadow_Over_Innsmouth"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#GreatOldOnes">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kthugguol">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>K'thugguol</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ubbo-Sathla"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Grand Shoggoth</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Slime-Thing</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as The Grand Shoggoth The Slime-Thing Created by the Elder Things Ubbo-Sathla Shoggoth First appearance EXP : " The Descent into the Abyss " Created by Lin Carter , a.k.a. the Slime-Thing or the Grand Shoggoth , is a fictional character created by Lin Carter for his short story " The Descent into the Abyss ". It is the oldest and mightiest member of the shoggoth , the first of its kind to have been created, and a servant of the entity Ubbo-Sathla , who the shoggoths adopted as their god. Description Like a typical shoggoth, is described as a large, gelatinous, amoeboid creature with myriads of eyestalks. It dwells deep in the subterranean realm of grey-litten Y'qaa and guards the entrance of the pit inhabited by Ubbo-Sathla.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Descent_into_the_Abyss"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lin_Carter"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Lumley">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftsCoAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>William Lumley</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1960</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Wt was a late associate of lovecraft for whom lovecraft ghostwrote " the diary of alonzo typer " the story was only published after lovecraft's death, in the february 1938 issue of weird tales . He corresponded with lovecraft from 1931 until lovecraft's death, though few of lovecraft's letters to him survive .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>New York Buffalo</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1880</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Order_of_the_Bloated_Woman">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Order of the Bloated Woman</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The order is an ancient cult devoted to a dark goddess . They believe she is an aspect of a primal deity worshiped all over the world . Its rituals are practiced both on the mainland and on some uninhabited islands . Their high priest is a wealthy import/export businessman from shanghai .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shadow">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shadow</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Drakh</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Keepers</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Soldiers of Darkness</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The shadows are a race that is billions of years old . They embrace chaos, seeing it as the universe's supreme force . The shadows have planet killers, called the "death cloud"</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Babylon 5</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#J._Michael_Straczynski"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Station_S">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Station 'S'</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Station 'S' Rachael Randolph Robert Hafferman Mark Lucas Cover Artist Stephanie McAlea United Kingdom English Call of Cthulhu Genre(s) Horror Stygian Fox Release Date 2020 24 Station 'S': An Anomaly in Scotland Heralds Doom for All Mankind is a short scenario supplement for Chaosium 's Call of Cthulhu roleplaying game. Overview Containing a complete stand-alone adventure set during the Second World War, Station 'S' comes with pre-generated characters and statistics for NPCs and monsters, along with a set of schematics and maps. It was written by Rachael Randolph, edited by Chitin Proctor , and features artwork by Stephanie McAlea , Robert Hafferman and Mark Lucas. It was published by third-party content creator Stygian Fox in 2020 and runs to a total of 24 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Rachael Randolph</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United Kingdom</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>24</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Call of Cthulhu</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2020</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPL_Vol._1:_Comic_Adaptations_of_the_Works_of_HP_Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleComicBookAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>HPL Vol. 1: Comic Adaptations of the Works of HP Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft (original stories) Nick O'Gorman (adaptations) Nick O'Gorman Cover Artist Nick O'Gorman English Target Destroyed Comics Release Date 2023 160 is an omnibus collection of Canadian artist Nick O'Gorman 's comic book adaptations of H. P. Lovecraft 's works. It was published through his Target Destroyed Comics label in 2023 after obtaining funding through a successful Kickstarter crowdfunding campaign ; both physical and digital editions were released. Overview Contents Beyond the Wall of Sleep HPL 1920 The Music of Erich Zann Herbert West: Reanimator Yule Horror References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nick_OGorman"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>160</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2023</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Neil_Gaiman">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Neil Gaiman</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author Birth Date 10 November 1960 Portchester, Hampshire, England United Kingdom Horror Fantasy Science Fiction Black Comedy https://www.neilgaiman.com/ Neil Richard MacKinnon Gaiman is a prolific British author of fantasy, horror, science fiction and black comedy, a number of whose works are either set in, or feature connections to, the Cthulhu Mythos . Many of his writings have been adapted for film, television and comic book mediums. Selected Works " I, Cthulhu " (1987) Good Omens (1990) " Only the End of the World Again " (1994) " Shoggoth's Old Peculiar " (1998) " A Study in Emerald " (2003)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#England Hampshire Portchester</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://www.neilgaiman.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>10 November 1960</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Israel_Cole">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSRelatives"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Israel Cole</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>28 January 1886</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Husband of Esther Phillips, he was a farmer in Foster, Rhode Island.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isRelativeToR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1807</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dreams_in_the_Witch_House_%28DART_production%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftCircleAudioAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dreams in the Witch House (DART production)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The dreams in the witch house was created by the h. p. lovecraft historical society as part of their dark adventure radio theatre series . It is an adaptation of the short story of the same name . Available in both compact disc and digital download formats, it comes with the usual selection of period-authentic thematic props .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isBasedOnW>The Dreams in the Witch House</ex:isBasedOnW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#After_the_After_Party">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>After the After Party</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>M. Stern English Rogue Planet Press Lovecraftiana Vol 5, Issue 4 date 2021 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos story by M. Stern , first published in Vol 5, Issue 4 of the Lovecraftiana zine in 2021. Synopsis Lyle, a man besotted with a just-married woman, goes to save his beloved, believing that she is to be a sacrifice in her husband's bizarre ritual. However, he has misread the situation, and both of the newlyweds are willing participants in a plan to unite themselves in blissful eternity. Lyle arrives just in time to be a part of the rituals' completion, and bears witness to the birth of two powerful entities with a complete disdain for the human race. Mythos Connections The components involved in the ritual included a book written by Von Junzt and a sacrificial knife referred to as the "dagger of Sothoth ".</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#M._Stern"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Issue 4</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Lovecraftiana Vol 5</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2021</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Whippoorwills_in_the_Hills">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#AugustDerlethWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Whippoorwills in the Hills</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A man named dan harrop takes possession of a house in the vicinity of arkham and aylesbury . The house used to belong to a man named abel harrop, who disappeared a few weeks earlier . He is kept awake at night by the incessant callings of a flock of whippoorwills . According to local folklore, whippoorwills can capture the soul of a person who's dying .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#August_Derleth"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>September 1948</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
