    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Boat Trip</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The 3rd spectral book of horror stories was published by tickety boo press in 2016 . It is a short story about the cthulhu mythos by british author david a. riley .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_A._Riley"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The 3rd Spectral Book of Horror Stories</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2016</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Howard_Phillips_Lovecraft_1">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Howard Phillips Lovecraft 1</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Philippe Druillet France French Robert Laffont Release Date September 1991 1,174 is a French- collection Lovecraftian fiction and scholarship, mostly the works of H. P. Lovecraft and his friends, but with a handful of more recent authors' works also included. Running to a total of 1,174 , it was published by Robert Laffont in September 1991 . Contents Note: unless otherwise stated, all works are by H. P. Lovecraft Introduction générale by Francis Lacassin Chronologie by Francis Lacassin Le complot des étoiles by Francis Lacassin "Dagon" (" Dagon ") "Nyarlathothep" (" Nyarlathotep ") "La cité sans nom" (" The Nameless City ") "Le molosse" (" The Hound ") "Azathoth" (" Azathoth ") "Le festival" (" The Festival ") "Le descendant" (" The Descendant ") "L'appel de Cthulhu" (" The Call of Cthulhu ") "L'étrange maison haute dans la brume" (" The Strange High House in the Mist ") "La couleur tombée du ciel" (" The Colour Out of Space ") L'affaire Charles Dexter Ward ( The Case of Charles Dexter Ward ) "L'abomination de Dunwich" (" The Dunwich Horror ") Celui qui chuchotait dans les ténèbres ( The Whisperer in Darkness ) Les montagnes hallucinées ( At the Mountains of Madness ) Le cauchemar d'Innsmouth ( The Shadow Over Innsmouth ) "La maison de la sorcière" (" The Dreams in the Witch-House ") "Le monstre sur le seuil" (" The Thing on the Doorstep ") Dans l'abîme du temps ( The Shadow Out of Time ) "Celui qui hantait les ténèbres" (" The Haunter of the Dark ") "Histoire du Necronomicon" (" History of the Necronomicon ") "Cthulhu : un culte en expansion" by Francis Lacassin "Les mangeuses d'espace" by Frank Belknap Long (" The Space-Eaters ") "Les chiens de Tindalos" by Frank Belknap Long (" The Hounds of Tindalos ") "Talion" by Clark Ashton Smith (" The Return of the Sorcerer ") "La pierre noire" by Robert E. Howard (" The Black Stone ") "La chose ailée sur le toit" by Robert E. Howard (" The Thing on the Roof ") "L'héritier des ténèbres" by Clark Ashton Smith (" The Nameless Offspring ") "Le feu d'Asshurbanipal" by Robert E. Howard (" The Fire of Asshurbanipal ") "Ubbo-Sathla" by Clark Ashton Smith (" Ubbo-Sathla ") "Le visiteur venu des étoiles" by Robert Bloch (" The Shambler from the Stars ") "Épouvante à Salem" by Henry Kuttner (" The Salem Horror ") "Au-delà du seuil" by August Derleth (" Beyond the Threshold ") "L'habitant de l'ombre" by August Derleth (" The Dweller in Darkness ") "L'ombre du clocher" by Robert Bloch (" The Shadow from the Steeple ") "Manuscrit trouvé dans une maison abandonnée" by Robert Bloch (" Notebook Found in a Deserted House ") "On rôde dans le cimetière" by J. Vernon Shea (" The Haunter of the Graveyard ") "Sueurs froides" by Ramsey Campbell (" Cold Print ") "La Cité Sœur" by Brian Lumley (" The Sister City ") "Le rempart de béton" by Brian Lumley (" Cement Surroundings ") "Ceux des profondeurs" by James Wade (" The Deep Ones ") "Le retour des Lloigors" by Colin Wilson (" The Return of the Lloigor ") "Répertoire biographique des auteurs" by uncredited "Préface des Premiers contes" by August Derleth "La petite bouteille de verre" (" The Little Glass Bottle ") "La caverne secrète ou L'aventure de John Lee" (" The Secret Cave, or John Lees Adventure ") "Le mystère du cimetière ou La revanche d'un mort" (" The Mystery of the Grave-Yard, or "A Dead Man's Revenge": A Detective Story ") "Le vaisseau mystérieux" (" The Mysterious Ship ") "La bête de la caverne" (" The Beast in the Cave ") "L'alchimiste" (" The Alchemist ") "Notes pour Le cauchemar d'Innsmouth" ("Notes for "The Shadow over Innsmouth"") "Brouillon abandonné pour Le cauchemar d'Innsmouth" ("Discarded Draft of "The Shadow Over Innsmouth"”) "Notes pour Les Montagnes hallucinées" ("Notes for "At the Mountains of Madness"") "Notes pour Dans l'abîme du temps" ("Notes for "The Shadow Out of Time"") "Sur l'authenticité du Necronomicon" "Le livre de raison" The Notes &amp; Commonplace Book Employed by the Late H. P. Lovecraft" "Quelques commentaires sur la fiction interplanétaire" (" Some Notes on Interplanetary Fiction ") "Quelques origines du royaume des fées" (" Some Backgrounds of Fairyland ") "Lord Dunsany et son œuvre" (" Lord Dunsany and His Work ") "Lettre au rédacteur en chef d'All Story Weekly" ("Letter to the Editor of the All-Story Weekly") "Lettre au rédacteur en chef de Weird Tales" ("Letter to the Editor of Weird Tales") "Critique de Ebène et Cristal de Clark Ashton Smith" ("Ebony and Crystal: Poems in Verse and Prose") "L'épidémie du vers libre" (" The Vers Libre Epidemic ") "Ce qui doit se dire en vers" (" What Belongs in Verse ") "La littérature de Rome" (" The Literature of Rome ") "Sur les traces de Poe" (" Homes and Shrines of Poe ") "Winifred Virginia Jackson : une poétesse "différente"" (" Winifred Virginia Jackson: A "Different" Poetess ") "In memoriam : Henry St. Clair Whitehead" (" In Memoriam: Henry St. Clair Whitehead ") "Robert Ervin Howard : 1906-1936" (" Robert Ervin Howard: 1906-1936 ") "Suggestions pour un guide du lecteur" (" Suggestions for a Reading Guide ") Bibliographie References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#France"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>174 1</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>French</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 1991</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Collected_Essays_Volume_4:_Travel">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Collected Essays Volume 4: Travel</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. P. Lovecraft Cover Artist Virgil Finlay United States English Genre(s) Non-fiction Hippocampus Press Release Date !arch 2006 300 is a collection of non-fiction works by the late American Howard Phillips Lovecraft . Edited by leading Lovecraft scholar S. T. Joshi , it was published in paperback and hardcover formats by Hippocampus Press in March 2006; in August 2008, an ebook edition was released . Contents Introduction by S. T. Joshi " The Trip of Theobald " " Vermont—A First Impression " " Observations on Several Parts of America " " Travels in the Provinces of America " " An Account of a Trip to the Antient Fairbanks House, in Dedham, and to the Red House Tavern in Sudbury, in the Province of the Massachusetts-Bay " " An Account of a Visit to Charleston, S. C. " " An Account of Charleston, in His Majty's Province of South-Carolina " A Description of the Town of Quebeck, in New France, Lately added to His Britannick Majesty's Dominions " European Glimpses " with Sonia Greene " Some Dutch Footprints in New England " " Homes and Shrines of Poe " " The Unknown City in the Ocean " " Charleston " " A Descent to Avernus " " Sleepy Hollow To-day " References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Non-fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>300</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>!arch 2006</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
