  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Serpent_Crown">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MysticalArtefacts"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Serpent Crown</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>The Crown of Lemuria</ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>The Helmet of Power</ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>The Helmet of the Ancients</ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>The Seven-Headed Serpent Crown of Lost Lemuria</ex:hasAlternativeNamesA>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional item in the marvel universe which first appeared in 1968 (as the helmet of power) in issue #101 of the 1st volume of the tales to astonish comic book series . It made its first appearance as thein 1969 in issue #9 of the 1st volume of the sub-mariner comic book series .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasFunctionA>Mind control</ex:hasFunctionA>
    <ex:hasTypeA>Mystical artefact</ex:hasTypeA>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA>Tales To Astonish #101</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA>
    <ex:wasCreatedByA>Stan Lee</ex:wasCreatedByA>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Emma_Legrasse">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MagicUsers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Emma Legrasse</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Mad Hatter</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as streetwise, unarmed combat, firearms, teleport, detective, intelligence police human . Created by dan wickline in 2012, first appearing in issue #3 of the 1st volume of grimm fairy tales presents: call of wonderland .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Grimm Fairy Tales Presents: Call of Wonderland Vol 1 3</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Dan Wickline</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Gavin_Inglis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Gavin Inglis</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Games Designer Scotland, United Kingdom United Kingdom http://www.gavininglis.com/about/ is a British author and games designer. Overview has written both short fiction and full-length novels; with regards to the Cthulhu Mythos inspired by the works of H. P. Lovecraft , he has written a number of pieces for Chaosium 's popular horror roleplaying game Call of Cthulhu . Selected Bibliography Alone Against the Flames (2016) Alone Against the Frost (2019)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>Scotland United Kingdom</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://www.gavininglis.com/about/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Games Designer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nightscapes_December_2006">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nightscapes December 2006</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Edward P. Berglund Release Date December 2006 Preceded by October 2006 is the seventeenth and final issue of the sporadically-released online fanzine Nightscapes . Billed as a special Christmas edition, it was edited by the late American and Lovecraft scholar Edward P. Berglund . Contents Fiction "Whispers from the Dark Past" by Phillip A. Ellis "The Cosmic Horror" by Richard F. Searight "The Horror Out of Dunwich" by Glynn Barrass "Night" by Ken Silver " Big Nasty " by Josh Reynolds "Whiteout" by James Ambuehl and E. P. Berglund Parodies "Toho Academy: A Whole New Dimension" by Simon Leo Barber "Scampy, the Very Naughty Christmas Elf" by Todd H. C. Fischer "Yes, Virginia, There Is a Great Cthulhu" by Steven Marc Harris Poetry " Lovecraftian Cliffs Notes for Ech-Pi-El's: The Cats of Ulthar " by Franklyn Searight " Lovecraftian Cliffs Notes for Ech-Pi-El's: The Festival " by Franklyn Searight " Yule-Thoughts in Kingsport " by Ann K. Schwader External Links full issue online at the Nightscapes website</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 2006</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu_Codex_Hallowmas_1997">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Cthulhu Codex Hallowmas 1997</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various Cover Artist Robert H. Knox English Necronomicon Press Release Date November 1997 40 Preceded by Lammas 1997 Followed by Eastertide 1998 is the twelfth issue of the Necronomicon Press fanzine Cthulhu Codex . Edited by Robert M. Price and featuring cover art by Robert H. Knox, it was published in November 1997. Contents Editorial: From the Scriptorium by Robert M. Price "The Pain Eater" by Benjamin Adams "Hall of Terror" by Andy Boot "What If the Dead Are Laughing?" by Darrell Schweitzer "There Is a Pond" by Franklyn Searight "Beneath the Black Obelisk" by Stephen Sennitt "Lamastide" by Frederick Stansfield "Night Lives" by Ann K. Schwader</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>40</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>November 1997</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Something_Eating_at_You">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Something Eating at You</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story is a reimagining of h. p. lovecraft 's 1927 short story " the colour out of space ." It was published in the jesse dedman-edited anthology ancient ones ii in march 2018 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#R._C._Mulhare"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ancient_Ones_II"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>March 2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Snake_of_Many_Colors">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Snake of Many Colors</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Rainbow Serpents</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The snakes of many colors are a fictional race created by marvel comics which were created in 1992 by roy thomas and sal buscema . They made their first appearance in issue #193 of the 1st volume of the savage sword of conan comic book series .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Savage Sword of Conan Vol 1 #193</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Roy_Thomas"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>John Buscema</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_House_Of_The_Ocelot">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The House Of The Ocelot</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>&amp; more lovecraftian nightmares date 2019is a short story by mark . Mclaughlin .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Mark_McLaughlin"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>More Lovecraftian Nightmares</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The House of the Ocelot</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Unthinkable">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Unthinkable</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The story takes place at the end of the cold war, but in an alternative timeline . Technological progress has occurred side-by-side with the exploitation of magic and supernatural creatures . The story involves elements of the cthulhu mythos and has been included in anthologies such as cthulhu 2000: a lovecraftian anthology .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Bruce_Sterling"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>USA</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Science Fiction</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>The Magazine of Fantasy</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>1991</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Bride_of_Slorioth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MysticalArtefacts"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Bride of Slorioth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional item in the Marvel universe which first appeared in 1994 in issue 15 of volume one of the Secret Defenders comic series. Background The was a mystical statue related to the Great Old One , Slorioth . Which permitted the ex-Avenger Dr. Druid to transform Shadowoman's soul into a shadow-form, which had various superhuman abilities. Unknown to Dr. Druid, it also claimed a portion of his own soul, corrupting it into a dark soul.</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chorazin_%28entity%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Chorazin (entity)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cthulhu"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>The Psychic Manifestation of Great Cthulhu</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The chorazin is an avatar of cthulhu created by chaosium for their call of cthulhu roleplaying game . It appears as an ethereal representation of its "parent" entity, but can only make its presence known through the dreams and nightmares of those nearby . Once it reaches a critical mass, it explodes into our dimension in a flash of raw energy .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ye_Booke_of_Monstres_II"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Lovecraft_Tarot">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Lovecraft Tarot</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Daryl l. hutchinson created this unique version of the standard 78-card tarot deck . A second edition was published in 2002 by the now-defunct lovecraftian small press mythos books . All the artwork is by the creator, artist hutchinson, who produced them as a labour of love .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Daryl L. Hutchinson</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Eric Friedman</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>1997</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Out_of_the_Belly_of_Sheol">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Out of the Belly of Sheol</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The prophet jonah finds himself adrift in the middle of the ocean after attempting to ignore his creator's command . When the storm subsides, a colossal being breaches the surface and, recognising jonah's unique gift - to hear the babbling of the many gods across the universe - swallows him whole to act as his new prophet . Inside the belly of the beast, who he soon discovers is great cthulhu himself, he</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>German</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Dark Testament</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2002</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Lovecrafts_Alien_Civilisations:_A_Political_Interpretation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Lovecraft's Alien Civilisations: A Political Interpretation</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>S. T. Joshi United States English Genre(s) Non-fiction Necronomicon Press Selected Papers on Lovecraft date June 1989 " " is a non-fiction work by H. P. Lovecraft scholar S. T. Joshi . It was published in the collection of Joshi's own works Selected Papers on Lovecraft by Necronomicon Press in June 1989.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#S._T._Joshi"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Non-fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Selected_Papers_on_Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>June 1989</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Call_of_the_Deep_%28William_Meikle%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Call of the Deep (William Meikle)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the call of the deep" is a short story by british author william meikle . It was first published in the anthology return of the old ones: apocalyptic lovecraftian horror in 2017 . It was later included in the collection of meikle's own works into the black: tales of lovecraftian terror in 2019 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Return of the Old Ones: Apocalyptic Lovecraftian Horror</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2017</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Edgar_J._Davis">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LovecraftSFriendsAndAcquaintances"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Edgar J. Davis</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>1949</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Young amateur journalist with whom Lovecraft explored Newburyport and other locales in New England.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasRealPersonMateR rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>1908</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Eeny_Meeny_Miney_Mi-Go">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Eeny Meeny Miney Mi-Go</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The keeper of the gate is a short hardboiled/ cthulhu mythos story by british author . It was first published in the chapbook collection of his own works the keeper of the gate in august 2019 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Midnight_Eye_Files"/>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Keeper_of_the_Gate"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>August 2019</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Bryce_Stevens">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonFictionAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Bryce Stevens</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Bryce John Stevens Pseudonym(s) David Kuraria B. J. Stevens Connection to the Mythos Author Editor Artist Birth Date 10 September 1957 Christchurch, New Zealand New Zealand (born 10 September 1957) is an author, editor and occasional artist from Christchurch, New Zealand. He has had a hand in a number of Lovecraftian works, including the Cthulhu Deep Down Under series, The Australian H. P. Lovecraft Centenary Calendar 1990-91 , and the Shoggoth fanzine. Many of his more recent Lovecraftian works have been issued through small press publisher IFWG Publishing . Selected Works Editor Cthulhu Deep Down Under: Volume 1 (2015, with Steve Proposch and Christopher Sequiera ) Cthulhu Deep Down Under: Volume 2 (2018, with Steve Proposch and Christopher Sequiera) Cthulhu: Land of the Long White Cloud (2018, with Steve Proposch and Christopher Sequiera) Cthulhu Deep Down Under: Volume 3 (2021, with Steve Proposch and Christopher Sequiera) Non-Fiction " Blasphemous Tomes: A Guide to Lovecraftiana in the Small Press " (1992, with Leigh Blackmore and Chris A. Masters) Cover Art Shoggoth #2 (1993) See Also Images by External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>Christchurch New Zealand</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Bryce John Stevens</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>New Zealand</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>B. J. Stevens</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:hasPseudonymR>David Kuraria</ex:hasPseudonymR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Editor</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>10 September 1957</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Inhabitant_of_the_Nameless_City">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#EarthNativeSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Inhabitant of the Nameless City</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Reptile Person</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The inhabitants of the nameless city are a fictional species created by h. p. lovecraft for his short story " the nameless city " . They are referred to as the reptile people , a race of quadrupedal reptiles with scaly skin and horns .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Keeper_of_the_Key"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Keepers_Companion"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Nameless_City"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Calling:_Cthulhu_Chronicles">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Calling: Cthulhu Chronicles</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Cthulhu mythos is a limited-run comic book series written by michael alan nelson and johanna stokes with artwork provided by christopher possenti . It was first published by boom! Studios between july and october 2010 . An omnibus edition was released in march 2011 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Alan_Nelson"/>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Johanna Stokes</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2010</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nameless_Horrors">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nameless Horrors</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>First released in 2015, a largely-unchanged second edition was published in 2023, credited to the same writers . Despite being an update, it claims a lower page count than the previous edition at only 202 . Despite being an update, it claims a lower page count than the previous edition at only 202 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
