  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Armand_Rosamilia">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Armand Rosamilia</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author New Jersey, USA United States Weird fiction http://armandrosamilia.com/ is an American author and podcaster who has written a number of works set in the greater Cthulhu Mythos created by H. P. Lovecraft and others. Born and raised in New Jersey, he currently lives in Florida. With regards to this wiki, Rosamilia is best known for his Keyport Cthulhu story cycle. Selected Bibliography Collections Keyport Cthulhu (2013, with contributions from Chuck Buda and Katelynn Rosamilia) Chapbooks Ancient: A Keyport Cthulhu Tale (2012) Barren (2012) Cabal (2012) Short Fiction " Ancient " (2012) " Barren " (2012) " Cabal " (2012) " Dagon " (2012) " Evil " (2012) " Rats in the Cellars " (2012) " Cthulhunicorn " (2013, with Katelynn Rosamilia) " Lockbox " (2017)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA http://example.org/lovecraft#New_Jersey</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://armandrosamilia.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dreams_in_the_Witch-House">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HPLovecraftWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Dreams in the Witch-House</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"the dreams in the witch house" is a short story by h. p. lovecraft . It was written in january/february 1932, and first published in the july 1933 issue of weird tales . The story is part of the cthulhu mythos cycle of horror fiction .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror short story</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Cthulhu Mythos</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Charles_R._Tanner">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Charles R. Tanner</rdfs:label>
    <ex:diedOnR>9 January 1974</ex:diedOnR>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full Name Charles Roland Tanner Connection to the Mythos Author Birth Date 17 February 1896 Cincinnati, Ohio, USA Death Date 9 January 1974 United States http://www.charlesrtanner.com/ (17 February 1896 - 9 January 1974), was an American science fiction writer who wrote the Cthulhu Mythos story " Out of the Jar ". He is perhaps best remembered for the Tumithak series, set several generations after the Earth has been conquered by spider-like aliens from Venus , and humanity has been divided into several races, some driven to underground corridors and others enslaved and modified by selective breeding. Selected Bibliography Short Fiction " Out of the Jar " (1941) External Links at Wikipedia at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Ohio Cincinnati</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasFullNameR>Charles Roland Tanner</ex:hasFullNameR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://www.charlesrtanner.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
