  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beyond_Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Beyond Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Frank Forte Cover Artist Frank Forte English Asylum Press Release Date September 2020 is a collection of Lovecraftian and Cthulhu Mythos stories by artist and Frank Forte , who also created the cover image. It was issued through his own publishing house, Asylum Press, in September 2020 with both paperback and digital editions receiving a release. Contents " Asphinxiation " " The House at the End of the Street " " The Connection " " The Sleeping One " " Shocking Terrors #13 " " Dead Thing " " Incident at the Hanford Inn " " The Insidious Doom " " The Strange Terror From Beyond " " The Cursed Appeal of Knowledge " " An Account of Ozgamuun " " That Which Lurks " " The Experiment "</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Forte"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 2020</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Black_Whore">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Black Whore</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep"/>
    <ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>Abigail Dexter</ex:hasAlternativeNamesC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Also known as Abigail Dexter Relatives Doctor Ambrose Dexter (father) Nuclear Physicist Nyarlathotep Human First appearance EXP : " October Surprise " Created by Kevin L. O'Brien is an Avatar of Nyarlathotep created by American author Kevin L. O'Brien . History After merging with Doctor Ambrose Dexter and turning him into a new Avatar for himself, Nyarlathotep impregnated Bierce's wife with his own seed; the resultant child, Abigail Dexter, would therefore be Nyarlathotep's Avatar from birth. As an adult, Abigail earned her doctorate in nuclear physics and took a post with the United States government. She then masterminded a plot to detonate a nuclear weapon underwater to destroy a Deep One city; this fulfilled the schemes' primary goal of cracking an Elder Sign which held the Great Old One Cthaeghya in imprisonment Abigail Dexter's current whereabouts are unknown. Behind the Mythos was created by Kevin L. O'Brien for his 2006 short story " October Surprise ".</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#October_Surprise"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kevin_L._OBrien"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Pelgrane_Press">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Publishers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Pelgrane Press</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Pelgrane is a roleplaying games manufacturer based in the united kingdom . Their publications include a number of cthulhu mythos titles, as well as works of fiction under their stone skin press imprint . Pelgrane also produce a small number of supplements for arc dream publishing's delta green roleplaying game, set in the era of the vietnam war .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://site.pelgranepress.com/</ex:hasWebsiteR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Compleat_Crow">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#BrianLumleyWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#CrossroadPress"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Compleat Crow</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Titus crow is an anthology of short stories by horror writer brian lumley . It forms part of his titus crow of mythos -set fiction . The stories were written by lumley over the course of seventeen years .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Brian_Lumley"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United Kingdom</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Titus_Crow"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Grioth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#SapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Grioth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The are a malevolent race that worships nyarlathotep and whom are enemies of the dominion of the black . Use portals to travel to other worlds, to pillage them for resources . The elder possess unusual psionic powers, which aids the against their mortal enemies, the dominion of the black .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>The Dragon's Demand</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Mike Shel</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
