  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Christchurch_Cemetery">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Christchurch Cemetery</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Arkham , Massachusetts Cemetery First appearance HPL : " Herbert West--Reanimator " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a cemetery in the fictional town of Arkham , Massachusetts . At one point Herbert West considered using the cemetery as a source of bodies for his reanimation experiments, but decided that the embalmed state of those buried there would not have been suitable for this purpose. Later, the reanimated corpse of Dr. Allan Halsey killed a night watchman at the cemetery when the corpse attempted to return to its tomb. ( HPL : " Herbert West--Reanimator ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Cemetery</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Massachusetts"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Herbert_West--Reanimator"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Grace_Holdinghaus">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Grace Holdinghaus</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Games designer is a games developer who designs for publisher Fantasy Flight Games . Her credits include tie-in works for the Lord of the Rings franchise and a number of expansions for the Cthulhu Mythos crawler Mansions of Madness . Selected Works Expansion Sets Streets of Arkham (2017) Sanctum of Twilight (2018) External Links designer profile at BoardGameGeek</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Games designer</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beyond_the_Rim_and_Other_Tales_of_Cosmic_Horror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Beyond the Rim and Other Tales of Cosmic Horror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>John Glasby Cover Artist Gavin L. O'Keefe English Dancing Tuatara Press Ramble House Release Date September 2015 278 is a collection of Lovecraftian fiction by the late British John Glasby . Featuring cover art by Gavin L. O'Keefe and running to 278 , it was posthumously published as a paperback by Dancing Tuatara Press and hardback by Ramble House in September 2015. Including an introduction by John Pelan , the collection consists primarily of reprinted stories, with only one, "Spectre over Torsands", being original to this volume. Overview Contents London Calling... Cthulhu, introduction by John Pelan "The Weird Shadow Over Innsmouth" "Return to Y'ha-nthlei" "Mythos" "The Dweller in Darkness" "Spectre over Torsands" "Devil Reef" " The Old One " "Beyond the Rim" Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#John_Glasby"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>278</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>September 2015</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Innsport">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Innsport</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A fictional city created by american author brandon berntson for his lovecraft mysteries trilogy of cthulhu mythos novels . It made its first appearance in the first book in the series, the night of dagon . The city is home to " regular dregs and seedy nightcrawlers and criminals " found in most major urban areas .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>City</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>United States East Coast</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Night_of_Dagon"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#She_Sleeps_in_the_Depths">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>She Sleeps in the Depths</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Two people who are tormented by a song which constantly plays in their heads discover each other whilst looking for an answer to their condition . Travel to the islands off the north-west coast of scotland, they feel that the source of the singing is coming from the waters around the base of the monolithic old man of hoy . When they disturb an ancient statuette sunken beneath the waves something ancient and terrible begins to awaken .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#William_Meikle"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>DarkFuse #1</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_Hambling">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Editors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>David Hambling</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Author of several cthulhu mythos series, including harry stubbs , william blake , and age of monsters . The first two of the series take place in post-world war i britain . The latter two are loosely linked together .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>London UK</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>British</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>July 11th</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Doom_in_the_Room">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Doom in the Room</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Jeffrey Thomas English Mythos Books Unholy Dimensions date October 2005 " " is a humorous Cthulhu Mythos short story by American Jeffrey Thomas . It was published in the collection Unholy Dimensions by Mythos Books in October 2005. Synopsis A Miskatonic University professor in search of a mysterious Egyptian crystal finds his way to a decrepit Arkham townhouse wherein he believes his goal to lie. What he discovers is a monstrous creature from beyond, juggling the shards of the crystal which it has just accidentally dropped and shattered. The story's conclusion implies that he does not survive the encounter.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jeffrey_Thomas"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Unholy_Dimensions"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>October 2005</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Amazing_Stories">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Periodicals"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Amazing Stories</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Hugo Gernsback English April 1926 , launched in 1926 by Hugo Gernsback , was the first magazine devoted to science fiction. Its September 1927 issue featured H. P. Lovecraft 's "The Colour Out of Space" ; after Lovecraft's death, his collaboration with Henry S. Whitehead , " Bothon ", appeared in the magazine's August 1946 issue. is considered to have had an enormous impact on the development of the science fiction genre; writers whose first stories appeared in the magazine include John W. Campbell, Isaac Asimov, Ursula K. Le Guin, Roger Zelazny, and Thomas M. Disch. External Links at The Internet Speculative Fiction Database References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Kyresh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#NonSapientSpecies"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Species"/>
    <rdfs:label>Kyresh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>'Ygirothians</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a fictional species created by walter c. debill, jr. for his short story "in 'ygiroth" described as a "morbid relic of an older time", were already extinct in most of the dreamlands when the thing in the yellow mask taught the 'ygirothians how to ride them .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>In 'Ygiroth</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Walter C. DeBill. Jr.</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hyades">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsIncorporatedFromTheRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#LocationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hyades</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Taurus constellation Star cluster ADJ : " An Inhabitant of Carcosa " ADJ : The King in Yellow The is a real-world star cluster located in the constellation of Taurus. As the nearest star cluster to our own solar system, it is one of the most thoroughly studied. In the Mythos In August Derleth 's short story " The Gable Window " (one of his controversial " posthumous collaborations " with Lovecraft ) one of the characters writings remark that the glass from which the titular window is made with glass from " Leng … possibly Hyadean in origins". This suggests that the fabled Plateau of Leng, whose has long been a topic of debate, may in fact be situated somewhere in the star cluster.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#An_Inhabitant_of_Carcosa"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_King_in_Yellow"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Star cluster</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Taurus constellation</ex:isLocatedAtL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Eldritch_Horror">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Eldritch Horror</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Arkham horror files is a cooperative board game produced by fantasy flight games as part of their arkham horror files range of cthulhu mythos -related products . The game is a streamlined version of its sister game arkham horror , many of its more cumbersome elements have been stripped down . The goal of the game is to prevent the awakening of an entity known as an ancient one .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2013</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Atlantis_%28poem%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ClarkAshtonSmithWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Atlantis (poem)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Atlantis Full story online here Clark Ashton Smith United States English Poseidonis Publication date November 1912 " Atlantis " is a Cthulhu Mythos poem by the late Clark Ashton Smith , and forms the first part of his Poseidonis story cycle. Synopsis As it’s title might suggest, "Atlantis" comprises a description of the lost continent from which the poem takes its name. Publication History First published in the Clark Ashton Smith collection The Star Treader and Other Poems in November 1912, "Atlantis" has been reprinted many times in several different publications.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Clark_Ashton_Smith"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW>Poseidonis</ex:isPartOfSeriesW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>November 1912</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#I_Do_the_Work_of_the_Bone_Queen">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>I Do the Work of the Bone Queen</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>John R. Fultz United States English Genre(s) Weird fiction 01Publishing Whispers from the Abyss date 2013  " " is a short Lovecraftian story by American John R. Fultz . Synopsis A crippled man commits suicide to escape the prison of his ruined body. His ghost is subsequently given a fresh corporeal form by an entity known as the Bone Queen, and sent back to run the factory where he had his accident in life. However, the factory has been repurposed, and now functions as an assembly line for bizarre flesh golems which are sacrificed to some unknown abomination. History "" was published in the Kat Rocha -edited Lovecraftian anthology Whispers from the Abyss by 01Publishing in 2013.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#John_R._Fultz"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Whispers_from_the_Abyss"/>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>2013</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sanbourne_Institute_of_Pacific_Antiquities">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sanbourne Institute of Pacific Antiquities</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Sanbourne is a fictional research facility created by lin carter for his xothic legend cycle . Mirroring miskatonic university, the two have a particular specialisation in the occult . However, the two seem to lean more towards the research aspect of graduate study rather than higher learning .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_in_the_Gallery"/>
    <ex:hasPurposeL>Anthropological Studies</ex:hasPurposeL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Centre for Higher Learning</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Research Facility</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#California"/>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>Santiago</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL>USA</ex:isLocatedAtL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dweller_in_the_Tomb"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#My_Stalk">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>My Stalk</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Is a short story by and editor aaron french . It is inspired by the fiction of lovecraft .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Aaron_J._French"/>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Weird fiction</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPublishedAsW>Aberrations of Reality</ex:isPublishedAsW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>September 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chester_Chase">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Chester Chase</rdfs:label>
    <ex:ceasedOnC>Early 1980s</ex:ceasedOnC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Chester was a cocky, well-built construction worker who married a woman named emily . By the time of his appearances, he is an ageing widower of 75 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasCharacterMateC>Emily</ex:hasCharacterMateC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Michael_Shea"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shugoran">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Avatars"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shugoran</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nyarlathotep"/>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Nyarlathotep created by henry kuttner is an avatar of the outer god nyarlathotep created by h. p. lovecraft contemporary henry kuttner . It has since been expanded on by several other authors, including t. e. d. klein . Chaosium was incorporated into chaosium 's lovecraftian roleplaying game call of cthulhu, first appearing in 1992's escape from innsmouth by kevin ross .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Henry_Kuttner"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ubbo-Sathla_%28short_story%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ClarkAshtonSmithWorks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#HyperboreanCycle"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ubbo-Sathla (short story)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>"ubbo-sathla " is a short story by the late american and lovecraft contemporary clark ashton smith . It forms a part of his hyperborean cycle . First printed in the july 1933 edition of pulp periodical weird tales .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Clark_Ashton_Smith"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Fantasy</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:hasGenreW>Horror</ex:hasGenreW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
