    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ElderGods"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Derleth (Doctor Who)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Derleth is an Elder God fought by The Seventh Doctor in Doctor Who audio stories.</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Book_of_Eibon_%282002_anthology%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Chaosium"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Book of Eibon (2002 anthology)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The book of eibon is divided into five parts, or "books" book one collects stories of ancient wizards. The stories in book two are about eibon himself. Book three is concerned with the history of the world, according to the mythos .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>432</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2006</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nightscapes_December_1997">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ebooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nightscapes December 1997</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Various English Edward P. Berglund Release Date December 1997 Preceded by October 1997 Followed by January 1998 is the fifth issue of the long-running online fanzine Nightscapes . It was edited by the late American and Lovecraft scholar Edward P. Berglund . Contents Fiction "Seafoam" by Alan Peschke "The Sudden and Dramatic Disappearance of Henry Resnick" by Jon Hansen "Shoofly" by Tim Waggoner " The House in the Woods " by R.S. Cartwright "Darker" by Alan Peschke " When the Stars Are Ripe " by Stanley C. Sargent "The Prodigal" by Andy Nunez "End Times" by Ricardo Madeira Non-Fiction "An Interview with Brian Lumley" by Robert M. Price "The Dream Quest of Brian Lumley" by Robert M. Price " Cthulhu in the Comics Part One: The Superhero Books " by James Ambuehl , Boyd E. Pearson and Dan Ross Parodies " The Cthulhu Cult " by Dan Clore " Mob Hit " by Boyd E. Pearson Poetry " Folks of Innsmouth: Fire Chief " by Franklyn Searight "The Gates" by Dominic Servello " The Book in the House " by Ron Shiflet " Spawn of Tindalos " by James Gruetzmacher and Ron Shiflet " Weak " by Peter A. Worthy Reviews By Paul T. Riddell External Links full issue online at the Nightscapes website</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Various</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>December 1997</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shoggoth_Rising">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shoggoth Rising</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>dreipol Publication Date December 2014 Mobile App is a single-player shoot 'em up mobile app which draws its inspiration from the Cthulhu Mythos based on the works of H. P. Lovecraft . Overview The player takes on the role of Ned, a sailor shipwrecked on a deserted island who is forced to defend himself from waves of enemies whose difficulty increases as the levels progress. A variety of weapons and upgrades are also available the further one advances. Release was released for iOS, Android and Windows by dreipol in December 2014. Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>December 2014</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Planets">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Nargis-Hei">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DeceasedInMythos"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Nargis-Hei</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Mnar was the king of sarnath at the time of the city's destruction from the vengeance of bokrug . Created by h. p. lovecraft was the king of the city at the time of the city's destruction from the vengeance of bokrug .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Doom_That_Came_to_Sarnath"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dr._Fenton">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Dr. Fenton</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>New York State Psychiatrist Human First appearance HPL : " Beyond the Wall of Sleep " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a psychiatrist at the mental hospital in New York State where Joe Slater was confined. He is the supervisor of the unnamed intern in the story " Beyond the Wall of Sleep " by H. P. Lovecraft . When the intern (who also narrated the story) spoke of his supernatural experiences with Slater to , the doctor was skeptical, assuring him that Slater was nothing more than "a low-grade paranoiac whose fantastic notions must have come from the crude hereditary folktales which circulate in even the most decadent of communities."</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Beyond_the_Wall_of_Sleep"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Narath">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalLocations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Structures"/>
    <rdfs:label>Narath</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Dreamlands City Humans First appearance HPL : " The Silver Key " Created by H. P. Lovecraft is a fictional city created by the late American author H. P. Lovecraft for his short story " The Silver Key ". Description Located somewhere in the Dreamlands , is described as a city of peerless beauty with a hundred carven gates and domes of chalcedony. ( HPL : " The Silver Key ")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasTypeL>City</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:isInhabitedByL>Humans</ex:isInhabitedByL>
    <ex:isLocatedAtL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dreamlands"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Silver_Key"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Stranger">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Stranger</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Full story online here Ron Shiflet United States English Publication date May 2000 " " is a short Cthulhu Mythos poem by American Ron Shiflet . Synopsis A man walking along a forest path encounters a gibbering stranger with a head full of tentacles. Publication History "" was published in the May 2000 edition of the online fanzine Nightscapes .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ron_Shiflet"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>United States</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>May 2000</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Yuzh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stars"/>
    <rdfs:label>Yuzh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Stellar body First appearance CIRCLE : " The Infernal Star " EXP : " Priestess of Nycrama " Created by Clark Ashton Smith is a fictional star first mentioned by the late American author Clark Ashton Smith in his unfinished 1933 story " The Infernal Star ". Overview In his story fragment, Smith reveals almost nothing of , save than that it is a binary star in partnership with its sister Yamil Zacra , and that the two are orbited by the planet Pnidleethon ( CIRCLE : " The Infernal Star "). John W. Patterson later states to have become the prison for the soul of the monstrous being Nycrama after its death at the hands of Endura/Avrenim, although how or why this is the case is left unexplained ( EXP : " Priestess of Nycrama "). Behind the Mythos In his afterword to the digital edition of "Priestess of Nycrama", Patterson states is one of the " fantastic names and places … me to write ".</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceL rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Priestess_of_Nycrama"/>
    <ex:hasTypeL>Stellar body</ex:hasTypeL>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>The Infernal Star</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnL>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Arkham_House">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#DefunctRealWorld"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Publishers"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Arkham House</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The company's name is derived from arkham , lovecraft's fictional new england city . Under august derleth august derleth was the guiding force behind, financing the company . Also published horror and fantasy fiction by many of lovecraft's contemporaries .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Ghaszaszh_Nyirh">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Ghaszaszh Nyirh</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAffiliationC>Old Ones</ex:hasAffiliationC>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Terry shoemaker is a fictional character in the marvel universe which first appeared in 1987 in issue #9 of the 2nd volume of the strange tales comic book series . It is unknown so far whether is a great old one , or a lesser old one , one of the great old ones' servants and spawn .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>Strange Tales Vol 2 #8</ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Peter B. Gillis</ex:wasCreatedByC>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC>Terry Shoemaker</ex:wasCreatedByC>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Paul_Carrick">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Paul Carrick</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Artist United States Lovecraftian horror Fantasy https://paulcarrick.com/Home.html http://nightserpent.com/index.html is an American artist and sculptor based in Boston , Massachusetts , who also operates under the name of nightserpent. He specialises in fantasy and gaming-related art, and has a particular affinity for Lovecraftian imagery . Carrick has drawn extensively for Chaosium 's horror roleplaying game, and has provided cover art for a number of Lovecraftian publications, including Fantasy Flight Games ' The Art of H. P. Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos and Edward P. Berglund 's online zine Nightscapes . Selected Works Cover Art Secrets (1997) Urban Cthulhu: Nightmare Cities (2012) Interior Art Secrets (1997) The Keeper's Companion (2000-2002) Unseen Masters (2001) H. P. Lovecraft's Dunwich (2002) Nightscapes May 2003 (2003) The Art of H. P. Lovecraft's Cthulhu Mythos (2006) Secrets of Kenya (2008) Atomic-Age Cthulhu (2013) See Also Images by External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads (as nightserpent) at DeviantArt References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://nightserpent.com/index.html</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>https://paulcarrick.com/Home.html</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
