    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>A group or institution, real or fictional, playing a role in the mythos or related works.</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Sinkhole">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamingSupplements"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Sinkhole</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>A promising graduate student named hayes encountered one of these cults and found their activities appealing . He decided to go back to his beginnings by reviving a tulushuggua cult . The adventure begins when he needs help to lure people into his planned cult .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Color_of_Madness_%28Darkest_Dungeon%29">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Color of Madness (Darkest Dungeon)</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Color of Madness Red Hook Studios Publication Date 19 June 2018  " The Color of Madness " is a DLC expansion pack for the roguelike horror roleplaying game Darkest Dungeon . It was first released by Red Hook Studios on 19 June 2018. Overview "The Color of Madness" opens a new setting for the game in which a small farmstead has been struck by a comet which has laid a blight upon the land and transformed many of its inhabitants into twisted, malevolent creatures. Behind the Mythos Although the comet and its effects on the locals bear no direct relation to Lovecraft 's works, the description of its incomprehensible colouration and repeated story references to "the blasted heath" show a clear inspiration from " The Colour Out of Space " . External Links " The Color of Madness " at the Darkest Dungeon wiki References</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>19 June 2018</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Call_of_Cthulhu:_The_Wasted_Land">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#GamesAndAdaptations"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Call of Cthulhu: The Wasted Land</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Red Wasp Design Publication Date January 2012 Tactical roleplaying is a single-player tactical roleplaying Cthulhu Mythos video game. Premise In 1915, a scholar and a British army officer battle a German Army cult who are using the stolen work of Dr. Herbert West to create a legion of undead soldiers to fight the war in France. However, the cult's ultimate goal is later revealed to be the summoning of a Star-spawn of Cthulhu , which will eliminate mankind in its entirety and pave the way for a new species of Star-spawn/human hybrids. Release The Wasted Land was released for iOS and Windows in January and May 2012 respectively, and for Android in July of the following year.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:wasPublishedOnW>January 2012</ex:wasPublishedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#BhyhlunSeries">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Dimensions">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hellstar_Remina">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraterrestrialCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hellstar Remina</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Is a neptune-sized living planet that consumes planetary bodies . It bears a strong resemblance to ghroth, an outer god from the expanded cthulhu mythos . It is likely sentient and at least aware, being able to sense when it was being observed light years away .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#J._J._Savage">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>J. J. Savage</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author is a children's author who has to date written two books inspired by the works of Howard Phillips Lovecraft . These books, their Young Cthulhu series, have been published through online marketplace Amazon, and feature illustrations by Jennifer Singer . Selected Works Children's Books A Call for Cthulhu A Home for Cthulhu (2022) External Links at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Tiefenrausch">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Tiefenrausch</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>H. p. lovecraft's bibliothek des schreckens is a collection of lovecraftian stories by cody goodfellow . It was published in a hardcover format by festa as part of their h. p. lovecraft's bibliothek des schreckens in october 2022 . The collection includes stories such as "cahokia" (trans. Of " cahokia") and "pendeln" (trans. Of " swinging)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Cody_Goodfellow"/>
    <ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>Germany</ex:hasCountryOfOriginW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>570</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>German</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:isPartOfSeriesW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecrafts_Bibliothek_des_Schreckens"/>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>October 2022</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Welcome_to_Neverbury">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Welcome to Neverbury</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Neverbury is a collection of horror fiction by uk-based author, christopher lynch . It was self-published on amazon’s digital kindle platform in june 2023; an audiobook edition has since been released through audible . The individual tales run a range of horror genres, from black comedy ("yes, no refunds") to gothic ghost stories ("a design for living")</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Chris Lynch</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>180</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>June 2023</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Taint_of_Lovecraft">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>The Taint of Lovecraft</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>English mythos books release date 2002 (2002) is an anthology compiling stories, poems and essays by stanley c. sargent . It also contains artwork by allen koszowski , jeffrey thomas , daniel alan ross (who provided the cover), peter a. worthy and dale l. hutchinson .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stanley_C._Sargent"/>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>2002</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Allen_Koszowski">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artists"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Allen Koszowski</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Koszowski was a cover artist for crypt of cthulhu during its lengthy run . He has also illustrated newsletters, zines and publications from eodapa . He is a past winner of the l. ron hubbard illustrators of the future award .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>USA Pennsylvania Philadelphia</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United States</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:hasWebsiteR>http://www.allenk.com/main.html</ex:hasWebsiteR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Artist</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>27 June 1949</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hunger">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hunger</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>is an extra-dimensional eldritch entity from the fictional universe of Marvel by Marvel Comics . Background is a universal-scale parasite which lives in the Cosmic Vortex. It feeds on matter, energy, and the fabric of reality, and has devoured a number of realities. The entity has a sense of humor and breaks the "Fourth Wall".</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Xena/Army_of_Darkness:_What...Again%3F">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ComicBooks"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Xena/Army of Darkness: What...Again?</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Xena/Army of Darkness: What...Again? Elliott R. Serrano, Brandon Jerwa Miguel Montenegro English Dynamite Entertainment Release Date Oct 2008 - Jan 2009 Media Type Comic book Xena / Army of Darkness: What...Again?! is a four-issue comic book mini series written by Elliott R. Serrano and Brandon Jerwa in 2008-2009 which was published by Dynamite Entertainment. Synopsis Ash Williams once again faces the forces of the Necronomicon , this time with a time-displaced Xena and Gabrielle right alongside with him at the dawn of the 21st century.</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Brandon Jerwa</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:hasAuthorW>Elliott R. Serrano</ex:hasAuthorW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>Oct 2008 - Jan 2009</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#CallOfCthulhuRealWorld">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Location"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#OrganisationsOriginatingFromMythosAdjacentWorks">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Organisation"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#MysticalArtefacts">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Hytherion">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Hytherion</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Background is a multiversal lovecraftian-like entity in the fictional universe of transformers by takaratomy . It's made of alterium, a dimensionally-resonant material, and sustains itself on time . To lower-dimensional beings the entity is both invisible</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Taffy">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Taffy</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>also known as The Pale Brown Thing , is a paramental creature brought into being through the focused blacked magic of Megapolisomancy . It takes its physical form from a vaguely woman-shaped piled of old pulp magazines strewn across the protagonist's bed. At the climax of the story the magazines shred themselves into paper dust and form a dry pale brown face figure with a long tangle of dark "hair" and a snout for sucking bone marrow from its victims after it has choked them to death and shattered their bones.</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Midnight_Shambler">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Fanzines"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Midnight Shambler</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>First two issues, released in 1988, were edited by david barker . Ceased publication until 1996, when it was revived under robert m. price's editorship for another eight issues, through 1998 . Joseph s. pulver, sr. took the helm for the eleventh and final issue in april 1999 .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Stephen_Hernandez">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExpandedMythosAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
    <rdfs:label>Stephen Hernandez</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Connection to the Mythos Author Birth Date 4 May 1960 London, England, U.K. United Kingdom (born 4 May 1960) is a British author with a handful of fiction credits to his name, amongst them at least two Cthulhu Mythos stories. These have been published in the Rogue Planet Press anthologies Swords Against Cthulhu (2015) and Swords Against Cthulhu II: Hyperborean Nights (2017). Selected Bibliography "The Thing in the Swamp" (2015) " A Sister's Love " (2017) External Links at the Internet Speculative Fiction Database at Goodreads</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasBirthplaceR>http://example.org/lovecraft#England London U.K.</ex:hasBirthplaceR>
    <ex:hasNationalityR>United Kingdom</ex:hasNationalityR>
    <ex:isConnectedToMythosR>Author</ex:isConnectedToMythosR>
    <ex:wasBornOnR>4 May 1960</ex:wasBornOnR>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Scholars">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#RealWorldPerson"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Seven_Cryptical_Books_of_Hsan">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosBooksFictional"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdfs:label>Seven Cryptical Books of Hsan</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The Hsan (presumed) Real World Information First appearance HPL : " The Other Gods " HPL : The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath EXP : " The Return of Zhosph " Created by H. P. Lovecraft The are a collection of occult grimoires created by H. P. Lovecraft for his short story " The Other Gods ". Overview Little is known of the contents of the Seven Cryptical Books , even where they come from: both the Dreamlands and the waking lands of Earth 's prehistory have been suggested as their place of origin. Presumably written by a person or entity named Hsan, their contents also remain a mystery. Despite the uncertainty of their history, copies of the Seven Cryptical Books are known to exist in the Dreamlands of the modern age. Lovecraft's Work " The Other Gods " (1933) The Dream-Quest of Unknown Kadath (1943) Expanded Mythos Works " The Return of Zhosph " (1972)</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAppearanceA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Dream-Quest_of_Unknown_Kadath"/>
    <ex:hasAppearanceA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Return_of_Zhosph"/>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Other_Gods"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByA rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#H._P._Lovecraft"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Jade_God">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherSupernaturalBeings"/>
    <rdfs:label>Jade God</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>The is a green jade statue of a winged ape . The statue was between two and three feet tall . It appears in the short story the by robert e. howard .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Roger_Little">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Humans"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Roger Little</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Little is an occult detective and inventor known for having investigated various cases of supernatural phenomena . He has an interest in criminal psychology and a reputation as something of an eccentric . He has a psychic sensitivity and had a dream prophesying the return of chaugnar faugn and its brothers .</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:madeFirstAppearanceOnC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#The_Horror_from_the_Hills"/>
    <ex:wasCreatedByC rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Frank_Belknap_Long"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#hasAlternativeNamesA">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label>hasAlternativeNamesA</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Alioth">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Character"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#ExtraDimensionalCharacters"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosCharacters"/>
    <rdfs:label>Alioth</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>Alitoh is a trans-temporal entity, which appears as a vast cloud . It exists across divergent timelines, and destroys all it touches . He is the first being that ever broke free from the constraints of time .</ex:hasAnnotation>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#Shadows_from_Norwood">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#MythosLiterature"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#OtherAuthors"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Work"/>
    <rdfs:label>Shadows from Norwood</rdfs:label>
    <ex:hasAnnotation>David Hambling English CreateSpace Release Date July 2013 Media Type Collection 460 is a collection of Lovecraftian short stories by British David Hambling . Overview Containing seven stories and running to a total of 460 , was independently published through CreateSpace in July 2013. Contents Introduction by David Hambling " The Dulwich Horror of 1927 " "Two Fingers" " The Thing in the Vault " " The Monsters in the Park " "The Devils in the Deep Blue Sea" "The Norwood Builder" "Shadows of the Witch House" Gallery</ex:hasAnnotation>
    <ex:hasAuthorW rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#David_Hambling"/>
    <ex:hasPageCountW>460</ex:hasPageCountW>
    <ex:isInLanguageW>English</ex:isInLanguageW>
    <ex:wasReleasedOnW>July 2013</ex:wasReleasedOnW>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://example.org/lovecraft#ArtefactsOriginatingFromMythosInspiredWorks">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://example.org/lovecraft#Artefact"/>
